lanco"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T05:31:14Z","email":"pointerbyte21@outlook.com","name":"Manuel Garcia Blanco"},"message":"feat(logger): implement synchronous file sink with rotation and compression options\n\n- Added a new file sink for logging that supports optional rotation and compression.\n- Introduced configuration options for maximum file size, backup retention, and age.\n- Implemented functionality to append logs to a file, rotate files when size limits are exceeded, and compress old backups.\n- Created comprehensive tests to validate the file sink behavior, including rotation and backup management.\n\nfeat(tests): add unit tests for file sink functionality\n\n- Developed unit tests to ensure the file sink appends records correctly, handles rotation, and manages backups based on specified configurations.\n- Included tests for compression of backups and validation of directory and file permissions.\n\nbuild(tools): add scripts for coverage checking and dependency isolation\n\n- Introduced a script to collect coverage profiles and enforce coverage thresholds.\n- Added a script to verify optional gRPC package boundaries against Deno''s resolved graph.\n- Implemented a documentation linting script to check public package entry points against Deno''s documentation standards.","tree":{"sha":"1965ca56f49f33b83fd84227e855dde9cc8c7ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PointerByte/DenoForge/git/trees/1965ca56f49f33b83fd84227e855dde9cc8c7ecc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PointerByte/DenoForge/git/commits/fbafc4381692072a13ea060f1bfb844279825d19","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60157724?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PointerByte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PointerByte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PointerByte/following