uthoredDate":"2026-08-15T20:51:07Z","committedDate":"2026-08-15T20:51:07Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"taills","providerType":"User"},"email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:34:08.720Z","repositoryId":1284700219,"sha":"64df9e043986ef23c83c80a6b28535e51fdc41d6"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:34:08.720Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8ff7c138919d44a248e30dde95f879b2f7cddfcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:10:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:10:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"Merge branch ''feat/example-plugin-frontends''\n\nThe console''s 扩展模块 section had nothing in it. Each of the six examples\nthat declares a menu now ships the page that menu points at.\n\n- Six vite + vite-plugin-qiankun projects, built by build-examples.sh into\n  the package directories Core serves from. The plugin is not optional:\n  vite emits ES modules and qiankun 2.x evals its entry scripts, which\n  cannot run one.\n- Opening a plugin URL your role cannot see rendered a blank page. sync()\n  took its early return before setting the message, because \"nothing to\n  mount\" and the initial mountedKey were the same empty string. Only\n  reachable once some plugin had a page to withhold.\n- The dev proxy still forwarded /extensions, dead since 4a25553 and\n  harmless for exactly as long as no plugin had a frontend.","tree":{"sha":"888384b06ac7208ae371606dc5918394a575440f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/888384b06ac7208ae371606dc5918394a575440f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/8ff7c138919d44a248e30dde95f879b2f7cddfcf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8ff7c138919d44a248e30dde95f879b2f7cddfcf","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDhmZjdjMTM4OTE5ZDQ0YTI0OGUzMGRkZTk1Zjg3OWIyZjdjZGRmY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","sha":"e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883","sha":"8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883"}],"sha":"8ff7c138919d44a248e30dde95f879b2f7cddfcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8ff7c138919d44a248e30dde95f879b2f7cddfcf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix(frontend): the dev proxy points at /plugins, where sub-apps actually live\n\nThe proxy still forwarded /extensions, the reverse-tunnel era''s asset path that\n4a25553 removed along with the tunnel itself. Plugin micro-frontends are served\nfrom /plugins (gateway.PluginAssetPrefix).\n\nDead config is usually harmless, and this was — for as long as no plugin had a\npage. `npm run dev` would have failed to load every sub-app, which nobody could\nobserve because there were none. The examples have pages now.","tree":{"sha":"888384b06ac7208ae371606dc5918394a575440f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/888384b06ac7208ae371606dc5918394a575440f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDhiN2Y3NmRiYWMyODJlODk0MzdmMDA2OWJmM2FmNzlhM2FjNWY4ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8","sha":"525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8"}],"sha":"8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b7f76dbac282e89437f0069bf3af79a3ac5f883"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:21Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:21Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a plugin page your role cannot see says so instead of rendering nothing\n\nsync() skips work when the target has not changed, comparing a key built from\nthe resolved entry. A route with nothing to mount has the empty key, and\nmountedKey also started as \"\" — so the very first run on such a route took the\nearly return and never reached the line that sets the message. The page was\nblank, with nothing on screen or in the console to say why.\n\nmountedKey starts as null now, which is a state a key cannot collide with, and\nis assigned on the empty path too so the second run still skips.\n\nThe bug needed a route the menu does not cover, which until now could not\nhappen: every entry Core sent reached every user, and no example had a page to\nwithhold. Three of them are admin-only as of this commit, and Core filters\nthose out of the tree by role — so a non-admin opening /apps/redact directly\nlands exactly here. Found that way, in the browser, not by reading.\n\nThe wording covers both ways to arrive rather than the one that was easier to\nphrase: the console genuinely cannot tell a disabled plugin from one filtered\nout by role, because both reach it as an absent entry.","tree":{"sha":"8e695319b18b70f41509067c5ca66e2a97a7d1ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/8e695319b18b70f41509067c5ca66e2a97a7d1ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDUyNTgzMmYxODc3YzU2N2E5NTU0NDA1ZGI3MWZhYjJkM2FlZTg1Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51","sha":"1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51"}],"sha":"525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/525832f1877c567a9554405db71fab2d3aee85f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat(examples): the six example plugins ship the pages their menus point at\n\nThe console''s 扩展模块 section was empty. Before that it was worse: six of the\neight examples declared menus with no frontend anywhere, so Core handed out\nentries resolving to /plugins/<key>/, the asset handler answered 404, and\nqiankun mounted that response body as the page. fc685ca stopped serving the\nbroken entries, which emptied the sidebar rather than filling it.\n\nThis fills it. Each of apikey, audit, digest, inventory, notes and redact gets\na vite + vite-plugin-qiankun project under frontend/, built by\nbuild-examples.sh into the package directory Core reads.\n\nThe plugin is not optional decoration. vite emits <script type=\"module\">, and\nqiankun 2.x runs entry scripts through eval inside its sandbox, which cannot\nexecute an ES module. vite-plugin-qiankun rewrites that into a dynamic import\nplus a classic script that assigns the lifecycles — and the assignment being\nthe last global write is what makes them findable at all, since the host mounts\nunder `app:/notes` (derived from the menu path) and no plugin should have to\nknow that name. Verified end to end before the other five were written.\n\nPages do what their plugin''s API allows rather than settling for a read-only\nlist: notes creates and deletes, inventory upserts and reserves and restocks,\napikey mints and revokes. Three things they all handle, because the codebase\ndoes them: errors arrive as {\"error\":...} from some routes and bare text from\nothers, admin-only routes answer 403 in words worth rewording, and paging is by\ncursor. apikey shows a minted key once and drops it from the DOM on dismiss,\nwhich is all that can be done with a value Core only stores the hash of.\n\nEach frontend duplicates api() and escapeHtml() instead of importing them from\none place. An example is copied whole, and ../../shared/api.js would break the\nmoment someone lifts a directory out as a template.\n\naudit''s menu gains roles: [admin]. Not a security fix — the handler has checked\nHasRole since it was written, and apikey/README.md spells out why the menu\nfield is not authorization. It is so a non-admin stops seeing a menu item that\nleads to the word \"forbidden\".\n\nbuild-examples.sh skips the frontend work when npm is absent or SKIP_FRONTEND\nis set: it is how Go developers build plugin binaries, and six npm builds turn\na second into a minute for nothing when only Go changed.\n\nThe new architecture test fails if an example ever declares a menu again\nwithout shipping a page, which is the state all six were in.","tree":{"sha":"7145202fa1a84a9c02363f6cd587c7f91b7ff306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7145202fa1a84a9c02363f6cd587c7f91b7ff306"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDEzOTBmYzBmZmMwZGFlOWQ5NDBiNmRjYzA1MGZlYjgyMWI1MmJjNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","sha":"e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f"}],"sha":"1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1390fc0ffc0dae9d940b6dcc050feb821b52bc51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:48:43Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:48:43Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"Merge branch ''fix/plugin-uptime-and-native-build''\n\nTwo things the console showed that were not true, and the build target\nthat put the machine in the way of finding them.\n\n- Plugins built for linux/amd64 could not exec on the development\n  machine, so every plugin reported exec format error. The example\n  build script takes a target now and still defaults to Linux.\n- A plugin that never started reported 739847 days of uptime: omitempty\n  does not apply to a time.Time, so the zero value shipped as\n  0001-01-01 and the console subtracted it from now.\n- A backend-only plugin was given a menu entry that resolved to 404,\n  which qiankun mounted as the page. Six of the eight examples did it.\n- The topbar read `[ \"apikey\" ]`, a repeatable route param interpolated\n  as an array.","tree":{"sha":"04a5259e0dea1d04821b0e296bfc238ce4c1442e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/04a5259e0dea1d04821b0e296bfc238ce4c1442e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGU4ZWM0ZmE3MzlmMjZlYTE0NzM0MWQ4NTA0NjYwNDg1MTc1ZTkzMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","sha":"0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c","sha":"cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c"}],"sha":"e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e8ec4fa739f26ea147341d8504660485175e931f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:33:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:33:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: the topbar names the page from the menu, not from a repeatable route param\n\nIt read route.params.pathMatch straight into the template. That param\ncomes from `apps/:pathMatch(.*)*`, and the trailing `*` makes it\nrepeatable — so it is an array, and Vue interpolated it as the topbar\ntext `[ \"apikey\" ]` where the page name belongs.\n\nresolveTitle looks the path up in the menu instead, so the topbar reads\n\"API 密钥\". It matches group nodes as well as leaves: a group has no\nentry but does have a title. Falling back to the path segment keeps the\nvalue a string for a plugin that was just disabled, which is the case\nthat produced the array.\n\nOnly /apps routes resolve. The console''s own pages render their own\nheading, and naming them here put \"/system/plugins\" directly above a\npage whose <h2> already read 插件管理.\n\nThe test mounts Layout and reads .crumb rather than calling resolveTitle\ndirectly: the defect was in what the template chose to read, and a unit\ntest on the helper would have passed against it. Reverting the template\nalone turns it red with the exact string from the report.","tree":{"sha":"04a5259e0dea1d04821b0e296bfc238ce4c1442e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/04a5259e0dea1d04821b0e296bfc238ce4c1442e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGNmZTQyYmEyNmY3ZjdiY2ViMmY0MmQxMzQwZjZkODMxMjJjNjYwOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd","sha":"fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd"}],"sha":"cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cfe42ba26f7f7bceb2f42d1340f6d83122c6609c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:33:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T03:33:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a plugin with no frontend gets no menu entry, so the page cannot 404\n\nThe guard for this existed but covered one branch of two:\n\n    if len(menus) == 0 && pkg.FrontendDir != \"\"\n\nFrontendDir was only consulted when the plugin declared no menus. A\nplugin that did declare them went through menuNodesFrom, which fills in\nthe asset entry for every leaf without asking whether there is anything\nto serve. The entry resolved to /plugins/<key>/, plugin_assets.go\nanswered 404, and qiankun mounted that response body — so the page read\n\"404 page not found\" beneath a sidebar that looked fine.\n\nAll eight shipped examples are backend-only and six of them declared\nmenus, so every extension in the console did this. Their manifests are\ncorrected too: the author''s guide already says a backend-only plugin\nshould not declare menus, and the examples are what people copy.\n\nCore still enforces it rather than trusting the manifest, for the same\nreason a plugin with no ready replica is omitted: the console is what\nan operator sees, and a packaging mistake should cost them an absent\nmenu entry, not a page reading 404.\n\nThe gateway fixtures had no FrontendDir, which is what made\nTestAppsHandlerListsEnabledPlugins pass against the broken version —\nthe fixture was a backend-only plugin standing in for one with a UI.\nSame for the end-to-end echo fixture, which now writes a frontend\ndirectory. TestBackendOnlyPluginGetsNoMenuEntry covers the other side\nthrough the real package scan, since FrontendDir comes from a directory\nexisting on disk.","tree":{"sha":"e0f5c54690594f9dfc47894f6f5ee54f2d9a2663","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e0f5c54690594f9dfc47894f6f5ee54f2d9a2663"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGZjNjg1Y2FiYzYyODdjYWRlYjVkNDZjZjBkMDBhNWFmYTAxMzI0ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63","sha":"c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63"}],"sha":"fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fc685cabc6287cadeb5d46cf0d00a5afa01324dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:06:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:06:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"build: the example build takes a target, so plugins can be built for the machine Core runs on\n\nGOOS and GOARCH were pinned to linux/amd64 for the musl runtime image\nthe compose file mounts them into. Running Core straight off a macOS\ndevelopment machine therefore loaded ELF binaries the kernel will not\nexec, and the console showed exec format error for all eight plugins\nwith nothing pointing at why.\n\nBoth are overridable now and still default to linux/amd64, so the\ncompose path is unchanged:\n\n  GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 ./scripts/build-examples.sh\n\nThe script echoes the target it built for, since the symptom shows up\nmuch later and somewhere else.","tree":{"sha":"550c9e4f30f9feb6c7c32fd0ba7bdf3afc5cb762","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/550c9e4f30f9feb6c7c32fd0ba7bdf3afc5cb762"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGM1MzFkYTE0OWYwYTcyZDQ4NDdhYWRmM2I0M2ExNDQ5ZmFlMTFiNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36","sha":"ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36"}],"sha":"c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c531da149f0a72d4847aadf3b43a1449fae11b63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:06:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:06:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a plugin that never started reports no uptime, not 739847 days\n\nStatus carried OldestStartedAt and QuarantinedAt as time.Time with\nomitempty, which does nothing for a struct: encoding/json only omits\nempty strings, zeroes, nils and empty slices/maps. So every plugin\nwithout a start time shipped \"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\", the console\nsubtracted it from now, and rendered 739847 days of uptime next to a\nplugin that had failed to load.\n\nThe manager already guarded the write with !at.IsZero(). That kept a\nzero out of the field but could not keep the field out of the JSON,\nwhich is where it went wrong — so both are pointers now and omitempty\napplies.\n\nQuarantinedAt had the same defect and no consumer yet; fixed together\nrather than left as the next one to surface.\n\nThe new test asserts on the encoded bytes, not the struct, because a\nstruct-level assertion passes on the broken version. Plugins.vue keeps\na floor at the epoch as well, since a plugin cannot have started before\n1970 and an older Core still sends the zero.","tree":{"sha":"69a0727981b05c2648bab8caa5880fd9784a2a99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/69a0727981b05c2648bab8caa5880fd9784a2a99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGFkNzYxNDI2YzRkY2ZkMzZhNmRhNTFiNGRiOTk3MDAzYmNiMTZlMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","sha":"0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da"}],"sha":"ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad761426c4dcfd36a6da51b4db997003bcb16e36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T15:04:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T15:04:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a refused request is audited with the status it was refused with\n\nFound while answering \"air won''t start\". air was fine — the plugin binaries in\nplugins/ are ELF x86-64 built for the Docker target and cannot exec on a darwin\narm64 machine, which is what \"exec format error\" means per the guide''s own\nrule. Rebuilding them for the host is all that was wrong.\n\nBut driving Core through air and looking at what the audit example recorded\nshowed something else:\n\n    POST /api/plugins/notes/notes -> 0    user=       (refused 401)\n    POST /api/plugins/notes/notes -> 201  user=admin\n\nA short circuit was written straight to the wire without being recorded on the\nrequest, so every refusal — a filter''s, and Core''s own unauthenticated 401 —\nreached the log phase carrying status 0. That is the same thing the field says\nwhen nothing knew, and refusals are most of what an audit trail is for. The 413\npath had been fixed before; the six writeResponse call sites and the 401 had\nnot.\n\nwriteResponse now records status, headers and body onto the request context\nrather than each of its callers doing it, for the reason the log phase became a\ndefer: a value written in one place and remembered in another drifts, silently.\n\ntests/audit_blindspot_test.go covers it — the existing tests there prove the log\nphase runs, which turns out to be a different claim from it being told what\nhappened. The echo fixture records the upstream status it was shown, behind a\n/statuses path so the benchmark load is unchanged.\n\nMy first version of that test used /deny, which the fixture matches exactly\nrather than by suffix, so the request was never refused and the test passed on a\n200. Its own precondition assertion caught that — and the comment immediately\nabove the fixture''s /refuse branch warns about precisely this trap.\n\nAlso in .air.toml: include_dir = [\"core\"] pulled in core/frontend/node_modules,\nso air watched 701 dependency directories out of 722 — 97% of the watching, for\nfiles no Go build reads. Excluded: 722 -> 19.\n\nFull suite green, twenty packages.","tree":{"sha":"ec7b0b2d5656d4761b44f7988655b55ac3067ad7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ec7b0b2d5656d4761b44f7988655b55ac3067ad7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDA2MTBlMzhiN2Y2NWZmODE5NTc4ZDIzMDI1MzE5NmYxMGMxZjUzZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855","sha":"38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855"}],"sha":"0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0610e38b7f65ff819578d230253196f10c1f53da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:25:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:25:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: run the suite on the platform it ships to, and assert the manifest error points somewhere\n\nForty-four commits into this session, including a breaking SDK change and\nseventeen new guards, every run had been on darwin. CLAUDE.md says plainly that\na green run on the development machine is not the same as a green run in\nproduction — ETXTBSY and Pdeathsig exist only on Linux — and I had been reading\npast it.\n\nLinux, with host services so the database- and storage-gated tests actually run\nrather than skipping: twenty packages green, tests in 172.989s against darwin''s\n~225s.\n\nGreen was not the finding, though. The whole point of running there is the\nchecks that exist only there, and a run that skipped them would look identical.\nSo it was checked rather than assumed:\n\n    === RUN   TestPdeathsigKillsOrphanedPlugins\n        2 process(es) reference the plugin (orphanhost plus its child)\n        the plugin died with its parent, as Pdeathsig asks\n\nThat is the only test of the guarantee that a plugin dies with Core, and it does\nnot compile on macOS.\n\nThe reverse also holds and is worth stating: TestBuildOutputNamesAreIgnored\nneeds git, which golang:alpine does not ship, so it runs only on darwin. Each\nplatform has one check the other cannot make, which means neither one alone is a\ncomplete pass. Both were run.\n\nSeparately, three areas were measured before being worked on and all three\nturned out already covered — the console''s unmount-on-disappear and SSE refetch,\nthe menu tree''s appear/disappear requirement end to end, and role filtering.\nThat last one was worth confirming rather than assuming: roleAllowed treats an\nempty role as seeing only unrestricted nodes, so Core running without a database\nhides admin menus instead of exposing them. The opposite would have been a hole.\n\nThe one gap found was a promise with nothing holding it. The guide says an\nunknown manifest field is refused with an error that points at the line, and it\nis — \"line 5: field filter not found\" — but the test only logged the error. It\nasserts now, on both the field name and a line number. Calibrated by wrapping\nthe parse error into a generic message, which makes all four cases report \"gives\nno line number\".","tree":{"sha":"2ee92c2e94793328a05f32b0dd04cc28d706a2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/2ee92c2e94793328a05f32b0dd04cc28d706a2da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDM4YmY1MjM2MzQzYWEyNzI5YWEyZjRmMWMyODYxZjEwZTUwMzQ4NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747","sha":"36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747"}],"sha":"38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/38bf5236343aa2729aa2f4f1c2861f10e5034855"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:02:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:02:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test(hostsvc): pin which permission gates which call, on both sides\n\nThe permission gate was already covered: tests/plugin_e2e_test.go proves it\nholds across the process boundary, tests/degraded_test.go proves a refusal is\nnot confusable with a Core that has no database. Nothing checked the mapping.\n\nThat is a different property. If Enqueue were gated on cache rather than queue\nthe mechanism would still work perfectly — it would simply be guarding the wrong\ndoor, and every existing test would stay green while a plugin approved for the\ncache reached the queue.\n\nSo all thirty host RPCs are now checked against a table that states, separately\nfrom the implementation, which permission each needs. The list comes from\nreflecting over pb.HostServicesServer rather than being written by hand: a new\nRPC fails here for want of an entry instead of arriving silently ungated.\n\nBoth directions are asserted, and the second is not padding:\n\n    grant everything except X  -> must be refused, naming X\n    grant only X               -> must not be refused\n\nCalibrated with three mutations. Gating Enqueue on cache fails both sides, the\nsecond naming the permission it actually asked for. Removing its gate entirely\nfails the first. Adding a spurious db check to Ack fails only the second — which\nis the case a one-sided test would wave through, and over-gating is a real\ndefect: it sends an author to ask for a permission the reviewer then cannot\njustify.\n\nThree RPCs deliberately need nothing — GetConfig, Log and RecordMetric. Refusing\nthose would leave an author unable to see why anything else was refused. Log is\na client stream and reads it immediately, so it panics on a zero-valued\nargument; that is accepted as evidence of reaching its own body, since a gate\nreturns a refusal rather than panicking, and the reasoning is written where it\nis relied on.\n\nFull suite green, twenty packages.","tree":{"sha":"7be82a568157e353038a8676e9dc57ce9778220c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7be82a568157e353038a8676e9dc57ce9778220c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDM2MTU5MjgxYmViNjUyMTlmODJmN2Q1ZDZmOTM4NjA5MGZjZDY3NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204","sha":"b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204"}],"sha":"36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/36159281beb65219f82f7d5d6f9386090fcd6747"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:50:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:50:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat(sdk): every capability reports itself without a Core, and a sweep keeps it that way\n\nLast round left this half done and wrote the reason into the guide: the other\nsix clients still panic when unbound, because the general fix — a stub\nHostServicesClient — needs fake streams for Consume, Subscribe and Log.\n\nThat reason was wrong, and wrong in a particular way worth naming. It described\nthe obstacle to the stub, which is not the design I had used. The guards\nactually written for DBClient return before touching anything, streams included.\nSo the work I recorded as blocked was seventeen early returns. Mistaking one\ndesign''s difficulty for another''s turned fifteen minutes into a documented\nasymmetry.\n\nNow guarded: TxClient, QueueClient, CacheClient, LockClient, FilesClient,\nEventClient, HTTPClient and Lease. Publish, Consume, Subscribe, Acquire, Renew,\nRelease and the rest return sdk.ErrHostUnavailable rather than dereferencing a\nnil client.\n\nPer-method guards have their own weakness: nothing makes the next method carry\none. TestEveryCapabilityReportsItselfWithoutACore walks the exported methods\nwith reflection and calls each on a nil receiver, so a new method arrives\nalready covered instead of waiting for someone to remember a list. It found 25.\n\nIt also found the one legitimate exception. DBClient.Where returns *Query with\nno error, because a query has to be buildable without a Core — Describe() is how\nquery construction is tested. Rather than skip it, the exception has its own\ncheck: the query builds, Describe reports it, and All, Rows, Count and Sum all\nreport ErrHostUnavailable. All four, because two of them ignored that field\nuntil this week while the other two honoured it and nothing ever set it.\n\nCalibrated in both directions. Delete a guard and it reports \"CacheClient.Set\npanicked on a nil client\". Change a guard to return nil instead of the error and\nit reports \"returned a nil error with no Core behind it, so a caller would treat\nthe call as having worked\" — the more dangerous of the two failures, since a\ncapability that silently succeeds is worse than one that crashes.\n\nFull suite green, twenty packages.","tree":{"sha":"93f9e796a31ac1d8b5b59ff6d6cfbf0d2aeb9057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/93f9e796a31ac1d8b5b59ff6d6cfbf0d2aeb9057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGI0NDgyMzZhMGVmNDkwNDhjOTY0YzQ4YmMzZTUyNDFjMjFjNDQyMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75","sha":"7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75"}],"sha":"b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b448236a0ef49048c964c48bc3e5241c21c44204"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:39:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:39:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test(examples): audit''s purge and its admin gate, measured before writing\n\nThe last example without tests, and the point was to check whether it needed\nany rather than to make the count come out even. Measured first:\n\n    recordWrite     four end-to-end tests already — an ordinary request, an\n                    oversized one refused at 413, with an identity, anonymous.\n                    Stronger than a unit test could be. Left alone.\n    onConfigChanged no coverage\n    purgeExpired    no coverage\n    listEntries     no coverage\n\nThe purge is the one that matters. It deletes the record of what happened, and\nnothing gets it back — too wide and the trail is gone, too narrow and the disk\nfills quietly. So the cutoff arithmetic is now pinned: computed from\njob.Scheduled rather than the clock, so a run delayed an hour deletes what it\nwould have deleted on time; and the 90-day cutoff is asserted to sort lexically\nbefore the 7-day one, because Lt compares strings and RFC3339 is used precisely\nso that lexical order is chronological order. Get that backwards and the delete\ntakes the wrong side of the boundary.\n\nlistEntries'' admin check is pinned for a different reason. Its own comment says\na menu''s roles: [admin] does not protect the route — that only hides the menu\nitem — and this is exactly the check someone deletes while simplifying. The\nfailure is silent: the audit trail just becomes readable by everyone.\n\nMutation-checked, four of them. Removing the admin gate, using time.Now()\ninstead of job.Scheduled, writing Gt where Lt belongs, and clamping an\nover-large page size to the ceiling instead of falling back to the default —\neach fails the test that names it, and all four restore to green.\n\nTwo extractions made this reachable, both the pattern established last round:\nexpiredQuery and entriesQuery return the query so Describe() can report what was\nbuilt, without a store behind it.\n\nAlso removed a stale comment. listEntries still carried a note from the\ndoc-only-author experiment — \"no .After()/.Cursor()/.Since() appears in any\nexample, guessing .After(cursor)\". The gap it recorded is closed: notes uses\n.After and the guide documents it. What was left was an example sounding unsure\nof itself.\n\nAll eight examples now carry tests. Full suite green, twenty packages.","tree":{"sha":"a20bbe7f7520914282f1a1b89f00fc6d82c7958d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/a20bbe7f7520914282f1a1b89f00fc6d82c7958d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDc5MjMwMDY1MDJkMjYyNzNkMzhlZWIyY2Q5NzI5Y2IyNGRkYTVlNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f","sha":"71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f"}],"sha":"7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7923006502d26273d38eeb2cd9729cb24dda5e75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:23:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:23:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat(sdk): a query can be inspected, and an unbound sdk.DB reports itself\n\nThe Where gap has been open for several rounds, recorded as \"queries cannot be\nrun in a test, so build an in-memory store or use the end-to-end path\". Both\nhalves of that were the wrong framing.\n\nWhat is actually unreachable is not the running — it is the query itself. Query\nhas entirely unexported fields and no read-only accessor, so an author cannot\neven assert what their code built. And building is where the decisions are: in\nnotes'' listing, whether the author filter was applied, whether the cursor was\ncarried, what the page size really is. None of that has anything to do with\nwhich rows come back.\n\nSo Query.Describe reports the request rather than the answer. Faking the builder\nmeans reimplementing it; inspecting it does not. The operator renders as its\nenum name minus the OP_ prefix rather than through a hand-written table of\nsymbols, which cannot drift when an operator is added.\n\nThis is deliberately not an in-memory store. One would have to reproduce\nsemantics like the one found two rounds ago — a predicate on a field a document\nlacks excludes it, Ne included, because the JSONB path is SQL NULL — and a fake\nthat gets that wrong is worse than no fake, because tests pass against the lie.\n\nTwo things turned up while wiring it. Query.err is a deferred-error field that\nnothing ever assigned, and Count and aggregate did not check it while All and\nRows did — a dead mechanism, inconsistently honoured. Both now check it, and\nWhere assigns it when there is no Core.\n\nsdk.DB''s methods also stopped segfaulting when unbound: Put, Get, Delete,\nPutIfVersion and Tx return sdk.ErrHostUnavailable. That makes validation logic\nreachable — notes refuses an untitled note before the store is touched, and a\ntest can now see it do so — and turns going past it into a sentence instead of a\ndead process.\n\nThe other six clients still panic when unbound, and the guide says so rather\nthan leaving it to be discovered. The general fix is a stub HostServicesClient\nreturning the same error, which the compiler would keep complete as methods are\nadded, but it needs fake streams for Consume, Subscribe and Log. Half a\nguarantee is more misleading than none, so it is written down as half.\n\nnotes has eight tests: the listing asks for the newest page with a limit, the\nauthor filter reaches the query, an empty parameter is not a filter on the empty\nstring, the cursor survives paging, an untitled note and a non-JSON body are\nrefused with 400 before the store, and a query builds without a Core but refuses\nto run. Mutation-checked — dropping the limit, sorting ascending, filtering on\nan empty author and losing the cursor each fail the test that names them.\n\nThe gap''s size now has two samples rather than one: 1 of 14 functions in apikey,\n3 of 11 in notes. The count overstates it either way — two of notes'' three are\n\"call Count and format\", and the one with judgement in it is what Describe now\ncovers.\n\nFull suite green, seven of eight examples carrying tests.","tree":{"sha":"70f64f7187637b8c4a72b2703f98cba40b7866a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/70f64f7187637b8c4a72b2703f98cba40b7866a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDcxZTY2NTFiOTI0ZDFlMmE3NTk0N2YzYWQxY2UwY2Q4NmIwNDNiOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483","sha":"966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483"}],"sha":"71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/71e6651b924d1e2a75947f3ad1ce0cd86b043b8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:02:24Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:02:24Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test(examples): syncer''s lock, and why this one needed no SDK change\n\nsdk.Lease has the same shape as sdk.TxClient did last round — an unexported\ngRPC client, so no test can build one — and the reflex was to widen it the same\nway. That would have been a second breaking change for nothing.\n\nA Lease is returned to the author; a TxClient is handed to the author''s\ncallback. A return value can be narrowed on the way past into an interface the\nplugin declares, and *sdk.Lease satisfies it with no SDK change at all. A\nparameter type is not the author''s to pick. The two gaps look identical and the\nanswers are opposite, which is now in the guide, along with the condition that\nmakes it work: Renew and Release are methods, and Lease.Expires is a field —\na field cannot be widened, so code needing it keeps the concrete type.\n\nWhat the tests cover is the part that is invisible in production until it has\nalready gone wrong twice: the lease is renewed while the work runs, and a\nrenewal reporting the lock gone stops the work rather than finishing it.\nFinishing is the double-write.\n\nMutation-checked. Continuing past a failed renewal fails two tests; dropping the\ndeferred release fails two; returning an error for a busy account instead of\nrequeueing fails the contention test — which is the accounting bug this example\ndocuments, where a message bounced between replicas burns its retry budget and\ndies having never failed.\n\nThree things went wrong on my side and are recorded rather than smoothed over.\n\nThe renewal interval is (work + leaseMargin)/3, not leaseMargin/3. I assumed the\nlatter, expected five renewals where one happened, and three tests failed. The\nfix was not new numbers but making the harness compute the interval and hand it\nback, so each test asserts against `tick` instead of against something I\nguessed.\n\nOne test then failed by 31ms — and reading the numbers, the implementation was\nright and my threshold was too tight. Loosening it would have passed with a 6%\nmargin, which is a flake waiting for a loaded machine. The fake now fails the\nfirst renewal instead of the second, which moves the margin to 50%.\n\nleaseMargin became a var so a test can shrink it. At the production 30s the\nrenewal path takes ten seconds to observe once, which in practice means nobody\ntests the one thing here most worth testing.\n\nAlso documented: a seam returning an interface must return an explicit nil when\nthe concrete pointer is nil, or the caller gets a non-nil interface holding a\nnil pointer and `if l == nil` is false — the nil surfaces later as a panic.\n\nFull suite green, six of eight examples now carrying tests.","tree":{"sha":"7ed65d4226b8c8ddee440ebdd82cbee39f46d398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7ed65d4226b8c8ddee440ebdd82cbee39f46d398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDk2NmNiZmJhZmVmYjhlMzVkMWVhODA1ZmI1Y2NkMDVmNmI5MTI0ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0","sha":"0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0"}],"sha":"966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/966cbfbafefb8e35d1ea805fb5ccd05f6b912483"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:43:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:43:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat(sdk)!: a transaction body takes sdk.TxOps, so it can be tested\n\nBREAKING: sdk.DB.Tx''s callback parameter changes from *sdk.TxClient to\nsdk.TxOps. A plugin written as func(tx *sdk.TxClient) error changes one type\nname; *TxClient satisfies the interface, so nothing else moves. Two call sites\nexisted in this repository — the inventory example and one doc snippet.\n\nTxClient holds an unexported gRPC client, so no test can build one, and a\ncallback typed to it could only be run by a live Core. That put the whole of\ninventory''s reserveOnce out of reach: read the level, refuse when short, take\nthe stock and record the reservation together, compute the remainder from the\nuncommitted write. Those are the invariants a transaction exists to protect, and\nthey are exactly what could not be tested. A worse gap than sdk.DB.Where, which\nis documented and blocks 1 of 14 functions there.\n\nThe blast radius was measured before the change rather than after. This repo''s\nhabit is one clean path over a compatibility layer — PLUGIN_DEV_MODE and the\nwhole tunnel were deleted rather than deprecated — and two call sites is as\ncheap as this ever gets. If the trade is wrong, reverting is the same one-line\nsignature.\n\ninventory now has seven tests over a recording fake: stock taken but not\nconsumed, both documents written or neither, the version read inside the\ntransaction written back, the remainder computed from the uncommitted value,\noversell refused with nothing written, exactly-what-is-available accepted, an\nunknown SKU refused, and a version conflict reported rather than swallowed.\n\nMutation-checked. Ignoring existing reservations fails the oversell test;\nchanging < to <= fails the boundary test; passing a constant instead of the\nversion read fails two. One mutation was invalid and is worth recording:\nreplacing PutIfVersion with Put left `version` unused, so the package did not\nbuild — a compile error is not a test catching anything, and it was redone as a\nconstant expectation to actually exercise the assertion.\n\nThe seam carries a real trap, now in the guide:\n\n    // not var runTx = sdk.DB.Tx\n    var runTx = func(ctx context.Context, timeout time.Duration, fn func(sdk.TxOps) error) error {\n        return sdk.DB.Tx(ctx, timeout, fn)\n    }\n\nsdk.DB is nil until Core hands over the reverse connection, so a method value\ncaptured at package initialisation binds that nil receiver permanently. It looks\ncorrect and panics on the first order in production — the same timing trap as\nreading configuration in main().\n\nAlso checked, and negative: whether the five runtime limits are actually\nenforced, not just documented correctly. All five are, and all five have tests.\nMy first probe said four were untested, because it searched for the constant\nname while the tests lower the limit through its configurable field\n(locks.MaxHeld = 10, events.MaxSubscriptionsPerPlugin = 3, pq.MaxDepth = 5) —\nwhich is the better way to test them. Third time this session a probe answered a\ndifferent question than the one asked.\n\nFull suite green, five example packages in it.","tree":{"sha":"6aeb6d5b79dc340efe3e4a99751977a8c708c2a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/6aeb6d5b79dc340efe3e4a99751977a8c708c2a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDBjZWEzODgzMTYyOGI0ZmI2NmFhMGI3MzU2ZDJkZTQ4YmQyNzJjYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629","sha":"53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629"}],"sha":"0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0cea38831628b4fb66aa0b7356d2de48bd272ca0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:31:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:31:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: the transaction limit says 4 and the code says 8, and now something checks\n\nAudited the two limits tables in the plugin guide against the constants they\ndescribe. Eleven numbers, one wrong:\n\n    037854a perf: raise the transaction ceiling to 8, measured\n      -const MaxOpenTxPerPlugin = 4\n      +const MaxOpenTxPerPlugin = 8\n\nThe table was correct when it was written and was never updated. The cost is\nconcrete: an author sizing concurrency against the guide leaves half their\nallowance unused, and one debugging a refusal starts looking four transactions\ntoo early.\n\nTen of eleven being right is what makes this hard to catch by reading. The table\nlooks maintained, and the wrong row is indistinguishable from the others until\nsomeone compares them to the source.\n\nSo each row now names its constant — a reader gets told where the truth lives,\nand TestDocumentedLimitsMatchTheCode gets an anchor it can match on instead of\nguessing which prose number means which limit. Calibrated on both axes: change\na documented value and it reports \"the guide says db.MaxOpenTxPerPlugin is 4,\nthe code says 8\", which is verbatim the bug that was there; delete a row and it\nreports \"found 10 of 11 limits in the guide; no row names [...]\" rather than\npassing on a smaller sweep.\n\nThe manifest table was extended into the same check even though all six of its\nrows were right. They rot the same way; being correct today is not the property\nworth relying on.\n\nOne of my own methods was wrong on the way, and it is in tests/README.md. To\nfind when the constant changed I used `git log -S \"MaxOpenTxPerPlugin = \"`,\nwhich returned exactly one commit — from which the conclusion would have been\nthat the constant never moved and the docs were wrong from the start. That is\nbackwards. -S is the pickaxe: it finds commits where the number of occurrences\nof a string changes, and rewriting `= 4` to `= 8` leaves the count untouched, so\nthe one commit that mattered was invisible to it. -G matches diff content and\nshows both.\n\nSame shape as the rest of this session: a probe that cannot see a thing and a\nprobe that finds nothing produce identical output. When a tool answers \"only\none\", ask what it was actually looking for.\n\nFull suite green.","tree":{"sha":"001dc8ee5ce29a380171fd54dc86a6eeab7dd9be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/001dc8ee5ce29a380171fd54dc86a6eeab7dd9be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDUzYjk0MzZjODg1NTNiNjdiNzYyMTZmNDc0ZTkyZTI4Y2U3NDk2Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56","sha":"02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56"}],"sha":"53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/53b9436c88553b67b76216f474e92e28ce749629"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:20:58Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:20:58Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test(examples): apikey''s security decisions had no tests, and the DB gap is smaller than I wrote\n\nSet out to close the gap the guide records twice — no in-memory double for\nsdk.DB, so anything touching the store needs a live Core. Measured the need\nbefore building it, on the example most dependent on the database.\n\nOf apikey''s 14 functions:\n\n    8   need no seam at all\n    5   need a Get/Put/Delete seam, which already works\n    1   hits sdk.DB.Where\n\nA conformance-tested in-memory store to unblock 1 of 14 is out of proportion,\nand the risk is not small: a fake that diverges is worse than none. Last round\nturned up that a predicate on a field a document lacks excludes that document,\nNe included, because the JSONB path is SQL NULL — a map-backed fake would\nalmost certainly get that wrong and authors would write passing tests against\nthe lie. So the gap stays open, with its size now written down rather than\nimplied.\n\nWhat the measuring turned up instead is that this plugin decides who may reach\nwhat and had no tests. authorize — the refusal itself — takes a context it does\nnot use and touches nothing, so it was testable all along and nobody had.\n\n    authorize    anonymous on a protected path, a nil Identity (a panic in a\n                 filter kills the process, not the request), an authenticated\n                 caller, an unprotected path, a path below a protected prefix,\n                 and nothing protected before an operator configures it\n    authenticate a valid key becomes an identity; an absent, unknown or revoked\n                 one leaves the caller anonymous rather than refused, because\n                 refusing is the authorize phase''s job\n    fail_closed  a store failure returns an error rather than anonymous access\n\nMutation-checked, since green is not the same as load-bearing. Swallowing\nlookup''s error fails the fail_closed test; letting authorize Continue for\nanonymous callers fails the table; changing isProtected from prefix to exact\nmatch fails it too, on the sub-path case. All three restore to green.\n\napikey''s OnConfigChanged was an anonymous closure passed to sdk.Serve, so\nprotected_prefixes — the list that decides who gets refused — was untestable by\nconstruction. That is the second example with this shape (redact was the first),\nwhich reads less like carelessness than like nothing having shown the\nalternative. It is a named configure now.\n\nauthenticate''s one host-backed step goes through a package-level `var resolveKey\n= lookup`. The guide now sets that beside digest''s interface field and says when\neach fits: a struct field for new plugins, a func var for code already built\naround package state, with the cost stated — global mutable state a test must\nrestore and cannot swap concurrently.\n\nFull suite green, four example packages in it.","tree":{"sha":"a6c5e1286f2e353eba922147ce3b727a5df8886f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/a6c5e1286f2e353eba922147ce3b727a5df8886f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDAyYmQ4MGRmYWNmNzU5MWJjMzFjZmVhNDIxMDczZjg1YmQ2NmRhNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471","sha":"de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471"}],"sha":"02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/02bd80dfacf7591bc31cfea421073f85bd66da56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:03:27Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:03:27Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: the benchmark fixture is part of the instrument, and it had drifted\n\nWent to check whether the documented latency table still held, since the gateway\nhot path has been rewritten several times since it was written. It did not:\nBenchmarkE2EPluginRequest measured 109µs against a documented 95µs, and the\nfilter-depth rows were 9-14% high. Core''s own route was unchanged at 40.6µs on\nboth versions, which appeared to rule out the environment — machine state and Go\nversion move every number in the same direction, not one up and one down.\n\nThat gave a self-consistent conclusion: this session''s correctness fixes — the\nlive registry lookup, the deferred log phase, the re-resolution after a rewrite\n— had cost 10% latency and 55 allocations per request. It would have gone into\nthe docs, and someone would have gone looking for it in Core.\n\nWhat stopped it was asking the same question three times.\n\nFirst, the benchmark file: 110 lines added, zero deleted, the three E2E\nfunctions byte-identical. Clean, so I continued.\n\nSecond, the profiles. A -base diff put our own FromProtoHeaders on top — but the\ntwo samples had run different iteration counts (32916 against 35617) and pprof\nsubtracts raw counts, not per-op ones. Redone with -benchtime=30000x on both\nsides, FromProtoHeaders drops off the list entirely. Its first place was an\nartefact of not normalising.\n\nThird, and only then, the fixture. tests/fixtures/echoplugin is the load every\none of these benchmarks runs against, and it grew 566 lines this session because\nit doubles as the prop for dozens of correctness tests. Two of those lines sit\non the default response path:\n\n    \"X-Saw-Probe\":   {Values: []string{firstHeader(req.GetHeaders(), \"X-Probe\")}},\n    \"X-Saw-Removed\": {Values: []string{firstHeader(req.GetHeaders(), \"X-Remove-Me\")}},\n\nfirstHeader returns \"\" when the header is absent, so every request — every\nbenchmark iteration — carried two empty headers across the wire. Every entry in\nthe profile diff matches: MIMEHeader.Add, canonicalMIMEHeaderKey, protobuf\nstring serialisation, Request.write.\n\nIsolating it settles it. This Core, the older fixture:\n\n    baseline Core + baseline fixture    272 allocs/op\n    HEAD Core     + HEAD fixture        327 allocs/op\n    HEAD Core     + baseline fixture    277 allocs/op\n\n50 of the 55 were the fixture. The real cost of this session''s fixes is +5\nallocs/op, 1.8%, with no latency I can measure.\n\nFixed both halves. The two headers are conditional now (327 -> 306), and\nTestTheBenchmarkFixtureStaysLean pins the default response''s shape —\ncalibrated by adding a header and watching it report \"carries 9 headers, want 8\"\nand name the offender.\n\nThe table in the plugin guide is refreshed to today''s numbers, with the caveats\nthis cost me: absolute values drift with Go version and machine state while\nratios do not; the fixture is part of the instrument; and the table in\ndeployment.md is a different instrument entirely (real stack, 300 requests per\nbucket, p50/p99 with a database) whose numbers must not be read against these.\nI did not touch those, having not re-measured them the same way.\n\nTwo mistakes of my own, recorded in tests/README.md rather than quietly dropped.\nI credited Core''s route going from 52µs to 41µs to this session''s hot-path work\n(89->86 allocs); the same benchmark on the baseline commit also measures 41µs,\nso that improvement is real but worth about 0µs, and what I had attributed to\ncode was the environment. And in writing the ratios I claimed a cross-process\nhop costs about four Core routes; it is 65µs against 41µs, so 1.6. A derived\nnumber needs checking as much as a measured one — more, because it reads as\nthough it came from the table when it only came from me.\n\nFull suite green.","tree":{"sha":"427397c3c37e51a0a11a2dc3dd476743dc65d4ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/427397c3c37e51a0a11a2dc3dd476743dc65d4ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGRlNDI4YzIxMDVjMTBjZDJjNzczNmRhNzkyMWQwOWVkYzdhMjc0NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24","sha":"51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24"}],"sha":"de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/de428c2105c10cd2c7736da7921d09edc7a27471"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:34:27Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:34:27Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat(examples): digest — the eighth example, covering the three untouched capabilities\n\nMeasured the capability surface against the examples: 11 permissions, 8 covered,\nand http:egress, files:write and files:read with no example between them. Those\nare the three nobody had written a real plugin against.\n\ndigest fetches a URL on a schedule through Core''s egress proxy, hashes what came\nback, and stores it as a file only when it differs from last time — with a small\nread API that hands out short-lived download links rather than bytes.\n\nLast round I recorded that a plugin author cannot test a successful\nsdk.HTTP.Get, since Core refuses egress to loopback and no address a test can\nlisten on will be dialled. That stands, but the conclusion I drew from it was\ntoo gloomy. The SDK deals in standard library types:\n\n    func (h *HTTPClient) Get(ctx, url string) (*http.Response, error)\n    func (f *FilesClient) Put(ctx, name, mime string, r io.Reader) (string, int64, error)\n    func (d *DBClient) Put(ctx, collection, id string, value any) (int64, error)\n\nso a one-method interface is satisfied by the SDK client directly, with no\nadapter. A seam costs almost nothing here — it had simply never been shown\nanywhere. digest''s whole job is covered by seven tests with no Core, no\ndatabase and no object storage, and the assertions at the foot of its test file\nhand that claim to the compiler instead of asking the reader to believe a\ncomment:\n\n    var _ fetcher = (*sdk.HTTPClient)(nil)\n\nThe behaviour worth having logic for is that unchanged content is not archived\nagain: a scheduled job that writes a file every run accumulates identical copies\nforever and the storage bill is the first anyone hears about it. The last digest\nlives in the store rather than a field, so a restart does not re-archive.\n\nMutation-checked rather than assumed green. Removing the skip fails\nTestUnchangedContentIsNotArchivedAgain and TestARestartDoesNotReArchive;\nreplacing job.Scheduled with time.Now() fails TestTheFirstRunArchivesWhatItFetched;\nrestoring returns all seven to green.\n\nA guard installed earlier proved itself on this, unplanned:\n\n    TestBuildOutputNamesAreIgnored/digest\n        ./digest is not ignored, so `go build ./extension-example/digest`\n        leaves something a `git add -A` will commit\n\nIt was calibrated against a synthetic canary; catching a real omission is better\nevidence than that was.\n\nOne thing changed after review rather than before. The listing first excluded\nthe marker document with Ne(\"id\", \"_latest\"), which works — a predicate compiles\nto `<jsonb path> != $1`, the path is SQL NULL for a document without the field,\nand `NULL != ''_latest''` is NULL, so the row drops out. Correct, and the opposite\nof what a reader expects Ne to mean. It is IsNotNull(\"file_id\") now, and the\nguide records the general rule, because a schemaless collection makes this\nreachable by anyone.\n\nHonest boundary, in the code, the README and the guide: sdk.DB.Where returns a\nconcrete fluent builder, so faking it means reimplementing it. That is the one\npart of the host surface with no natural seam, and it is why the list handler\nhas no unit test while the job has seven.\n\nFull suite green with the example included.","tree":{"sha":"cbce09a5ab9b9170af7e980c6bea1ae17b26b7cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/cbce09a5ab9b9170af7e980c6bea1ae17b26b7cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDUxZDhiNmEzM2YyN2Q2NzM5ZTc4ZTFjNzc0MmJiM2U1MTM3MGNkMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95","sha":"db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95"}],"sha":"51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/51d8b6a33f27d6739e78e1c7742bb3e51370cd24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:15:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:15:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix(sdk): logging must not decide whether a plugin''s code can be tested\n\nThe guide devotes a section to testing and opens it with the claim that a\nplugin''s handlers and filters are ordinary Go functions that test with ordinary\ngo test, no Core running. Seven shipped examples had no tests between them, so\nnobody had ever checked.\n\nWriting the first one — for ratelimit, the example with the least in its way,\ntouching no host capability at all — produced this:\n\n    panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference\n    sdk/plugin.(*Logger).log(0x0, ...)              host.go:870\n    extension-example/ratelimit.(*limiter).check    main.go:69\n\non the most ordinary shape there is:\n\n    sdk.Log.Warn(ctx, \"rate limit exceeded\", \"bucket\", key)\n    return sdk.Stop(http.StatusTooManyRequests, body), nil\n\nThe host clients are nil until Core hands over the reverse connection in\nConfigure, and Logger had no guard. Logging when refusing a request is what one\nwould write, so the documented claim was false for most real filters. sdk.Log\nappears in four of the seven examples and eleven times in the guide.\n\nLogger and its metric siblings are now nil-safe. Unbound records go to stderr —\nnot stdout, where they would replace the startup handshake — with fields sorted\nso a test can assert on the output. Metrics are dropped.\n\nScoped deliberately to logging and metrics rather than all eight clients.\nsdk.DB.Get is deliberate I/O and an author should structure a seam around it;\nsdk.Log.Warn is incidental and cross-cutting, appearing inside logic that is\notherwise pure. Whether a function can be unit-tested must not depend on\nwhether it happens to log. The remaining clients still panic when unbound,\nwhich is a poor diagnostic but does not block the documented pattern; the guide\nalready records the absence of in-memory doubles as a known gap.\n\nTwo examples now carry tests, which is what makes the claim checkable:\n\n  ratelimit  burst exhaustion, the 429, Retry-After\n  redact     both traps it documents — that a short circuit carries only its\n             own headers, and that Continue is correct when nothing changed —\n             plus the four pass-through paths\n\nThey also form the control that keeps this honest: redact logs nothing, so its\ntests passed before the fix as well as after. Only the logging path changed.\n\nredact''s OnConfigChanged was an anonymous closure passed to sdk.Serve, which a\ntest cannot reach, so its normalisations (lowercasing field names, defaulting\nthe mask) were untestable by construction. It is a named configure now, matching\nratelimit, and the guide says why that matters.\n\nFull suite green, including the two example packages for the first time.","tree":{"sha":"899da0f7ff676f5fd68a5506ec2fa32dcadf1673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/899da0f7ff676f5fd68a5506ec2fa32dcadf1673"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGRiMDZkYThjN2JkMmU1YmYxNzdjMTE4YTRhOGVjNTI0YmZhN2ViOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921","sha":"6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921"}],"sha":"db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/db06da8c7bd2e5bf177c118a4a8ec524bfa7eb95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:57:22Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:57:22Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: extend the database lock to all four packages that share it\n\nThe previous commit locked the tests package and I treated the problem as\nsolved. It was half solved. Asking \"who else touches this database\" — one grep,\nwhich I ran only after pushing — turned up four packages, not one:\n\n    core/auth   core/db   core/hostsvc   tests\n\n`go test ./...` runs packages concurrently, and core/db is the most destructive\nof them: it TRUNCATEs plugin_queue outright, with nothing qualifying it. So the\nqueue tests in tests/ can have their table emptied underneath them during a\nsingle ordinary invocation. No one has to misuse anything.\n\nReproduced by hammering core/db while the queue tests ran:\n\n    --- FAIL: TestQueueRedeliversAfterConsumerCrash\n        the message was never redelivered after its consumer died;\n        work handed to a plugin that crashed has been lost\n    --- FAIL: TestDeadMessagesDoNotShowInTheDepth\n        dead depth = 2, want 3\n\nThe first of those accuses the framework of losing work when a plugin crashes.\nIt is false — the queue is fine — but it is a P0-shaped claim produced by a\nneighbouring package clearing the table. This is strictly worse than what the\nprevious commit fixed: that one needed someone to run two suites at once, this\none needs nothing. It stayed hidden because core/db finishes in about a second\nwhile tests runs for over three minutes, so the overlap is only the opening\nseconds — which is exactly the profile of a rare, unreproducible failure.\n\nThe lock therefore moves to internal/dbtest (a package, not a _test.go file,\nbecause four packages need it) and all four TestMains take it. Under identical\nhammering: 3 failures before, 0 after.\n\nThen the same question, asked systematically rather than once:\n\n    PostgreSQL   four packages     serialised by the lock\n    S3 / MinIO   tests only        single package, no cross-package exposure\n    t.Parallel   0 uses in tests/  no intra-package collisions\n\nThat table is in tests/README.md to record the boundary of the audit, so the\nnext rare failure starts from \"is there a new shared resource\" rather than\nfrom scratch.\n\nCost is close to nothing: the fast packages finish while tests is still\ncompiling its fixture, and even when they do wait, they wait concurrently with\ntests running. Full suite 222s against 219.7s before — within noise. Green,\n0 leftover directories.\n\nWhether this is what produced the unexplained 338s darwin failure I cannot say:\nthe mechanism is confirmed to exist and to produce failures of exactly that\ncharacter, but I discarded that run''s log, so the specific claim is not\navailable. The mechanism is closed either way.","tree":{"sha":"f87f1d1928093401e47dd82f848067dec3728677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/f87f1d1928093401e47dd82f848067dec3728677"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZmZDYyYWIwNzRlOTJkZDY2ZGNhYWM4YmY3ZGMxOTRhMzQxMTU5MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa","sha":"bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa"}],"sha":"6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6fd62ab074e92dd66dcaac8bf7dc194a34115921"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:48:52Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:48:52Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: make the suite''s exclusive use of the database enforced, and stop leaking 12.2GB\n\nAn unexplained darwin failure at 338s was left open last round with the\nsuspicion that a second suite sharing the machine was to blame. Rebuilt that\ncondition deliberately — two full suites, one database — and the suspicion was\nwrong about the mechanism: both suites failed, 19 times between them, and the\ncounts were exact doubles.\n\n    listed 4 dead messages, want 2\n    dead depth = 6, want 3\n    the first publish reported itself as a duplicate\n\nContention makes a run slow; it does not make a count double. Two writers do.\nFixtures address rows by the plugin key from their own manifest — owner_key\n''syncer'', ''crasher'' — and clear them with unqualified DELETEs and TRUNCATEs.\nThose keys are the plugins'' real identifiers and those tables are the ones Core\nprovisions for them, so neither takes a per-run suffix without generating a\nfresh manifest for every run and testing something other than what ships.\n\nSo exclusive use of the database is an inherent requirement of this suite, and\nit was never stated, let alone enforced. Sequential re-runs were unaffected —\neach fixture clears its own rows on the way in — so -count=2 passes and gives\nno warning. The only way it surfaced was as a batch of failures indistinguishable\nfrom a real queue defect. That is what makes it worth enforcing: the cost is\nmeasured in hours spent debugging code that is correct.\n\nTestMain now holds a pg_advisory_lock. Re-running the same experiment: 0\nfailures, and the second suite reports 434.310s against the first''s 217.868s —\nthe doubling is the wait, so the serialisation is measured rather than assumed.\n\nSeparately, and found on the way: os.Exit does not run deferred functions, so\nthe `defer os.RemoveAll(dir)` sitting directly above `os.Exit(m.Run())` in two\nTestMains had never fired once.\n\n    tests/plugin_e2e_test.go        516 dirs   9.0GB\n    core/pluginhost/launch_test.go  185 dirs   3.2GB\n\nIt hid because it changes no test result — the suite stays green while the disk\nquietly disappears. Both now do their work in a run(m) returning int. Verified\nfrom a cleared baseline: 0 directories before, 0 after.\n\nFixing two instances does not fix the class, so tests/testmain_defer_test.go\nwalks every TestMain in the repository with go/ast and fails on any that mixes\ndefer with os.Exit.\n\nTwo mistakes of my own are recorded in tests/README.md rather than quietly\ncorrected. The detector''s first version calibrated only its judgement, not its\nreach — positive and negative controls proved it could tell good from bad, but\na wrong root would have left it silently scanning nothing and still passing. It\nnow also asserts what it saw: \"checked 2 TestMain across 98 test files\". And\nthe lock''s waiting message was invisible where it mattered: go test discards a\npassing package''s output unless -v, so the person watching an apparently hung\nterminal for 3.6 minutes saw nothing. It now writes to /dev/tty as well, which\nhad to be verified under a real pty via script(1) — testing tty behaviour\nthrough a pipe returns a misleading negative.\n\nFull suite green: tests 219.697s, 0 leftover directories.","tree":{"sha":"870512873c6292d543fbccb1ca2b05c52f59c27b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/870512873c6292d543fbccb1ca2b05c52f59c27b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGJmMWU2YjlmMmY4NWE1M2Y4ODE4ZDY4ZmY3MWY2NmIxMTMyYmJkYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781","sha":"15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781"}],"sha":"bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bf1e6b9f2f85a53f8818d68ff71f66b1132bbdaa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:17:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:17:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: what a clean -race run does and does not rule out\n\nCLAUDE.md lists `go test ./... -race` among the standard checks and I had not\nrun it once this session, across a lot of concurrency work: the queue''s\nin-flight count, awaitRoom, the readyDone channel, resolving filter targets\nagainst the live registry, deferring logPhase. It is also the obvious next\nmove on the unexplained darwin failure, since contention widens exactly the\nwindows a real race lives in.\n\nClean: zero DATA RACE reports, every package passing.\n\nStated carefully, because it is easy to over-read. It rules out unsynchronised\nconcurrent access on the paths the tests reach. It does not close the failure,\nand it would not have found either concurrency bug this session already fixed\n— Drain killing a process while the consumer was still trying to nack, and\nAppView''s sync re-entering and mounting twice. Both are correctly synchronised\nand wrong about ordering: every memory access is properly guarded, and what is\nwrong is who waits for whom. Both needed a deterministic arrangement to\nreproduce — a held unmount, a slow filter parking a request — not more runs.\n\nThe useful number: 247s with -race against 220s without, 12%. This suite\nspends its time launching real plugin processes and waiting on timing rather\nthan on CPU, so the detector is cheap enough to leave on by default. Recorded\nin CLAUDE.md next to the command.","tree":{"sha":"40e4d1e466a6715b5b70e5fcf0553f5e087e4006","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/40e4d1e466a6715b5b70e5fcf0553f5e087e4006"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDE1Y2NiOTVmZjkyMDEyZmEzZGFmODZmNWU0NWRiYWQzMGFlOTc3ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d","sha":"422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d"}],"sha":"15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/15ccb95ff92012fa3daf86f5e45dbad30ae97781"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:03:00Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:03:00Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: the guide''s symbol check never looked past the first segment\n\nAdding three sections to the guide, I went to confirm the test that keeps it\nhonest actually covered them. It did not.\n\nThe pattern was `\\bsdk\\.([A-Z]\\w*)`, which captures one segment. In\nsdk.Log.Gauge it matched sdk.Log — a real name — and never looked at the\nmethod. So every `sdk.X.Y()` in the guide was checked as far as X, which is\nmost of how the guide refers to the SDK at all. Writing sdk.Log.Timer, a\nmethod that does not exist, passed. A second mechanism scanned Go code fences\nand caught some of these by accident; the metric kinds are documented in a\ntable, so nothing checked them.\n\nChecked references went from 42 to 59, and both mutations now fail: an\ninvented method in a table, and one in a code block.\n\nUnresolved, and recorded rather than closed: one full-suite run on darwin\nfailed at 338s against a usual 214s, while the same commit passed on Linux at\n166s, passed alone at 211s, and passes again here at 220s with the whole log\nkept. I cannot say what failed — my own command filtered the output down to\n`FAIL` and discarded the detail, so the run that failed is the only place the\nreason existed and it is gone. Load is a reasonable suspicion (two suites and\na container were sharing the machine and one Postgres) and it is not a\nfinding. Two failures in this session that looked exactly like load noise\nturned out to be real bugs, so it stays open.\n\nCLAUDE.md now runs the suite into a log file and greps the failures out of it,\nso the next one leaves evidence instead of a single word.","tree":{"sha":"7828c3e7588eba0f7f42b0be79ada51a2471d323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7828c3e7588eba0f7f42b0be79ada51a2471d323"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQyMmMzMjk3ZTFhOTk2MjYzNGNjNmNhNzVmMzAzMDQ1NWQwYmFlMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2","sha":"697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2"}],"sha":"422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/422c3297e1a9962634cc6ca75f3030455d0bae1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:53:30Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:53:30Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: a query result names its documents\n\nHanding the guide to somebody who had never seen the SDK, and asking them to\nwrite a plugin that deletes matching documents, produced one report I did not\nexpect: it cannot be done. They were right, and it is not a documentation gap.\n\nAll() decodes the document bodies and returns no ids. Delete and PutIfVersion\nboth take an id. So \"delete everything matching this filter\" — the ordinary\nreason to run a query — was unwritable unless the author had thought to\nduplicate the id inside the document body first. Core reads those ids on every\nquery and threw all but the last away; that one it kept, inside the cursor.\n\nSomebody who has read the source cannot find this. I know to put the id in the\nbody, so I never noticed that knowing it was necessary.\n\nQueryResponse now carries ids alongside documents, and Query.Rows returns them\nwith the decoded values. All is unchanged. Verified against PostgreSQL rather\nthan a fake: the ids that come back are the ones Put used, and deleting by\nthem empties the collection. A fake proves the field travels and nothing more.\n\nThe same experiment found two places where an implementation moved and the\nguide did not follow — both from this session''s own work. Gauge and Histogram\nwere added because Core has always handled three metric kinds and the SDK\nexposed one, and appeared in the guide zero times, so the author reported\nthere was no kind to pick. Renew was mentioned in a comment with no signature,\nand they declined to call a method whose signature they would have to invent —\nskipping lease renewal, which is the correct thing to do for long work.","tree":{"sha":"62e1b31d7309309adca83ce99b835245c940a3a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/62e1b31d7309309adca83ce99b835245c940a3a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDY5N2I1ODQ1ZTE1MjU4YmFlODgzZDE5ZDM2OTM1MGVkNzkzYmNkYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f","sha":"9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f"}],"sha":"697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/697b5845e15258bae883d19d369350ed793bcdc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:22:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:22:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: build outputs of two examples were not ignored\n\nTurning the last hardcoded example lists into discovery found something real\nrather than tidying. TestBuildOutputNamesAreIgnored checked six names against\nseven examples, so `go build ./extension-example/redact` or `.../syncer` left a\nbinary in the working tree that nothing objected to — and a `git add -A` would\nhave taken it. Four 18MB binaries reached this repository that way earlier in\nthis session, which is why that test exists.\n\n.gitignore had the same list and the same omission. Its comment explains why\nthe names are spelled out rather than matched by a pattern, and the reasoning\nholds; what it did not anticipate is somebody adding an example and not adding\nthe line. The list stays, and the test that discovers the examples now guards\nit.\n\nAlso makes six_plugins_test live up to its own comment. It says \"installs every\nshipped example\" and installed six of seven, so the composition it exists to\nexercise had quietly stopped being all of them. Confirmed after: seven\nexamples in one Core, syncer''s two replicas included, with the identity still\ntravelling from apikey''s authenticate filter through notes to audit''s record.\n\nintegration_test''s three-plugin list is left alone. It picks three\ndeliberately, and a hardcoded list is right when the comment says \"these\nthree\" rather than \"all of them\" — which is the distinction tests/README.md\nnow records, along with the guard that discovery must fail loudly when it\nfinds nothing.","tree":{"sha":"02aa32ad95b806ba2389abf598ff756242efb893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/02aa32ad95b806ba2389abf598ff756242efb893"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDk2NjFkOTJhYzUyNzA0MDZjYzUwY2Q3ZDYxZjlhZjgzMmQwNTg3NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce","sha":"7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce"}],"sha":"9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9661d92ac5270406cc50cd7d61f9af832d05876f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:11:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:11:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: find the examples instead of listing them\n\nTwo tests each kept a hand-written list of six examples. There are seven.\nsyncer was added a few commits ago and neither list was updated, so the newest\nexample — the one least likely to have been checked against a validation rule\nadded since — was the one nothing validated or started.\n\nThe timing makes the point sharper: max_body_bytes gained a rule in the same\nstretch of work, and redact was fixed by hand for it. Had syncer tripped the\nsame rule, nothing would have said so.\n\nA list of examples is exactly the kind of thing that stops being true without\nanyone noticing, because nothing fails when it does. Discovered from the\ndirectory now, with a guard that fails outright if discovery finds nothing —\notherwise both tests pass by covering nothing, which is the false green this\nsession keeps turning up.\n\nAlso corrects an assertion that would have failed syncer for being right:\nTestExamplesStart insisted on exactly one ready replica, and syncer declares\ntwo on purpose. It now compares against what the manifest asks for, and both\nof syncer''s replicas are confirmed up.\n\nChecked by adding a probe example with a manifest that breaks the\nmax_body_bytes rule: it was picked up automatically and rejected.","tree":{"sha":"4163b791be1d6c7dfd727f0519649564b0bbc916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/4163b791be1d6c7dfd727f0519649564b0bbc916"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDc5MDRkNjEzODYxNmM0OWJlMzM2NWZiOTlhZmQ2MTAyZTUwZjY0Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27","sha":"fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27"}],"sha":"7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/7904d6138616c49be3365fb99afd6102e50f64ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:01:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:01:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: the environment Core reads and the one the docs promise stay one set\n\nNothing was wrong: the two sides already agree. The check is here because the\ndrift is gradual and silent in both directions.\n\nA variable Core reads and nobody wrote down is a knob only its author knows\nabout, so the operator who needs it never finds it. A variable the docs promise\nand Core no longer reads is worse — somebody sets it, deploys, and the\nbehaviour they were told to expect does not happen, with nothing anywhere to\nexplain it. That one is not hypothetical: PLUGIN_DEV_MODE was documented in\nthree places and read in one, and removing it meant hunting the entries down by\nhand.\n\nThe test fails if the pattern ever stops matching, rather than passing because\nit found nothing — which is the shape of every false green this session has\nturned up. Both directions are mutation-checked: a variable read but\nundocumented fails, and one documented but unread fails.\n\nThe comparison that led here was itself wrong first time. grep -h strips the\nfilename, so the -v _test that was meant to exclude test files had nothing to\nfilter, and the list of \"what Core reads\" quietly included MODULESS_TEST_SECRET\nfrom a test file. A filter that silently does not apply is the same family as\nthe git ls-files scope, the pgrep that matched nothing, and the ps output that\nwas truncated.","tree":{"sha":"74de3f132ebcd88b5747e188500bffc5ee0f5325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/74de3f132ebcd88b5747e188500bffc5ee0f5325"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGZjYTliMTFlZjA1ZTVmYjc1NmIzZTYwMjhmMWNiMzJjN2E1ZmFhMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330","sha":"8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330"}],"sha":"fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fca9b11ef05e5fb756b3e6028f1cb32c7a5faa27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:41:57Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:41:57Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: a restore procedure, and the trap that undoes it\n\nLast commit made a migration tell operators to restore from a backup. The\nbackup section listed what to back up and gave no command for taking one, and\nthere was no restore procedure at all — so the error message pointed at\ninstructions that did not exist.\n\nWriting them turned up the trap. InitDB calls RunMigrations unconditionally\nwith no way to skip it, and the document already said as much a few lines\nlower without connecting the two: restore a pre-migration dump, start the\ncurrent Core, and it migrates the schema straight back. The rollback the\noperator just performed is undone in the first second, and nothing on screen\nsays so. So the procedure now leads with pinning the Core version to match the\ndump, before the restore rather than after.\n\nThe commands are ones I ran rather than ones that look right: pg_dump -Fc\nagainst the test database produced 166KB, pg_restore rebuilt 26 tables in a\nscratch database, and the scratch was dropped.\n\nAnd the claim that makes the procedure necessary is now a test rather than a\nsentence. TestInitDBMigratesTheDatabase fails if a skip flag is ever added —\nwhich would make this document quietly wrong at the moment somebody is\nfollowing it under pressure, which is the only moment it gets read.\n\nAlso states what a schema rollback can and cannot do: it handles \"the\nmigration I just applied is wrong\" and not \"take me back several versions\",\nbecause 000008 refuses and says so. Backups are the answer to the second, and\nnow there are instructions for them.","tree":{"sha":"98ab6e4f0d8e85bff0e520b81c27a1e343c9672f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/98ab6e4f0d8e85bff0e520b81c27a1e343c9672f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDhiOTE5NzBhN2VkYzU4YjA2NjFmMTM4N2RjYTc5MTk1MTM4OWMzMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c","sha":"07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c"}],"sha":"8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8b91970a7edc58b0661f1387dca791951389c330"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:31:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:31:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a rollback that walks past a one-way door now says so\n\nRunMigrations only ever calls Up, and nothing anywhere called Down — so the\neleven .down.sql files in this repository had never been executed by Core or\nby a test. They looked like a rollback capability. Whether they were one would\nhave been discovered by whoever first needed to roll back, at the moment they\nneeded it.\n\nThe first attempt failed, and not because a down was written wrong. 000008\ndropped the extension tables and declines to recreate them, which is the right\ncall — the model they served is gone, so rebuilding them gives empty shells\nrather than data. But it declined by doing nothing, and `migrate down` does not\nstop at a migration that does nothing. It carried on, and 000005 then tried to\nALTER a table 000008 had dropped. What an operator saw was `relation\n\"extensions\" does not exist`, three migrations away from the decision that\ncaused it.\n\nSo 000008 now refuses out loud, naming itself and saying to restore from a\nbackup. The alternative — making the chain walk through — would report a\nsuccessful rollback that had restored nothing, which is worse than failing.\n\nTwo tests, against a throwaway database so Down cannot take the schema out\nfrom under the rest of the suite: everything after the door rolls back and\nre-applies, checked down to the column 000011 adds rather than just the table\nit belongs to; and going further fails with a message naming both the\nmigration and what to do instead.\n\nThe reversible window is counted from the directory rather than written down.\nA constant would still pass after somebody adds 000012 — it would just stop\ncovering the newest migration, the one most likely to have a rollback nobody\nhas tried. Checked by adding a probe migration: the window followed to four,\nand breaking its down was caught.\n\nConfirmed these run rather than skip on Linux too. They have three skip exits,\nand any of them turns \"verified on Linux\" into nothing while the output still\nreads ok.","tree":{"sha":"633045f2fddaedf56ae96f8cb3c9ce6475ed1af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/633045f2fddaedf56ae96f8cb3c9ce6475ed1af4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDA3YzVhYTBiMGMzODE3YmQ0MDg3N2ZiMzVjMzgzMzU0MWRkN2E4OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1","sha":"35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1"}],"sha":"07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/07c5aa0b0c3817bd40877fb35c3833541dd7a89c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:07:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:07:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: cover the guard on the plugin list''s actions\n\nact starts and stops OS processes and had never been called by a test — the\nnine next door are all about what the list renders. It carries a guard of the\nshape that had just turned out broken in AppView: state set around an await,\nholding the interface together. Here it is written correctly, which is not the\nsame as being safe from the next edit.\n\nFive cases, and the double-click is not the important one. busy is released in\na finally, and if it were released only on success a single failed disable\nwould leave every button on the page dead until a reload — with an error\nmessage on screen explaining something else entirely, so the operator reads\nthe frozen page as a consequence of that error.\n\nEach mutation is caught: releasing busy only on success fails one, setting it\nafter the await rather than before fails all five, refreshing the menu on a\nfailed action fails one. The middle one failing everywhere is the point —\n\"claim before you yield\" is what AppView was missing, and here several tests\nsee it from different angles.\n\nAlso pinned: a failed action leaves the list on screen, because an operator\nwho cannot see the other plugins cannot tell what else is affected.","tree":{"sha":"80fff7040ab4cb5812ead8a5cf102077a9bbba57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/80fff7040ab4cb5812ead8a5cf102077a9bbba57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDM1MzgwYWM0MTczYjc2Yjc2ZmYwYjc5ODA1M2I4OTQ2MmRjYjUxZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff","sha":"116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff"}],"sha":"35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/35380ac4173b76b76ff0b798053b89462dcb51f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:54:13Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:54:13Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: AppView mounted a micro-app twice when two triggers overlapped\n\nsync guards against redundant work with a synchronous key comparison at the\ntop of an asynchronous function, and the key it compares against was written\nonly after the mount finished — while unmountCurrent cleared it on the way\npast. So a second trigger arriving before the first had finished unmounting\nsaw an empty key, passed the guard, and mounted again. The reference to the\nfirst was then overwritten, and that app was never taken down: a micro-app\nleft running in a container nothing points at, for as long as the console\nstays open.\n\nTwo triggers in one tick is the obvious case and not the only one. Any two\nwithin the time an unmount takes will do — navigating while an SSE event lands\na millisecond later is enough, and the registry watcher exists precisely so\nthose two coincide.\n\nIt was invisible because the test double diverged from what it stands for.\nuseRoute() returns a reactive object and the mock was a plain one, so\n`watch(() => route.path, sync)` never fired at all: every route-driven case in\nthe file was being carried by the registry watcher happening to read the new\npath. Making the mock reactive turned three existing tests red immediately —\nthree mounts where two were expected, and seven where the outgoing app throws.\n\nMutation testing corrected me twice on the way. I first credited the fix to\nclaiming the key before yielding; removing that changed nothing. Then a\n\"different targets\" test turned out to create no race at all, because Vue\ncoalesces changes from one source within a flush and both watchers call the\nsame sync, which reads the current route — so two triggers in a tick always\ncompute the same target. The race across flushes needed the unmount held open,\nwhich is what the test does now.\n\nWhat carries it is the generation check: removing that fails five. The early\nclaim failed nothing and the scenarios where it could differ end in the same\nstate, so it is gone rather than left reading as though it were load-bearing.","tree":{"sha":"5d97bf45f068368b96340657b615f3d066129e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/5d97bf45f068368b96340657b615f3d066129e0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDExNjg2NGRjNDFhMTAyZWE0Y2QwZDVjM2EwOWRjY2VhNGJiYmNiZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0","sha":"bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0"}],"sha":"116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/116864dc41a102ea4cd0d5c3a09dccea4bbbcbff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:40:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:40:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: cover the SSE stream that keeps the console from going quietly stale\n\nThe console learns that a plugin was enabled or disabled from a server-sent\nevent, which is the whole of requirement 4''s \"without a refresh\". The registry\nreplacement had tests and so did the mounting; the wire between them — the\nEventSource handler that refetches — had none.\n\nWhat that guards against does not look like an error. A stream that has\nquietly died leaves the console showing the menu it already had, so an\noperator who has just disabled a plugin watches its pages carry on working,\nand nothing anywhere says why.\n\nSix cases: credentials on the stream so the session cookie travels, a refetch\non registry.changed, the connected flag going both ways, reopening after an\nerror rather than sitting on a dead stream, opening nothing more after\nunsubscribe, and a failed refetch not taking the page down.\n\nMutation testing found a flaw in one of my own assertions. Removing the\nclearTimeout on unsubscribe left all six passing, because what actually\nprevents the reopen is the closed flag the retry checks first — the pending\ntimer still fires and does nothing. The behaviour is the contract and two\nguards deliver it, but the test was named as though it pinned the timer, so it\nis now named for what it pins and says which guard is load-bearing.\n\nTwo areas were checked and left alone. Egress has fifteen tests including\nredirects, cloud metadata, internal addresses and hop-by-hop headers. The\nevent bus still drops for a slow subscriber, deliberately — best-effort is the\ncontract, durable work belongs on the queue — and it no longer drops silently,\nwith main.go installing the hook that reports it.","tree":{"sha":"8d94a8edf615f643d03dd4891a8f79761e78acf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/8d94a8edf615f643d03dd4891a8f79761e78acf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGJmZDVhMWNkNzk3OGExMmVkOWZjMjM3NzNiZDQ4MTkzZTA3ZWNjYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3","sha":"60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3"}],"sha":"bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bfd5a1cd7978a12ed9fc23773bd48193e07eccb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:22:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:22:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: drop the trace-id context nothing read\n\nrequestWithContext put the trace id into the downstream request''s context on\nevery non-plugin route, and TraceIDFromContext existed for handlers to read it\nback. Nothing ever called the accessor. The one place that wanted the id — the\naudit middleware — sits outside this handler and never saw that context at\nall; it now reads X-Request-Id off the response, which is set before anything\ndownstream runs and needs no plumbing.\n\nSo every request to Core''s own routes was paying for a value nobody read.\nMeasured on BenchmarkE2ECoreRoute: 89 allocs/op and 8451 B/op before, 86 and\n8064 after — three allocations rather than the two I expected, since\nr.WithContext copies the Request as well. Time is inside the noise, as it is\nfor anything at this scale.\n\nRecorded because fixing a hole and leaving the pipe next to it is easy to do:\nthe audit fix went in through the response header, which made this path dead\nthe moment it landed. Left in place it would read as load-bearing to whoever\ncame next.","tree":{"sha":"52b817facc6118d70fad89d4b6c87bed44386149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/52b817facc6118d70fad89d4b6c87bed44386149"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDYwYzMwM2MwMTcyMjE1MTlmMjJjNTY4NjYzMzFhZDNjNDg2MjAzYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9","sha":"6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9"}],"sha":"60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/60c303c017221519f22c56866331ad3c486203c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:14:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:14:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: an audit record carries the trace of the request that caused it\n\nCore assigns a trace to every request, publishes it as X-Request-Id, and the\nplugin''s own log lines carry it — verified this round, along with the four log\nlevels, which had no test between them. The audit trail was the one place it\nnever landed: audit_logs had no column for it, so \"admin deleted user 5\" could\nnot be tied to the request that did it, nor to anything the plugins logged\nwhile doing it. Which is most of what an audit trail is for.\n\nFound by scanning for functions nothing calls. TraceIDFromContext had no\ncaller in source or tests, and the comment above it says Core''s own handlers\ncan log the trace alongside the plugin ones. None of them do.\n\nWiring it up ran into the reason: the audit middleware wraps the plugin\ngateway, and the trace is assigned inside that gateway and travels downstream\non a request this middleware never sees. Its own context is the outer one. But\nthe gateway publishes the same id as X-Request-Id before anything else runs,\nand the middleware records after next returns — so it reads it back off the\nresponse, and no ordering has to change.\n\nThe tests check that the three agree — what the caller sent, what came back,\nwhat was written — rather than that the field is non-empty, which for a join\nkey would mean nothing. A request that sends no id of its own still gets one,\nbecause a column where every unattributed row shares the empty string looks\nlike a join key and is not one. Removing the single line that carries it fails\nboth.\n\nVerified on Linux as well as darwin, with the database reachable so the audit\npath actually runs: 164s against the 61s the container manages without it.","tree":{"sha":"ef7cdbd8c8822b86c73a675594837516f47e8153","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ef7cdbd8c8822b86c73a675594837516f47e8153"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZlZTZjYTA3MmRlYTkxOTNhYzY1MWRmZjRlZTliNWIzOTg0YzVlYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3","sha":"097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3"}],"sha":"6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6ee6ca072dea9193ac651dff4ee9b5b3984c5eb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:00:46Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T07:00:46Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: how to make the Linux run cover more than a third of the suite\n\nThe container run documented here reaches no database or object storage, so\neverything gated on TEST_DATABASE_URL and TEST_S3_ENDPOINT skips — which is\nmost of the queue, lock and transaction coverage. Measured: 61s against 164s\nonce the host''s services are reachable through host.docker.internal.\n\nWorth spelling out because the whole reason to run on Linux is the behaviour\nthat differs there, and this session changed several things in that area\nwhile only ever seeing the shorter run. Also names the two tests that exist\nonly on Linux, since neither can be observed from the development machine at\nall.","tree":{"sha":"134a97aef5130f407697d5011f2f572e8803868b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/134a97aef5130f407697d5011f2f572e8803868b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDA5N2Y3ZjAzOTAxZjI0OWZkZDQyNTE1YzA2NGExYWRlZjEwZDA5ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9","sha":"a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9"}],"sha":"097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/097f7f03901f249fdd42515c064a1adef10d09e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T06:55:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T06:55:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: drop PLUGIN_DEV_MODE, whose own rationale does not hold\n\nDevMode existed to skip Pdeathsig, on the argument that \"air restarts Core on\nevery rebuild and taking every plugin down with it makes the edit loop\npainful\". Two measurements say that trade bought nothing:\n\n  - A second Core does not reattach to a surviving plugin. Nothing uses\n    go-plugin''s ReattachConfig, so the new Core execs a fresh process and the\n    old one is abandoned — measured, one plugin process before a restart and\n    two after. The cold start it was avoiding happens anyway.\n  - A graceful restart, which is what air does, already drains every plugin\n    through main.go''s registry.DrainAll. So the skip only ever took effect\n    when Core died *without* draining, which is precisely the case where an\n    orphan is pure cost.\n\nSo it paid an orphan per plugin per rebuild for nothing, and skipping\nPdeathsig was its only effect. Pdeathsig is now unconditional and the flag is\ngone, from the code, the env table and the docs.\n\nVerified where it means something. Pdeathsig does not exist on darwin, so a\ngreen run here says nothing about this change; TestPdeathsigKillsOrphanedPlugins\nis behind a linux build tag and had been skipped all session. Run in the\ncontainer it passes: the kernel takes the plugin with its parent.\n\nThat first Linux run also caught a defect in a guard test of my own.\nTestBuildOutputNamesAreIgnored shells out to git check-ignore, golang:alpine\nships no git, and the test reported \"./notes is not ignored\" — announcing the\nthing it checks as broken when the check could not run at all. check-ignore\nhas three outcomes, not two: 0 ignored, 1 not, and 127/128 unable to answer.\nIt now skips on the third with the reason.\n\nAlso, in callBackend, whether a plugin is gone or merely unavailable is now\nread from the live registry rather than from the snapshot the request arrived\nwith. Disable removes before it drains precisely so a caller gets 404, and\nanswering 503 tells them to retry something that is not coming back until an\noperator enables it.\n\nStated plainly: that last change was found while investigating one\nintermittent failure of TestDisableUnderLoad, and it did not reproduce. Two\nattempts at a deterministic reproduction both came out 404, and a full\nre-run passed. The flaw is real on its own terms — deciding \"gone\" from a\nstale snapshot after having just consulted the live one — but I am not\nclaiming it explains that failure.","tree":{"sha":"125ef70972fa13ef35e5ccff48c42eaebed72048","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/125ef70972fa13ef35e5ccff48c42eaebed72048"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGExMjY1YzA2MTk3OGU3NTRkYTM4NTEzNGVlNTNkODU0Njg4MjZkZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06","sha":"a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06"}],"sha":"a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a1265c061978e754da385134ee53d85468826dd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T06:21:11Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T06:21:11Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: stop leaking plugin processes, and cover a cancelled upgrade\n\nChasing something else turned up 5192 plugin processes on the development\nmachine, all from this session''s test runs, each holding the ~19MB a plugin\ncosts.\n\nNot a defect in Core. Manager.Close says plainly that draining is the caller''s\njob, via the registry, so that shutdown ordering stays explicit — and main.go\ncalls registry.DrainAll for exactly that. Eleven test sites created a Manager\nand none of them drained: `grep -c DrainAll` across the test files was zero.\n\nWhy nobody noticed is the part worth keeping. Pdeathsig is Linux-only, so on\ndarwin a child outlives the test binary; and every one of these tests runs in\nDevMode, which skips Pdeathsig even on Linux. Nothing failed as a result. It\ndoes not look like an error, it looks like a slower machine.\n\nFixed by honouring the documented contract rather than changing it — a\ndeliberate design decision should not be overturned because its callers got it\nwrong. drainOnCleanup closes the supervisor first, then drains, because a\nsupervisor still running relaunches what is being drained. Measured after: 0\nresidual processes against ~170 per run before.\n\nAlso adds TestACancelledUpgradeLeavesNothingBehind, which is where this\nstarted. An admin closing a tab cancels the operation — the handler passes the\nrequest context in deliberately — and three separate mechanisms make that safe\nwithout ever having been checked together: Launch kills the child on any error\npath, launchAll kills whatever it had already started, and the commit runs on\na WithoutCancel context so a swap cannot be torn in half. All three turned out\ncorrect; the test pins the property they add up to.\n\nTwo of my own mistakes are recorded in tests/README.md because they are the\nkind that repeat. The first detector counted four lines and I read that as\n\"the process exists\" — all four were the detector''s own command line. And a\nguess I had written down, that the stray processes explained the suite growing\nfrom 160s to 224s, is contradicted by the measurement: 213s with none of them\nleft. The suite is slower because this session added slow tests.","tree":{"sha":"ad4b043968648892e432f3a56ccf396911bb1435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ad4b043968648892e432f3a56ccf396911bb1435"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGE4ZWMxMjYyMTA2NmFjMGI0YTY5Y2RiOTIxMTcyOTZkZTdmYTNlMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682","sha":"6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682"}],"sha":"a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a8ec12621066ac0b4a69cdb92117296de7fa3e06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:58:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:58:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: pin the secret placeholder round trip and the config replace semantics\n\nThe console never receives a secret''s value, only a mask, so an operator\nediting any other field sends the mask back — and the handler has to read that\nas \"leave this one alone\". A comment says so; nothing checked it. Reverting the\nrule stores •••••••• over the credential, and nothing anywhere reports it: the\nrunning plugin keeps the value it was launched with and only fails at its next\nrestart, authenticating upstream with bullet points. That distance between\ncause and symptom is what makes it worth a test rather than a comment.\n\nThe implementation was right on all five counts — masked on the way out, an\nunset secret left unmasked so nobody sees a filled box over an empty setting,\nthe mask kept, a real new value still able to replace it, and the mask not\nspecial for a field that is not declared secret. Not every untested invariant\nis broken, but there is no way to know which until it is checked.\n\nThe sixth records a contract that existed only in the code: saving replaces\nthe whole set rather than merging, so a setting absent from the request is\ndropped. Correct for the console, which posts the entire form, and a trap for\nanything else — the endpoint takes POST and reads like something a script\ncould patch one field with, which would silently clear the rest. Documented\nrather than changed: full replacement is the honest reading of PUT, and\nmerging would make removing a setting impossible.","tree":{"sha":"ee49fb4665d3d681f4b2217494eb23d8c7fc7ab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ee49fb4665d3d681f4b2217494eb23d8c7fc7ab6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZmNjM0MDIyMDRiNTM4Njk4M2E5ZWM2ODY4OGJhZWY0ZTk3NjY2ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b","sha":"bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b"}],"sha":"6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6f63402204b5386983a9ec68688baef4e9766682"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:42:33Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:42:33Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: dead letters an operator can see and put back\n\nThe console showed a count — \"已放弃 4 条\" — and that was all of it. A count is\nnot something anyone can act on: it says four things were lost without saying\nwhich, why, or whether they mattered. Everything needed is already in the\nqueue table, just not reachable.\n\nThis is not hypothetical. Working out why four of six messages died in\ntests/contention_test.go last session meant querying PostgreSQL by hand, which\nis what an operator would have to do and may not be able to.\n\n  GET  /api/system/plugins/<key>/dead        id, topic, payload, attempts,\n                                             last_error, when it failed\n  POST /api/system/plugins/<key>/dead/<id>/retry\n\nThree decisions worth their reasons. A retry resets the attempt counter,\nbecause somebody is retrying it precisely on the judgement that the cause is\ngone — handing it back with its budget already spent means it dies again on\nthe first hiccup, and from outside that is indistinguishable from the retry\nhaving done nothing. An empty list is [] rather than null, so a console does\nnot have to tell apart two cases that mean the same thing. And without a\ndatabase the endpoint says so rather than answering with an empty list, which\nwould read as \"nothing has failed\" — a different and far more comforting\nclaim.\n\nBoth are admin-only, like the rest of this handler: a dead letter carries the\nplugin''s own payload.\n\nCovered at both layers, because the data layer having Dead and RetryDead is\nhalf of it and nothing reaches them unless the handler routes there and\nmain.go passes the store in — a capability complete on both ends with nothing\njoining them being the shape that keeps turning up here. plugins_handler.go\nhad no handler-level tests at all; this adds them for the two new routes and\nleaves a skeleton the others can use.","tree":{"sha":"7fd91cac5c507c96f18b51dced76ab77d7579a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7fd91cac5c507c96f18b51dced76ab77d7579a5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGJkZDZkY2I0M2Y0YmVkYjk1MTE2NGYwOTE1MjdkYWQxMmE0Mzg0OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88","sha":"0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88"}],"sha":"bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bdd6dcb43f4bedb951164f091527dad12a43849b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:32:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:32:23Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: let a plugin set its queue''s visibility timeout\n\nAn upgrade is polite — the handler is told to stop and the SDK reports the\nmessage on the way out, so the new version picks it up in the same second. A\ncrash is not, and that half had never been measured. There is no shutdown, so\nnothing nacks, and the message stays claimed until its lease lapses.\n\nSo the crash-recovery latency of a topic is its visibility timeout, and the\nSDK never sent one: it was always Core''s thirty-second default. Measured with\nmaintenance sampling 150 times faster than production, recovery still took\n34 seconds, because the lease is the floor and the sweep only notices it.\n\nWithVisibilityTimeout makes it the plugin''s decision, which is where the\nknowledge is. Both directions hurt: shorter recovers faster but must still\nexceed the longest a handler can run, or a message is redelivered while\nsomebody is still working on it; longer never misfires but strands the work\nfor that long after a crash.\n\nAnd it is not always shorter. syncer asks for 35s, above the default, because\nits handler can wait ten seconds for a contended account before doing the sync\n— under the default, its own messages would have been redelivered mid-flight.\n\nThat exposed a coupling worth writing down, and it is why busyHoldWait dropped\nfrom 30s to 10s here: how long the handler waits on a contended lock sets the\nfloor for the visibility timeout, which sets the crash-recovery latency.\nWaiting longer smooths contention and pays for it in how long a dead replica\nstalls the queue. They cannot both be small, and the chain runs through three\nlayers that each look fine alone.\n\nThe crash test skips under -short: what it measures is a lease lapsing, and a\nlease short enough to be quick would not be the one the example ships with.","tree":{"sha":"38d6534a74c4958e5bab9e6cef912dc88112291e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/38d6534a74c4958e5bab9e6cef912dc88112291e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDA1MjlhNTNmM2M2ZDg1OTkwMzM5NmMxOTdjYWVkZmQzNTgyZDdlODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea","sha":"16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea"}],"sha":"0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/0529a53f3c6d859903396c197caedfd3582d7e88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:18:15Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:18:15Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: contended work survives a full queue too\n\nLast commit taught the syncer example to put contended work back rather than\nfail it, because the queue counts an attempt when a message is claimed and a\nmessage bounced between replicas is dead-lettered having never failed.\n\nPutting it back is an enqueue, and Core refuses those once a plugin''s backlog\nreaches its limit — one shared table, so a pile-up is everyone''s. So the safe\npath turned back into the unsafe one exactly under pressure: measured with a\nlimit of three, four of six messages dead, the same symptom as before the fix.\n\nAdding to a backlog that is already over its limit is the wrong move anyway,\nand the message is already in the queue. So when there is nowhere to put it,\nthe handler now waits for the lock instead. Blocking there costs neither a\nretry nor a slot in the backlog, and it is the backpressure a full queue is\nasking for. Under the limit the example now does strictly less queue work than\nwithout it: {Done:6 Dead:0} and no requeues at all, against 21 deliveries for\nthe same six units of work when the backlog is unbounded.\n\nAlso records what the backlog limit is and is not. checkDepth reads a depth\nthat maintenance samples on a timer, 30 seconds in Core, so a burst arriving\ninside one interval is measured against a backlog that was empty when it was\nlast looked at: with a limit of three and minute-long sampling, all twenty\nenqueues were accepted. That is the price of making the check cheap and it\nguards a sustained pile-up rather than a rate — but \"the queue is capped at N\"\nreads like a guarantee, so the number is written down rather than left to be\ndiscovered.","tree":{"sha":"baed7501accb82db6a0c6aab0371df4d54f32ff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/baed7501accb82db6a0c6aab0371df4d54f32ff2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDE2NzA4Zjc5M2VlYWI0MWJhNWNkOWRlZGJiZmM0MGM2MDlmMTUyZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e","sha":"5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e"}],"sha":"16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/16708f793eeab41ba5cd9dedbbfc40c609f152ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:09:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:09:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: report a message''s outcome on a context the drain has not cancelled\n\nAn upgrade lands while a consumer is halfway through a message. At-least-once\nsays the message comes back; nobody had measured when.\n\nIt did not come back at all until maintenance reaped it — up to a minute with\nCore''s defaults — and the reason is two lines in the SDK. The handler is told\nto stop by cancelling its context, and the Nack that reports this was sent on\nthat same context, so the call failed at exactly the moment it mattered and\nits error was discarded. Ack had it too: a handler finishing as the drain\narrives could not say so, and the work was repeated. Both now report on a\ncontext the cancellation does not reach, with a bounded budget of their own.\n\nThat alone left a race rather than a fix. Core drains by calling Shutdown and\nthen killing the process once its in-flight count reaches zero — and that\ncount is HTTP requests, so a queue consumer is not in it. The plugin''s\nShutdown returned as soon as it had cancelled, leaving the consumer racing\ntermination to get its report out: it won on an idle machine and lost under\nthe full suite, which is how this surfaced. Shutdown now waits for the\nbackground goroutine to actually return, bounded by the drain deadline Core\nsends — a field Core had been sending that nothing read.\n\nMeasured after: a 2s job interrupted at 1s is redelivered to the new version\nin the same second, attempt 2, finishing 3.09s after it was queued.\n\nSeparately, the syncer example was teaching a pattern that discards work.\nReturning an error when another replica holds the account is the obvious\nthing, and the queue counts an attempt when a message is *claimed* rather than\nwhen it fails — so a message bounced between contending replicas burns its\nfive attempts and is dead-lettered having never failed once. Measured: six\nmessages for one hot account, four dead within three seconds, each recorded as\n\"account is being synced by another replica\", which reads as a diagnosis of\nthe work rather than the accounting artefact it is. It now acknowledges the\ndelivery and republishes with a delay, carrying its own requeue count so that\ngenuinely stuck work still surfaces. Same test after: nothing dead, all six\nunits of work done.\n\nNeither of these is visible from reading the code. Both needed the example to\nactually run.","tree":{"sha":"89b7b561895fd403ccaf02366fcb47e54caa2c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/89b7b561895fd403ccaf02366fcb47e54caa2c5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDVmNWI0N2RlMjIyZmU5NGU0ODYzMDZjNjA1ZGJlODNkMmFjYWIyMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5","sha":"f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5"}],"sha":"5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5f5b47de222fe94e486306c605dbe83d2acab20e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:44:37Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:44:37Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: prefetch bounds unacknowledged work, so replicas share a queue\n\nWriting an example disproved its own premise, which is the argument for\nwriting examples.\n\nsyncer demonstrates the lock — the one host capability with no example and no\nend-to-end test — and rests on two replicas consuming one queue. They did not.\nAdding a replica bought nothing, measured: 1 replica 2.04s, 2 replicas 2.03s,\nwith one process taking every message and its sibling idle.\n\nThe consume loop claimed, streamed and looped without waiting for an\nacknowledgement, so prefetch bounded the size of one claim batch and not the\nwork in hand — a single consumer took the whole backlog in milliseconds. The\nquieter half is that a claimed message is already out of every other\nconsumer''s reach with its visibility clock running, so a long enough queue\nredelivers work nobody has started, which reads as a plugin that is not\nidempotent.\n\nTwo wrong turns worth recording, both of which looked like the bug they were\nmeant to fix. Gating inside the deliver callback is one message too late,\nbecause the claim has already happened. Reserving before the claim leaks: a\npoll that finds nothing never delivers and never gets acknowledged, so the\nreservation is never returned and that consumer blocks for good — which is\nexactly what starved replica 0 the second time. It now waits without\nreserving, and counts on delivery.\n\nAfter: 1 replica 2.05s, 2 replicas 1.11s, with each replica taking one job.\n\nAlso in the SDK, both found by writing against it rather than reading it:\n\n  - OnReady, because background work had nowhere to live. sdk.Queue is nil in\n    main() — the clients arrive after Serve — and OnConfigChanged fires again\n    on every later change, so starting a consumer there leaves one running per\n    edit. Which is why none of the six existing examples consume a queue.\n  - InstanceID, because with only the key two replicas'' logs are\n    indistinguishable, and \"did both replicas pick up work\" cannot be answered\n    from them. It is what settled this bug.\n\nThe regression tests assert rather than log: removing the gate makes\nTestPrefetchBoundsUnacknowledgedMessages report four messages claimed at once\nagainst a prefetch of one. They compare differences rather than absolutes,\nbecause both runs carry the consumer''s poll interval and a half-second margin\nagainst a half-second poll is the shape of a test that is green alone and red\nunder the suite.\n\nOne of my own diagnostics lied on the way: it printed \"both processing after\n0s\" where 0 meant never observed, not observed immediately.","tree":{"sha":"d2a6e987ac80ab9ca611e18b65aedd9fd977e020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/d2a6e987ac80ab9ca611e18b65aedd9fd977e020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGY4ZTQxOWMwYzRjNjA1ZWJiM2I5YWM0ZTdhNmRkMTllMzAzNTg2YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205","sha":"6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205"}],"sha":"f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8e419c0c4c605ebb3b9ac4e7a6dd19e303586b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:13:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:13:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: A/B the hot path after four changes to it, and what the measurement caught\n\nThis session changed the request path four times — re-resolving an instance\nacross an upgrade, resolving filter targets against the live registry,\ndeferring logPhase, and capturing responses on demand — and never re-measured\nit. \"One extra atomic load and an open-coded defer against a 250µs RPC\" is a\nprediction, not a number, and predicting is what this session has spent its\ntime catching other people doing.\n\nMeasured against the pre-change commit in a worktree, same machine, same\nbenchtime: time is inside the noise at every filter depth.\n\nAllocations were not. Every depth was exactly 21 higher — 305→326, 434→455,\n684→705, 934→955 — which is far too regular to be noise, and looks precisely\nlike a regression in Core.\n\nIt was the instrument. The two response headers I added to the test fixture\nfor the header-mutation test are deserialised on Core''s side of every request.\nRemoving them puts the count back at exactly 305 and 20.7KB, so Core''s own\npath allocates the same after four changes as before.\n\ntests/README.md records it, because changing the measuring device and changing\nthe thing measured produce identical-looking numbers, and a worktree baseline\ncarries the old fixture — which is what made the difference visible at all.","tree":{"sha":"f83c7af482cd0755c91c78e2181cd9ec996ab156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/f83c7af482cd0755c91c78e2181cd9ec996ab156"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZiOTA2ZjZhOTM5OTU1YmZkZmRmNWUyYTE3YWJkN2I5NDQyOGEyMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b","sha":"475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b"}],"sha":"6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6b906f6a939955bfdfdf5e2a17abd7b94428a205"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:10:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T04:10:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: reach the metric kinds Core already had, and cover the rest of the SDK surface\n\nScanning the SDK for exported calls with no test, example or fixture behind\nthem found 10 of 83. This closes them to one, and they were not all the same\nkind of thing.\n\nTwo were a capability that stopped at the SDK. Core has switched on\nMETRIC_GAUGE and METRIC_HISTOGRAM from the start, and Logger.Metric hardcoded\nMETRIC_COUNTER, so two of Core''s three branches could not be reached by any\nplugin written against this package — somebody reporting a queue depth had to\nsend it as a counter and hope the reader knew better. Gauge and Histogram are\nnow siblings of Metric.\n\nOne was a stale comment in the worst possible place. PutIfVersion still told\nauthors a version conflict arrives as FailedPrecondition. It has not since\nconflicts moved to Aborted so they could be told apart from an expired\ntransaction — and FailedPrecondition now means exactly that expired\ntransaction, where retrying is the one thing that cannot work. Anyone\nfollowing the comment would write the opposite handling. errors.go''s own\ncomment quotes that sentence as the thing it was fixing, so the correction and\nthe stale copy have been sitting in the same repository; the stale one is the\none an author reads first, because it is on the method.\n\nThe rest were untested and correct: the four header mutations all work end to\nend, checked against the side that can confirm each — a request header only\nthe backend reports on, a response header only the client receives — with a\ncontrol run proving the assertions are about a difference. Avg maps to AGG_AVG\nlike its three tested siblings.\n\nAnd the sentinel errors, which the shipped inventory example''s retry loop\nbranches on, had nothing testing them. A wrong mapping there does not look\nlike a bug: the retry never fires and the symptom is lost writes under\ncontention. Covered now, including that an unmapped code keeps its own error\nrather than being guessed into a sentinel, and that unwrapping still reaches\nthe status Core sent — errors.Is goes through the Is method and would pass\nwith Unwrap broken, which is how a wrapper loses what is underneath it.","tree":{"sha":"130a9dc1083cf0cf75d789671e70edf4a78c3b5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/130a9dc1083cf0cf75d789671e70edf4a78c3b5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQ3NWVjN2E4NWZhYTc0ZjRjNmU1NjI2Njg4ZmNiYmE3YzdhYmVlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2","sha":"5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2"}],"sha":"475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/475ec7a85faa74f4c6e5626688fcbba7c7abee7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:58:18Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:58:18Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: capture a response when a filter asked for one, not when post_handler exists\n\nFilters are global — the handler wraps the whole gateway so a rate limiter or\na WAF sees Core''s own routes too — and the log phase does run for them. But\nwhether the response was captured on the way out followed \"is there a\npost_handler filter\", which is a different question from \"did anyone ask for\nthe response body\". A log filter declaring needs_response_body was handed one\non plugin routes and an empty one on Core''s, so an audit plugin was blind\nexactly over the users, files and plugin-management APIs. Measured: resp=0\nbefore, resp=52 after.\n\nChain gains NeedsResponseBody alongside NeedsRequestBody, and the recorder\nfollows it.\n\nAlso pins what post_handler does on those routes, which is nothing, as a\ncontract rather than a gap. Core''s own routes are written through as they are\nproduced — deliberately, because wrapping a ResponseWriter hides http.Flusher\nand buffering would stall every streaming response, the console''s own event\nstream included. By the time post_handler could run the client already has the\nanswer, so running it would let a filter believe it had reshaped something it\nhad not. A plugin backend is different: Core holds the whole response before\nwriting any of it, which is why the phase works there.\n\nThe test waits for the log phase before asserting post_handler''s absence.\nAsserting an absence without waiting for something that does arrive is how the\nlast two false results here happened, in both directions.","tree":{"sha":"1913085a7f4046d0a16a100a3dcc92fef68dec96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/1913085a7f4046d0a16a100a3dcc92fef68dec96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDU4MjZmMjU4NTZlOGE2Y2QxN2E1MjQyYzE0NjI4NThlMDZkMjhjYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582","sha":"bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582"}],"sha":"5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5826f25856e8a6cd17a5242c1462858e06d28cc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:52:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:52:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a rewrite into the plugin namespace now routes there\n\nThe SDK says RewritePath \"changes where the request is routed\", and it only\nhalf did. The plugin key and sub-path are split from rc.Path, which the\nrewrite updates, so rewriting inside the namespace worked. But whether a\nrequest was a plugin route at all was decided once, from the original URL,\nbefore the pre_route phase — the phase whose whole definition is that it runs\nbefore routing. So /legacy/items rewritten to /api/plugins/hello/items had\nalready been handed to the rest of the gateway and answered 404, which is the\nfirst thing anyone would try: a short public URL in front of a plugin''s own\npath, the archetypal ISAPI filter.\n\nMoving the decision is not a line move, because of the body. Filters must see\nit, so it is buffered before they run, and whether to buffer was the same\ndecision. A rewrite arriving after that lands on a request whose body was\nnever read, and handing the backend an empty body would be a quieter failure\nthan the 404 it replaces. It is only unbuffered when nothing wanted it, in\nwhich case r.Body is untouched and can be read then — which is what this does,\nwith TestABodySurvivesARewriteIntoThePluginNamespace pinning it. Removing that\nread makes the backend receive 0 of 37 bytes.\n\nRewriting out of the namespace still answers 404 rather than falling back to\nCore''s own routing, and the guide now says so along with the rest.\n\nRewritePath was one of the ten exported SDK calls with nothing exercising\nthem, which is how this surfaced.","tree":{"sha":"9650df42f5f3cdcc146023f13b0abbd43fadb4e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/9650df42f5f3cdcc146023f13b0abbd43fadb4e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGJkZGFkZGQ2MDhkNDFmMDlkN2NkMzk3MmQzZGI5MGY4MjVjMjI1ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a","sha":"85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a"}],"sha":"bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bddaddd608d41f09d7cd3972d3db90f825c22582"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:46:58Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:46:58Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a positive duration must never reach the wire as zero\n\nSix places in the SDK convert a time.Duration into the whole seconds the wire\ncarries, and every one truncated. Zero is not \"a very short time\" to any of\nthe readers — each treats it as \"use my own default\" or \"no limit at all\" — so\nasking for a small bound selected the unbounded case:\n\n  Cache.Set(k, v, 500ms)        an entry that never expires\n  Lock.Acquire(name, 500ms, …)  the host''s thirty-second default lease\n  Lock.Acquire(…, wait=500ms)   no waiting at all; taken is reported at once\n  DB.Tx(ctx, 500ms, …)          the thirty-second default, holding a pooled\n                                connection for it\n  Files.DownloadURL(…, 500ms)   the five-minute default on a link that was\n                                meant to be short-lived\n  WithDelay(600ms)              deliverable immediately\n\nThey now share one conversion that rounds up. Sub-second precision is not\nexpressible here and that is fine; silently selecting the opposite of what was\nasked is not.\n\nFound by scanning the SDK for exported calls with no test, example or fixture\nbehind them — 10 of 83, including LockClient.Acquire and Lease.Renew, which\nmeans the whole locking capability had never been exercised through the API a\nplugin author uses. The lock backend and its RPC layer have four tests; the\nwrapper in between had none, and the conversion lives in the wrapper.\n\nWorth recording that the lock TTL ran opposite to the guess: truncating looked\nlike it would shorten a lease and break mutual exclusion, and it does not —\nthe host reads zero as its own default and the lease gets *longer*. Reading\nthe consumer beat reasoning about the producer.\n\nThe guard walks every entry point rather than testing the conversion helper.\nThe helper being correct is not the property that matters; a seventh call site\nthat forgets to use it is the failure this has to catch. Reverting the helper\nto truncation fails all five subtests.","tree":{"sha":"52fed3267851b7fc1656d673e2ffb7705f23a8a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/52fed3267851b7fc1656d673e2ffb7705f23a8a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDg1ZDhlZjk0YjRjNjgyZmU4NjA5YmI2ZjZlZTVmNmQxNmQzMzA1MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00","sha":"1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00"}],"sha":"85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/85d8ef94b4c682fe8609bb6f6ee5f6d16d33051a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:37:21Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:37:21Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: WithDelay discarded any delay shorter than a second\n\nThe wire carries whole seconds and the option truncated into them, so\nWithDelay(600*time.Millisecond) published a message that was deliverable\nimmediately, and WithDelay(1500*time.Millisecond) one deliverable half a\nsecond early. Neither reported anything. A delay is a floor — \"not before\" —\nso rounding up is the only direction that keeps it, and that is what it does\nnow.\n\nFound by scanning for exported functions with no reference outside their own\ndeclaration. WithDelay, WithPriority and WithMaxAttempts are the whole\nauthor-facing surface of the queue''s scheduling behaviour and had no test\nanywhere, in Core or the SDK. All four publish options are covered now.\n\nThis also corrects a claim I added to the guide two commits ago. It said a\n600ms delay arrives at 605ms, which is true of db.Queue and was measured\nthere — but the sentence documented sdk.WithDelay, a path that test never\ntouched, and where the same 600ms meant no delay at all. The guide now says\nwhat the SDK does, including that the granularity is seconds.\n\ntests/README.md records the scan and the reason it needs a canary: the first\nversion reported zero findings, because a doc comment naming the function\ncounted as a use. Zero findings and a clean codebase produce identical output,\nso a checker that cannot be shown to detect a known-positive proves nothing.","tree":{"sha":"0bbc938ad80e395aff4bd760f0dedc5bccd667b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/0bbc938ad80e395aff4bd760f0dedc5bccd667b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDFmMjg4ZmZjZGEyYmVjYjc2YTAyNzM5ODRkYmRmNDE5YTA1ZGNiMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd","sha":"8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd"}],"sha":"1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1f288ffcda2becb76a0273984dbdf419a05dcb00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:31:07Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:31:07Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: close the audit blind spot at 413, and refuse a max_body_bytes that does nothing\n\nTwo claims about bodies, both stated in the guide, both partly untrue.\n\nThe log phase runs at every exit from serve() — short-circuited requests,\nfailed authentication, a 5xx backend — which is what \"auditing has no blind\nspot for rejected traffic\" rests on. It was ten calls kept in step by hand and\none exit did not have it: the body is buffered before the pipeline starts, so\nan over-limit body was answered 413 and returned before any phase ran. The one\nrejection a caller can produce at will was the one that left no record, so\nsomebody probing for the limit was invisible in the log meant to show them.\n\nDeferring logPhase makes that structural instead of clerical — an eleventh\nexit gets it without anyone remembering — and the 413 path now records the\nstatus it answered, or the audit entry would carry no outcome at all.\n\nmax_body_bytes is read only where the request body is attached. On a\nresponse-inspecting filter it caps nothing: measured, a filter declaring 1 KiB\nwas handed the whole 64 KiB response. Enforcing it there would be the wrong\nrepair, because \"over the cap skips a fail-open filter\" means a large response\nskips redaction and goes out unredacted — the caller could switch redaction\noff by asking for more rows. So the declaration is refused at validation\ninstead. The shipped redact example carried exactly that dead declaration,\nwith a comment showing its author had costed the number they were setting.\n\nAlso documents what the request-side limit implies and the guide did not: the\nbody size is the caller''s to choose, so a fail-open filter that inspects\nbodies can be taken out of the path by sending one over its declared cap. That\nis fine for an observer and not fine for a filter that is looking for\nsomething, which has to be fail_closed.\n\nTests: audit_blindspot_test.go, body_limit_test.go, response_body_limit_test.go,\neach with the control case that would otherwise let a vacuous pass through.\nTestGuideManifestsValidate runs the guide''s own manifests through Load and\nValidate — nothing did, and the sample would have failed the new rule.\n\nTwo test fixes in passing. waitForPhases(…, 1) returned as soon as any phase\nlanded while the assertion was about PHASE_LOG, which runs asynchronously\nafter the response: passes alone, fails under load, reads as flake. It is the\nmirror of the false green recorded in tests/README.md — there an arranged\nprecondition went unverified, here an awaited outcome went unawaited.","tree":{"sha":"486b7ccb7e1d5adfdad391a04e67c1a9abb2106c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/486b7ccb7e1d5adfdad391a04e67c1a9abb2106c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDhhNzBjZDcwZjUyOWVjNTJiOWYzNjQzMTdiZDFjNTJiMzQ3NWM0ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa","sha":"5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa"}],"sha":"8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/8a70cd70f529ec52b9f364317bd1c52b3475c4dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:12:28Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:12:28Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: resolve filter targets against the live registry, not the request''s snapshot\n\npipeline.Resolver''s own comment says resolution happens per call \"so a hot\nupgrade takes effect immediately: the next filter call lands on the new\nprocess without the chain being rebuilt\". The abstraction was right and the\nwiring defeated it: the gateway passed the snapshot frozen at the start of\nthe request, so every per-call resolution landed on the same stale table.\n\nThe consequence is worse than it looks, because a displaced instance is not\nmerely draining by the time a late phase runs — it is gone. Drain waits for\nthe in-flight count to reach zero, and a request parked before its\npost_handler filter has not admitted anywhere, so it does not count: the\ndrain completes at once and the process is killed. A fail_closed filter then\nrefuses the request, which means declaring a filter fail_closed — what\nauthentication and rate limiting are — silently also meant dropping traffic\nfor the duration of every deploy of that plugin.\n\nTwo intents were in tension and they are separable. The chain must stay\nfrozen, or which filters run could change mid-request. The instance behind a\nkey must be live, or an upgrade cannot take effect. The chain was already a\nseparate argument, so only the Resolver had to change.\n\nTestFailClosedFilterSurvivesItsPluginBeingUpgraded parks a request in a slow\npre_route filter and upgrades the guarding plugin underneath it: 503 three\ntimes out of three before, 200 after.\n\nAlso records in tests/README.md the false green that nearly hid the first of\nthese: the swap test passed while completing in less time than the filter\ndelay it depended on, so the request never spanned the swap at all. A test\nwhose validity rests on an arranged state has to assert that state — a\nfailed arrangement and a correct system produce the same green.","tree":{"sha":"035674c37df0853cb8ed74f25b974e92813ada50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/035674c37df0853cb8ed74f25b974e92813ada50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDVlM2U2ZmNlNmE4M2JiYTg1ZjNmOTkxNTU3YWM1NjQ2ZmFiMjdjYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775","sha":"925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775"}],"sha":"5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5e3e6fce6a83bba85f3f991557ac5646fab27caa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:07:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:07:17Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: serve requests that span a plugin upgrade, and correct the dedup claim\n\nA request carries the snapshot it loaded on arrival for its whole life, so\ncallBackend resolved its instance from a routing table that an upgrade may\nhave replaced underneath it. The instance it picked is draining by then and\nno longer servable, and the request — already accepted, already through its\nfilters — was answered 404: this plugin does not exist, during a routine\ndeploy.\n\nThe existing comment there anticipated the window and reused the request''s\nown admission to cover it, but that only helps a plugin that ran a filter on\nthis path. A plugin reached by a plain route arrives holding nothing, which\nis the ordinary case. Resolve the instance once more against the live\nregistry when the request''s own snapshot can no longer serve it; the routing\ndecision is unchanged, only the process behind it moved.\n\nThis surfaced as TestE2EHotUpgradeServesContinuously failing once under a\nloaded full-suite run and passing alone every time. Treating that as flake\nwould have required assuming that dropping requests across the swap is\nacceptable, which is the one thing a zero-downtime upgrade promises not to\ndo. TestRequestInFlightAcrossASwapIsNotDropped reproduces it deterministically\nby parking a request in a slow filter while the swap commits — it fails 3/3\nbefore this change and passes 3/3 after.\n\nAlso: a dedup key collapses a burst, it does not make an operation once-ever.\nIt is released as soon as its message is acknowledged, so a later replay of\nthe same scheduled job does produce a second result. The notes example and\nthe plugin guide both claimed the stronger guarantee. Measured alongside:\n20 simultaneous publishes of one key yield 1 accepted, 19 told duplicate and\n0 errors, and a 600ms delayed message arrives at 605ms.","tree":{"sha":"33da637e51177216b5a4c1efb4bbad25a954aacc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/33da637e51177216b5a4c1efb4bbad25a954aacc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDkyNWJjM2Y4YTE4ZmE1OTgzMjAzMWY5ODE4NWRlMGM1YTM5YjE3NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7","sha":"749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7"}],"sha":"925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/925bc3f8a18fa59832031f98185de0c5a39b1775"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:48:07Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:48:07Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: how long a plugin is out after the breaker trips\n\nThe breaker''s own comment calls five seconds \"short enough that a\nrecovered plugin returns to service quickly\" — a claim about wall-clock\nrecovery that had never been checked. There was reason to doubt it:\nclosing needs two consecutive probe successes and one probe is admitted\nper open window, which reads like two windows, ten seconds, twice the\noutage anyone was promised.\n\nMeasured, it is one window. With a 400ms window the filter is called again\n401-404ms after the plugin is healthy, and serves five consecutive\nrequests from there. The second probe does not wait out another window, so\nthe default is about five seconds and the comment is right.\n\nThe first version of the measurement was wrong in a way worth recording.\nIt used Breaker.Open() as the signal for \"recovered\", and that method only\nreports whether the open window has elapsed — it knows nothing about\nwhether any probe succeeded. So it measured \"a 400ms window took 414ms\",\nwhich is trivially true and says nothing about probes. The signal that\ntraffic is back is the plugin being called again, which is what it counts\nnow, several times in a row so that a single probe cannot pass for\nservice.\n\nThe companion test had the same defect: asserting a request still returns\n200 while the breaker is open does not distinguish a breaker that skips\nthe call from one that does not, since both return 200. It now checks that\nno filter call happened at all.\n\nThat is the third time this session the observed quantity was not the one\nthe claim was about — after in-flight counts under closed-loop load, which\ncannot grow by construction, and a reverse-channel measurement that timed\na route the fixture does not have. tests/README.md now carries all three\nin one table, since the correction is the same each time: observe the\nthing that changes when the claim is false, not the thing that happens to\nmove alongside it.","tree":{"sha":"b4b07238216e18abf1e317491f95ef6f62594106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/b4b07238216e18abf1e317491f95ef6f62594106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDc0OWQ3ZGM2OWUwNmFkODgyNGQ5OWI3ZDg0YzBjNmIwZjEzZWRkZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0","sha":"62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0"}],"sha":"749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/749d7dc69e06ad8824d99b7d84c0c6b0f13eddf7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:35:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:35:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: where the cost of a reverse-channel database call goes\n\nThe full-stack table put a plugin''s database call at about 850µs, three\ntimes the plugin call carrying it, and left it at that. An unexplained\nnumber in a performance document is a number somebody optimises the wrong\nthing against, so this takes the same operation at four depths.\n\n  a database operation, no framework          165µs\n  + the host service, in process              indistinguishable from it\n  a plugin call carrying nothing               36µs\n  one reverse-channel database operation      402µs\n\nTwo things fall out. The host service — permission check, wire conversion\n— costs nothing measurable, so \"fewer permission checks\" is not a\ndirection. And the reverse channel costs about 237µs, six times a forward\nplugin call; why is not measured, so the doc records the number without\ninventing a mechanism for it.\n\nFor a plugin author that is the useful ratio: removing an sdk.DB call is\nworth six times removing a plugin call, which is what the apikey example''s\nin-process cache buys and why BatchWrite exists.\n\nThe process is recorded in tests/README.md because it is the more\ntransferable part. Four runs of this measurement printed a plausible table\nwhile measuring something else: a route name that did not exist in the\nfixture, a string replacement I believed had landed and had not, a\nlaunchPlugin whose Deps carry no data backend, and a fixture route needing\na collection the test had not created. Every one produced numbers.\n\nWhat stopped them becoming documentation was making the measurement check\nitself — layer 3 does strictly more work than layer 1 and cannot be\nfaster, so an inversion means the layers are not nested the way the labels\nclaim. It now also probes once and inspects the reply before timing\nanything; any of the four wrong runs would have stopped there.\n\nAlso fixes a flaky test of my own from a few rounds back.\nTestOnErrorFiresWhenTheBackendFails passed alone and failed under the full\nsuite: waitForPhases looped a fixed hundred times with no pause — about\nfour milliseconds — rather than waiting out a deadline, and the log phase\nis asynchronous. A flaky test is worse than none, since it teaches people\nto re-run. The other two loops of that shape in the suite were checked and\nare not waits.","tree":{"sha":"7361169c7bd2d875dc9dc63610b04d4182d89b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7361169c7bd2d875dc9dc63610b04d4182d89b01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDYyY2EwNGM0N2U2MWEwMzZhNzE1Nzc2Yjk2OTlkY2RkMzQ2Mjc1YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f","sha":"1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f"}],"sha":"62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/62ca04c47e61a036a715776b9699dcdd346275b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:17:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:17:04Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: what a realistic installation costs\n\nTwo numbers existed in isolation and neither answered the question an\noperator has. A filter costs about 48µs, measured one at a time against a\nfixture that does nothing. A plugin process costs about 19MB, measured\nwith twenty copies of one binary — and that measurement''s own caveat was\nthat real deployments run different binaries with no shared text, so the\nfigure should hold and had never been checked.\n\nSix shipped examples in one Core, five of them with filters on the request\npath:\n\n  memory   6 different binaries, 109.6 MB, 18.3 MB each\n\nThat settles the caveat: the per-plugin figure holds when the binaries\ndiffer, so it can be used for sizing.\n\n  a path no plugin owns, matching filters only   p50 124µs   p99 360µs\n  a plugin call using no host capability         p50 374µs   p99 1.46ms\n  + a Count through the reverse channel          p50 1.23ms  p99 2.07ms\n  + a listing query through the reverse channel  p50 1.49ms  p99 2.70ms\n\nWhich decomposes into three numbers worth having: the framework itself\ncosts 124µs, a plugin call adds about 250µs, and a database operation\nthrough the reverse channel adds about 850µs — three times the plugin call\nit rides on, and the reason the apikey example caches in-process.\n\nThe third row was first written down here as \"no database work\". notes''\nstats route runs a Count. A mislabelled row is how a measurement becomes a\nwrong conclusion — \"notes is slow\" instead of \"a reverse-channel database\nround trip costs a millisecond\" — so every row is now labelled with what\nit actually does, and the correction is recorded next to it.\n\nAlso a floor that runs by default, like the one-plugin start-up check:\n365µs per request with all six installed, failing above 20ms, so a\ncomposed path that becomes milliseconds is noticed without anyone\nremembering to run the measurement.","tree":{"sha":"1b4fc034f5a138a5c3c4312c3dd6655c402dd75c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/1b4fc034f5a138a5c3c4312c3dd6655c402dd75c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDE4NDBhYTgxNDM5YjVlN2UyYjM3NmRkYjJiOGQ3NmVjMWY1YTNiOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81","sha":"4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81"}],"sha":"1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/1840aa81439b5e7e2b376ddb2b8d76ec1f5a3b8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:09:11Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:09:11Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: all six examples in one Core, and an identity that crosses three\n\nUntil now the largest composition tested was three plugins, and every\ninteresting interaction was pairwise: an identity reaching one other\nplugin, a rate limiter governing one other plugin. The claim worth\nchecking at six is transitive.\n\napikey resolves a key in the authenticate phase; notes serves the request;\naudit reads sdk.User(ctx) in the log phase and writes it to its own table.\nThree separate processes, one request, and the client never says who it is\nbeyond presenting a key. The identity arrives.\n\nThe negative case is what makes that mean anything, and it carries a\nforged X-User-Id: the same request without a key is audited as anonymous.\nIf audit recorded a constant, or believed a client header, the positive\ntest would pass against a system where no identity travelled at all.\n\nRecorded on the way: the apikey plugin cannot bootstrap itself. Minting\nneeds an admin, and on a Core with session authentication that admin is a\nperson with a session — so the first key is issued from the console, by\nhand, once. That is the trust chain rather than a gap: a plugin that could\nmint its own first credential could be made to mint one for anybody who\nreached it. The cost is one out-of-band step at deployment, now in the\nexample''s README, and the composed test provisions its key the same way.\n\nstackOfThree is now a thin wrapper over a stackOf that takes a list. The\neight existing composition tests are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"704384e275def554ffd63eddee35969cf8444969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/704384e275def554ffd63eddee35969cf8444969"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQzMDFmZTU5MTM5ZDcwMTRkY2ViYTI1MmQ3ZmE0M2Y0Yzg1ZjRlODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b","sha":"88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b"}],"sha":"4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4301fe59139d7014dceba252d7fa43f4c85f4e81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:00:03Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T02:00:03Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: redact example — the plugin that rewrites what others said\n\nThe sixth shape, and the last of the phases with no example: post_handler,\nwhere a plugin sees what the system is about to say and gets to change it.\nThe other five decide whether a request proceeds, watch it go by, or serve\nsomething of their own.\n\nIt removes configured fields from other plugins'' JSON responses, at any\ndepth, and demonstrates the mechanism documented last round — a short\ncircuit in post_handler replaces the response rather than preventing it,\nbecause by then there is nothing left to prevent.\n\nTwo traps, both now in the example and the guide:\n\nA replacement carries only its own headers. Core writes the short\ncircuit''s and drops the backend''s, so the obvious implementation strips\nContent-Type from every response it touches, and the symptom — a browser\nrendering JSON as text — points nowhere near the filter. Pinned by a test\nfirst, then handled by the example.\n\nReturning Stop when nothing changed is neither free nor harmless: it pays\nthat header copy and re-encodes JSON, reordering keys and dropping\nformatting on traffic that needed none of it. A test asserts an\nunconfigured response comes back byte for byte.\n\nThe manifest declares no permissions at all, which is worth noticing: this\nplugin sees every response body in the system and cannot store one, send\none anywhere or write one to disk. Reviewing it means reading what it\nlogs, not what it might exfiltrate — it has no way to.\n\nAnd the filter is scoped to two route prefixes rather than /**, on the\nmeasured grounds that needs_response_body copies every body across the\nprocess boundary twice: 16KB doubles an RPC and 256KB costs 944µs.\n\nThe test''s own first run is recorded in its comments, because the way it\nfailed is instructive: redaction did nothing, and the \"nothing configured\"\ncase passed. I had set Deps.Config but not LaunchSpec.Config —\nOnConfigChanged is fed by the latter — so the plugin ran as if\nunconfigured, which is indistinguishable from configured-with-nothing.\nCore feeds both from one place so they cannot disagree; a test that\nlaunches directly has to set both.","tree":{"sha":"32b5b9d8db199de124a17064a6ea13a4fd5de0d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/32b5b9d8db199de124a17064a6ea13a4fd5de0d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDg4ZWQ1ZjE3NzkyMTczODZiMWJmYzVkODQ5YzNkN2FhNTEwYzYzNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408","sha":"933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408"}],"sha":"88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/88ed5f1779217386b1bfc5d849c3d7aa510c635b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:46:54Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:46:54Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: how a filter actually rewrites a response body\n\nThe guide told authors that a filter wanting to \"rewrite or inspect the\nresponse body\" must declare needs_response_body. Inspecting is right.\nRewriting is not reachable the way that sentence implies: RequestMutation\ncarries request headers, response headers, the path, the identity and\ncontext values, and nothing for the body. An author reading the mutation\nAPI concludes it cannot be done.\n\nIt can, through a mechanism the guide never names. In post_handler the\nbackend has already answered, so there is nothing left to reject — a short\ncircuit there replaces the answer instead of preventing it. The same\nStop() means \"refuse this request\" in pre_route and \"replace this\nresponse\" in post_handler, and the phase is what decides which.\n\nFound by starting to write a sixth example — a cross-cutting redaction\nfilter — and discovering the API appeared to make it impossible. The\nexample is worth having and comes next; the mechanism it depends on is\nworth documenting first.\n\nThree tests, and two of them failed for reasons that were mine rather than\nCore''s, which is recorded because the fixture''s shape misleads: /deny is\nmatched exactly, so it only ever fires in the phase where the path is the\nfull one, and /items returns an empty body by design, so \"the body\nsurvived\" cannot be asserted against it. The fixture now suffix-matches\n/refuse the way it already did /slow-filter, and the assertions use a\nroute that returns real bytes.","tree":{"sha":"7d62e2f074b48a23f680646e7fd82bc6f95f4a15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/7d62e2f074b48a23f680646e7fd82bc6f95f4a15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDkzMzMxMmY5MjEwOTkxOTQ3OTllZTA5YTdiZmQ4OTY1Zjk4ZDk0MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847","sha":"6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847"}],"sha":"933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933312f921099194799ee09a7bfd8965f98d9408"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:36:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:36:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: what Core does while a plugin is slow, in both load shapes\n\nA backend call is bounded at 30 seconds, and nothing bounds how many may\nbe outstanding to one plugin at once — BeginRequest counts but does not\ncap, unlike the transaction ceiling beside it. So in-flight is arrival\nrate times latency, and each one holds a goroutine in Core, a gRPC call\nand a goroutine in the plugin. Whether that matters had never been asked.\n\nClosed-loop first: 200 concurrent callers against a plugin sleeping 150ms\nper request, twelve seconds.\n\n  at    in-flight  goroutines  heap      done/s\n  2s    200        1024        9.6 MB    1197\n  6s    200        1030        10.0 MB   1263\n  10s   200        1030        9.9 MB    1276\n\nFlat throughout, zero failures. But that result proves less than it looks:\neach caller waits for its response before sending the next, so in-flight\nis the number of callers by construction and cannot grow however slow the\nplugin gets. Writing this up as \"Core is fine under a slow plugin\" would\nhave been true of the measurement and false of the claim.\n\nSo the open-loop case is measured separately, since it is the one that\nhurts: 150 simultaneous arrivals at a plugin that never answers give an\nin-flight count of 150, all released once the timeout abandons them. The\narithmetic is then plain, and it belongs in the deployment guide —\n30 seconds at 1000 req/s means thirty thousand outstanding calls before\nthe first is given up on. That default is development tolerance, not\nproduction protection, and the guide now says to set BackendTimeout to\nwhat a healthy plugin''s worst response actually costs.\n\nThe release is asserted too: a slot that was never given back would make a\nplugin undrainable after a single hang.","tree":{"sha":"79a354a8d04514c68e17426d308536d5dab75d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/79a354a8d04514c68e17426d308536d5dab75d7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZjOGIxOGNhNmMxYWI5M2EzYjUzYjZhNDRmMTA5ZGM4YWEyMGM4NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d","sha":"6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d"}],"sha":"6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6c8b18ca6c1ab93a3b53b6a44f109dc8aa20c847"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:27:22Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:27:22Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: measure what one slow plugin costs everybody else\n\nIsolation is why this architecture pays for a process per plugin, and it\nwas only ever tested against crashes. Slowness is the harder case and the\nmore common one — a plugin does not usually die, it starts taking longer\nthan anyone budgeted — and a filter subscribed to /** sits on the critical\npath of every request in the system, including requests belonging to\nplugins that have nothing to do with it.\n\n200 samples against an unrelated plugin''s route:\n\n  no filter                          p50 132µs    p99 204µs\n  fast filter                        p50 176µs    p99 547µs\n  sleeps 50ms,  200ms budget         p50 52.9ms   p99 55.4ms\n  sleeps 200ms, 500ms budget         p50 203ms    p99 205ms\n  sleeps 200ms, 20ms budget          p50 146µs    p99 425µs\n\nThe first four rows say the thing worth saying: a generous budget passes a\nslow plugin''s latency straight through to everyone, one for one. So\ntimeout_ms is not a safety net that only matters when something breaks, it\nis the latency other plugins'' requests will pay, and setting it loosely\nspends someone else''s budget.\n\nZero failures throughout — a fail-open filter timing out is skipped, not\nfatal.\n\nThe last row is smaller than its own budget, which the timeout alone\ncannot explain. My first instinct was to write \"the circuit breaker\nopened\" into the comment, which is exactly how a wrong mechanism becomes\ndocumentation, so it is now a test instead:\nTestABudgetIsPaidUntilTheBreakerOpens. Five of twenty-five requests pay\nthe budget, then it drops to nothing. The hypothesis held and now has a\nnumber attached — a persistently slow plugin costs a handful of requests,\nnot every request.\n\nTwo assertions run by default: a filter far over its budget does not hold\nan unrelated request (2s sleep, 50ms budget, 53ms observed), and one\ninside its budget is still waited for — since a gateway that abandoned\nevery filter immediately would pass the first and make filters useless.","tree":{"sha":"0d7499d1d237b80d78451dc7c066bf59461929b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/0d7499d1d237b80d78451dc7c066bf59461929b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDZlN2JmYWQwZmUyMTRmOTEzNmUzNDVmYTVkMTdlODU3NzM5YTU3NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab","sha":"d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab"}],"sha":"6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/6e7bfad0fe214f9136e345fa5d17e857739a576d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:15:08Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:15:08Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: a lost audit record is announced, not silent\n\nThe audit example''s README said a failing log-phase filter means the\nrequest succeeds and the record \"silently vanishes\". The first half is\nright and is the reason to make the phase fail-open at all. The second is\nwrong, and \"silently\" was carrying the weight of the sentence.\n\nCore reports it, naming both the plugin and the filter:\n\n  auditor/access-log: plugin is not running\n\nThat changes what an operator should do. The holes in the audit trail are\ncountable: alert on filter errors and you know how much is missing and\nwhen. A record with known gaps is far more use than one that looks\ncomplete and is not, and the README was describing the worse of the two.\n\nBoth halves tested, because they are separate claims and only one of them\nhad ever been stated: the request still succeeds with the auditor dead,\nand the failure is reported.\n\nAlso corrected while there: the README''s advice to enqueue from the log\nphase for guaranteed completeness only narrows the window. The enqueue\nruns in the same fail-open filter, so a plugin that is entirely gone\ncannot enqueue either. Real completeness has to live in Core.\n\nFifth documented claim about failure to be contradicted by measuring it.\nLike the stdout rule, this one turned out better than written.","tree":{"sha":"a53d5b1116a372d3503fd71dfa19e146d4dd1e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/a53d5b1116a372d3503fd71dfa19e146d4dd1e7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGQ1YjViMjE3ZTQwNDU5ZDkwNDUxN2U5OWZkNzQ0Y2NlYWVhZTNmYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167","sha":"745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167"}],"sha":"d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d5b5b217e40459d904517e99fd744cceaeae3fab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:05:44Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T01:05:44Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: a long job is cut off by a drain, not waited for\n\nThe notes README said a job holds one of the plugin''s request slots so\ndraining waits for it, \"and a nightly rollup that takes ten minutes makes\nan upgrade during those ten minutes wait\". The first half is right. The\nsecond is not: a drain waits for its timeout and no longer, then\nterminates whatever is still in flight.\n\nMeasured — a 10s job against a 400ms drain:\n\n  drain timed out after 400ms with 1 request(s) in flight\n\nSo a long job does not slow an upgrade down. It gets killed by it. That is\na different kind of warning: the README''s version reads as a performance\nnote, and the real behaviour is a correctness one — a half-finished\nrollup, if it is not idempotent.\n\nBoth directions are tested, since a drain that never waited for anything\nwould produce the same timing: a job does occupy a slot, and a job that\nfinishes inside the budget is waited for (223ms for a 200ms job).\n\nThe consequences now sit in the guide too, not only in one example''s\nREADME: keep the work out of the job handler and put it on the queue,\nwhere at-least-once delivery means a killed attempt comes back — and be\nidempotent regardless, keyed on job.Scheduled.","tree":{"sha":"ea55d188745e3b65d400c089907123e1231878e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ea55d188745e3b65d400c089907123e1231878e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDc0NWQ4YTE1YjZlMzY5MDVhZWM5ZTFjYTJlMDg0ODk5MjAwMTgxNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60","sha":"f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60"}],"sha":"745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/745d8a15b6e36905aec9e1ca2e08489920018167"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:54:53Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:54:53Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: verify the troubleshooting table, row by row\n\nEvery row is a claim of the form \"symptom X means cause Y\", which is the\nkind of assertion this session has repeatedly found to be wrong: all three\nof CLAUDE.md''s headline rules described their own failure modes\nincorrectly. The table had never been checked, and two of its rows\ncontradicted measurements made in this same session — one of them in the\ntable I edited last round, while leaving the other two saying the\nopposite.\n\n  \"plugin fails to start with no information in the log\" — false. The\n  error quotes the plugin''s own stdout back at it, which is now the\n  symptom the row is keyed on.\n\n  \"odd behaviour after an upgrade / you used cp\" — does not happen on\n  Linux. cp is refused with ETXTBSY, so the symptom is a failed\n  deployment, not a misbehaving plugin.\n\nTwo rows that could be settled with a test now are: a package whose\ndirectory name does not match its manifest key, and a manifest that does\nnot validate, both report a specific reason the console can show. That is\nthe difference between fixing it in a minute and hunting for a plugin that\nis silently absent — so there is now also a row saying that a plugin\nmissing *without* a reason is a bug rather than a configuration mistake.\n\nThe one row that cannot be settled here — a reverse proxy buffering\nserver-sent events — is marked as unverified rather than left looking like\nthe others. A table where some rows are measured and some are folklore\nshould say which are which.","tree":{"sha":"bd47f396dca4d5792fdccc8423576ebed8cbe1e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/bd47f396dca4d5792fdccc8423576ebed8cbe1e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGY4YTc1ZTM2NTdiM2QzNWNhZTQ0NjU3MTc2MTQ1YzY1OGE3YWRkNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3","sha":"424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3"}],"sha":"f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f8a75e3657b3d35cae44657176145c658a7add60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:45:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:45:38Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: the third headline rule was wrong too, in the other direction\n\nCLAUDE.md said overwriting a running plugin binary \"corrupts that\nprocess\". On Linux it does not — the kernel refuses. Measured on debian\nwith a genuinely running executable:\n\n  cp: cannot create regular file ''/tmp/prog'': Text file busy\n  sh: cannot create /tmp/prog: Text file busy\n  mv → succeeds, and the running process carries on from the old inode\n\nSo using cp costs you a failed deployment, announced clearly, rather than\na corrupted process. Corruption is what happens where there is no ETXTBSY\n— a macOS development machine — and the stated target here is Linux.\n\nThat completes the set. All three of the rules CLAUDE.md calls the ones\nthat matter most had their failure modes described wrongly, each in a\ndifferent direction: stdout is friendlier than documented (go-plugin\nquotes your own output back), CGO_ENABLED points the wrong way (ENOENT\nfor a file that is plainly there), and this one does not happen at all on\nthe platform being targeted.\n\nEvery one of them would send somebody looking in the wrong place — one by\nexpecting the worst, one by naming a string that never appears, one by\nraising a fear of corruption where the OS already refuses.\n\ntests/README.md carries the table and the reproduction for each. Also\nrecorded there: doing the mv/cp experiment under alpine gives a false\npass, because its /bin/sleep is a busybox symlink and the copy never runs\nas a process at all. That is how the first attempt went.","tree":{"sha":"bd31681483dd18ffef3281963029a7b127edf560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/bd31681483dd18ffef3281963029a7b127edf560"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQyNGYwMGNkYTQzZWI2YWI4YmYyMmY4ZDBlYWRmMDUxNjI4OWEwZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba","sha":"c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba"}],"sha":"424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/424f00cda43eb6ab8bf22f8d0eadf0516289a0d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:40:06Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:40:06Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: the CGO_ENABLED=0 failure is not \"exec format error\"\n\nThree documents told an operator to look for `exec format error` when a\nplugin is dynamically linked. Measured, it is not that, and the real\nmessage is worse than opaque — it points the wrong way.\n\nBuilt with CGO_ENABLED=1 under glibc, run under musl:\n\n  sh: /plugin: not found\n  fork/exec /plugin: no such file or directory\n\nThe file is there and executable. The kernel returns ENOENT because the\n*interpreter* is missing — /lib/ld-linux-*.so — but the error names the\nbinary. Somebody reading it checks the path, the mount and the\npermissions, and the problem is a build flag.\n\n`exec format error` is ENOEXEC and means a wrong architecture, so telling\npeople to look for it guarantees they never find this. CLAUDE.md,\ndocs/plugin-development.md and docs/deployment.md now say what actually\nappears, and carry the one-line check:\n\n  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD:/x\" alpine ldd /x/bin/plugin\n\nNot automated: reproducing it needs Docker and a glibc build, which is\nmore than the check is worth in the suite. tests/README.md carries the\ncommands and the exact output instead.\n\nThis is the second of the three headline rules to have its stated failure\nmode contradicted by measuring it. The first, stdout, was better than\ndocumented; this one is worse.","tree":{"sha":"a2a3ef7291a73ee22b453143ee01fe00f894c768","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/a2a3ef7291a73ee22b453143ee01fe00f894c768"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGM1MTNhYjJmNjE3MTUxOGIxMzdmY2EzYTM1NWI0Mjk2MDI3OWEyYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180","sha":"4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180"}],"sha":"c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c513ab2f6171518b137fca3a355b42960279a2ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:35:41Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:35:41Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: spell out what per-plugin queue isolation rules out\n\nTopics are scoped to the plugin that owns them, which the guide already\nsaid. What it did not say is the consequence: a plugin cannot consume\nmessages another plugin enqueued, so an architecture where one plugin\nhands work to another cannot be built on the queue at all. An agent\nreading only the guide worked that out for itself and said so in its\nreport, having first read the task as though an external queue existed.\n\nThe honest remainder is also stated: cross-plugin delivery goes through\nthe event bus, which is best-effort, so ''across plugins and must not be\nlost'' has no ready answer — the receiver has to enqueue onto its own\nqueue from the event handler, trading one in-memory hop for durability\nafter it.","tree":{"sha":"e22b518aa9af293668ef8c9c0e12c66b68a7344b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e22b518aa9af293668ef8c9c0e12c66b68a7344b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDRmZTcwZDEwMzVhNzM5YWE1NWEzMjhiZGUyZWNjNGNhYThlNmYxODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900","sha":"5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900"}],"sha":"4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4fe70d1035a739aa55a328bde2ecc4caa8e6f180"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:27:25Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:27:25Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: the stdout rule, and what it actually costs to break\n\n\"A plugin must never write to stdout\" is rule one in CLAUDE.md, listed\nunder a heading saying these rules fail in ways that do not point at their\ncause. It had no test, and both halves of that turn out to be wrong.\n\nPrinting before sdk.Serve does stop the plugin starting — the handshake is\nread from the first stdout line and gets replaced. But the failure points\nstraight at it: go-plugin quotes the offending line back.\n\n  plugin noisy: handshake failed: Unrecognized remote plugin message:\n  debugging: about to start\n\nAn author sees their own debug string in the launch error. That is close\nto the best possible outcome, and the guide told them to expect the worst.\n\nPrinting after the handshake is survivable: the fixture prints, then\nserves twenty more requests with no degradation and no exit. So the rule\nis about start-up, not about stdout in general — worth stating, because\n\"never print anything\" reads as \"stop logging\", and the reason to prefer\nstderr is that sdk.Log carries the trace id, not that a Println is fatal.\n\nBoth documents corrected to what was measured. The rule itself is\nunchanged, and CGO_ENABLED=0 keeps the \"does not point at its cause\"\nwarning, which is its own separate claim and still true as far as anything\nhere has established.\n\nA quiet launch is the control, so the two cases above cannot both pass\nagainst a Core that could not start this fixture at all.","tree":{"sha":"826fa6f09eedc461f9efa3c503a7f620695d6e79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/826fa6f09eedc461f9efa3c503a7f620695d6e79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDVmZjJlNjcxMGM4YTRiOGRkNWViMDA5NWQ5MzhjYzIwN2I1NmY5MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758","sha":"b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758"}],"sha":"5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5ff2e6710c8a4b8dd5eb0095d938cc207b56f900"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:22:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:22:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: the message-size ceiling, from both sides of it\n\ngRPC defaults to 4 MiB and go-plugin does not override it, so anything\nbuilt on it inherits that limit unless both ends raise it. This project''s\nplan named it as a trap the team had already lost time to, and set both\nsides to 16 MiB with a value negotiated at Configure.\n\nNothing had ever sent a message big enough to find out whether that took\neffect. A ceiling configured on paper and not in fact looks exactly like a\nworking one until the day something large goes through it — which is the\nsame shape as the other gaps this session has turned up, in a place where\nthe fix was already written.\n\nIt works. Eight megabytes round-trips, so does 16 MiB minus a margin, and\nsix megabytes proves both directions were raised rather than one. Lowering\nDefaultMaxMessageBytes back to gRPC''s 4 MiB fails the first and the last,\nwhich is the check that these tests are measuring the ceiling and not\njust the fixture.\n\nOver the limit the error names both numbers — \"trying to send message\nlarger than max (20971726 vs. 16777216)\" — and that reason survives to the\nHTTP caller rather than being replaced by a bare 502. The plugin process\nlives through it and serves the next request.\n\nOne correction to the plan while writing this: it asked for \"a clear 413\nrather than an opaque ResourceExhausted\", and 413 is the wrong code. It\nmeans the request entity was too large; this is the response, and nothing\nthe caller changes will fix a plugin returning 20MB. 502 with the reason\nintact is what they need, and it is what Core already does.","tree":{"sha":"bcfd3e5607b75013d623be1621a5abc5ecbe1d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/bcfd3e5607b75013d623be1621a5abc5ecbe1d5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGIwZTcwMGI4YzEwOGZjODRhNjk5YzlkNjc3OTc3ODI0ZmIxNWY3NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f","sha":"933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f"}],"sha":"b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/b0e700b8c108fc84a699c9d677977824fb15f758"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:17:34Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:17:34Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: the console live-update chain, as one flow\n\n\"A plugin''s menus appear when it is enabled and disappear when it is\ndisabled, with no page reload\" is requirement four, and every piece of it\nhad a test: the registry fires OnChange with a new snapshot, UIEvents\ndelivers to an open subscriber, the menu tree follows the plugin. What had\nno test is the join — and the join is one line in main.go wiring OnChange\nto Publish.\n\nThat is the shape this codebase has produced a bug in four times now: both\nends complete, nothing checking the middle. It happens to be wired\ncorrectly here, which is worth knowing rather than assuming.\n\nDriven the way an operator creates it: a console is open on the event\nstream, someone enables, disables or upgrades a plugin, and the test\nchecks both that the console was told and that what it fetches afterwards\nhas changed. An event against an unchanged menu is a wasted round trip; a\nchanged menu nobody was told about is a stale page.\n\nThe fourth case is the one that keeps the other three honest: nothing is\npublished when nothing changed. A stream that emitted on a timer would\npass all three positive tests while telling an operator nothing about what\nactually happened — and since the console refetches the whole tree per\nevent, a chatty stream is a chatty console. Both mutations behave: cutting\nthe OnChange wire fails the positives, adding a 100ms heartbeat fails the\nnegative.","tree":{"sha":"fbf64f57617c9981ee975c6514dc1903f20ff603","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/fbf64f57617c9981ee975c6514dc1903f20ff603"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDkzM2IzNjQ3NjkxM2VmNzU5YzAwMjIwOTI4NjQyYTI4M2I1ZmJlMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08","sha":"a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08"}],"sha":"933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933b36476913ef759c00220928642a283b5fbe0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:14:55Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:14:55Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: a filter learns which declaration matched it\n\nThe manifest permits several filters in one phase — only names must be\nunique, nothing forbids two pre_route entries with different path rules —\nand the SDK dispatches by phase, so all of them arrive at one Go function.\nFilterRequest carried no name, so that function could not tell them apart.\nDeriving it from the path duplicates the matching Core just did, and is\nimpossible outright when both declarations match the same path.\n\nFound by an agent allowed to read only the plugin guide — the second\nstructural gap that exercise has turned up. It reported this one as a\nblank it could not fill rather than guessing, which is what makes the\nexercise worth running.\n\nFilterRequest gains filter_name; sdk.FilterRequest gains Name. The test\nuses two declarations that both match the same path, since that is the\ncase no amount of path inspection can disambiguate.\n\nIts other findings, each checked against the source before being written\ndown: routes are relative and Core strips the prefix, while a filter''s\nmatch.paths is the full path; Go 1.22 wildcards and PathValue work because\nit is a real *http.Request; the SDK marshals with encoding/json so\ndocument field names come from json tags; sdk.Cache has Delete; required:\ntrue enforces nothing and only marks the console; OnShutdown runs inside\nthe drain budget, 30s by default.\n\nAnd two pieces of prose it had to argue with. The fail_closed rule was\nwritten as \"any filter making a security decision\", which contradicts the\nguide''s own SetIdentity example. The real line is whether the filter can\nlet a request through: an authorize filter that refuses must fail closed,\nan authenticate filter that only labels callers should not — failing\nclosed there turns a wobble in the authenticator into a site-wide 503,\nwhile failing open merely downgrades a valid caller to anonymous and\nleaves authorize to refuse as it would anyway. The author reasoned that\nout and kept a long comment defending it, which is a sign the doc made\nthem do work it should have done.\n\nThe other was a paragraph written as \"this used to be broken and is now\nfixed\", with no version to anchor it, which left them re-reading three\ntimes to decide whether they were looking at current behaviour or a\npost-mortem. It now states the behaviour.","tree":{"sha":"9880b1cb00b60220163bf0a48c0b394b8b81db51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/9880b1cb00b60220163bf0a48c0b394b8b81db51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGEwYmZkYWIxMDhhOTExNTVjNjhiZmEyYTI2ZjM3MGI3YjhhODhiMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab","sha":"030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab"}],"sha":"a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a0bfdab108a91155c68bfa2a26f370b7b8a88b08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:03:43Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:03:43Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: measure what a plugin process costs\n\nThe premise of this architecture is one operating-system process per\nplugin, and nobody had the number that follows from it. It decides\ndeployment sizing and it decides how long an operator waits after a\nrestart, since every plugin is cold-started with Core.\n\n  plugins   start    per plugin   children   Core heap\n  1         298 ms   20.0 MB      20.0 MB    1.0 MB\n  5         191 ms   19.1 MB      95.7 MB    1.4 MB\n  10        391 ms   18.2 MB      181.9 MB   2.6 MB\n  20        830 ms   18.7 MB      374.7 MB   5.3 MB\n\nAbout 19MB each and flat — the floor is the Go runtime plus gRPC, so an\nempty plugin and a real one differ by the real one''s own data. Twenty\nplugins is roughly 375MB of children.\n\nOne caveat stated in the doc rather than glossed: these twenty processes\nrun the *same* binary, so their text pages are shared and RSS\ndouble-counts them — the true marginal cost here is lower than 19MB. Real\ndeployments run *different* binaries with no such sharing, which is why\n19MB is the honest number for the case that matters.\n\nCore itself grows about 0.26MB per plugin, which is nothing. The cost of\nthis architecture is entirely in the children.\n\nStart-up is linear at 39ms each — asserted, not just observed, since a\nper-plugin cost that grew with the number already running is what a scan\nof the existing set on every launch would look like. Twenty plugins are\nready 0.8s after Core starts, fifty in about two seconds, which is what a\nreadiness probe''s initialDelaySeconds has to accommodate.\n\nA third test runs by default and needs no MEASURE: one plugin becomes\nready inside two seconds. Not a benchmark, a floor — so a change that\nmakes start-up pathological is noticed without anyone remembering to run\nthe measurement.","tree":{"sha":"fdb07cdb9b61cfa37c87a9009534395e160c0d37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/fdb07cdb9b61cfa37c87a9009534395e160c0d37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDAzMGYzYzZiOTg1NGMwOTg5NjAzMGVmYTNmNjI1MjE5YTlkZDc3YWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c","sha":"836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c"}],"sha":"030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/030f3c6b9854c09896030efa3f625219a9dd77ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:58:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:58:32Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: show the struct, not a list of its field names\n\nA second agent, allowed to read only the plugin guide, wrote a plugin\nagainst the version of the guide the first one''s report produced. The\nbefore/after is the point of running it twice:\n\n  SetIdentity''s signature   author 1: compile error   author 2: correct\n  OnShutdown                did not know it existed   used it\n  Consume blocks            guessed, low confidence   correct\n  PutIfVersion in a tx      did not attempt           used\n\nThose four fixes worked. The one failure — three compile errors from a\nsingle cause — was created by last round''s own fix: the guide gained a\nprose list of QueueMessage''s field names, no types, and the next author to\nread it assumed ID was a string. It is an int64.\n\nA field list invites a type guess; a declaration does not. The guide now\nshows the struct, and TestGuideStructsMatchTheSDK holds it to the SDK:\nevery field the guide shows must exist on that type with that type. It\ndoes not demand the guide show every field — showing the interesting half\nis reasonable — only that what it shows is true. Verified by writing\nstring for ID, and by adding a field that does not exist; both fail.","tree":{"sha":"1a6b884392b2783553e30745bfd299a238df602d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/1a6b884392b2783553e30745bfd299a238df602d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDgzNjUzM2ZmNmU5Yzg0MmU3MDIxZjFiMjExZGY4ZjExMDVmM2E2NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6","sha":"585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6"}],"sha":"836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/836533ff6e9c842e7021f1b211df8f1105f3a66c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:53:33Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:53:33Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: make a plugin''s own filters and handlers testable\n\nAn agent given nothing but the plugin guide reported \"no testing story at\nall\". Two parts of that were not gaps in the documentation but gaps in the\nAPI: a plugin author literally could not test the two things this SDK\ntells them to get right.\n\nA filter is an ordinary function, so calling it was never the problem —\nchecking the answer was. Every field of FilterResult is unexported and\nthere were no accessors, so a test could invoke a filter and learn\nnothing. Inspect() returns a FilterDecision with all of it: the action,\nthe status and body of a short circuit, the identity and rewritten path\nand values of a mutation. One method rather than eight accessors, because\nRewritePath is already a setter and the names would collide.\n\nWithUser puts a caller into a context. The guide''s authorization pattern\nis `if !sdk.User(r.Context()).HasRole(\"admin\")`, and an author had no way\nto build a request that satisfies it — so the check most worth testing was\nthe one that could not be. Passing nil is the anonymous case, which is the\none that matters: the accessors are nil-safe precisely because a panic in\na plugin is not a 500, it is the process dying.\n\nBoth are exercised by a test written the way an author would write theirs,\nusing only exported API, so it fails if that surface stops being enough.\nThe guide now shows both.\n\nAlso: TestNoBuildOutputIsTracked, added last round, immediately caught me\ndoing the same thing again — `go build ./extension-example/.docauthor/`\ndropped an 18MB binary at the repository root and the previous commit\ntook it. The ignore list named the packages that exist today, which is the\nwrong shape for a name nobody predicted; it now covers dotted paths at the\nroot, with the tracked ones exempted. The size check remains the real\nbackstop, since it needs nobody to guess a name.","tree":{"sha":"676ea0f9339d6b3fb9d3abb65c3cfceff36423f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/676ea0f9339d6b3fb9d3abb65c3cfceff36423f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDU4NWRlYzVkZGIzY2U5YjA3NjE1MjY5YzJmMDBlMDRiYzQzN2ZhZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda","sha":"581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda"}],"sha":"585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/585dec5ddb3ce9b07615269c2f00e04bc437fae6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:45:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:45:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"docs: close the gaps a doc-only author actually fell into\n\nAn agent allowed to read exactly one file — docs/plugin-development.md,\nno SDK source, no examples, no tests — was asked to write a plugin using\na transaction with contention, configuration with a secret, a queue\nconsumer that handles exhausted retries, and a log-phase filter. It listed\nevery place it had to guess, then the guesses were compiled.\n\nTwelve documented guesses, one compile error. The docs are in much better\nshape than the last time this was done, and the one that broke is the\nworst one to have broken: SetIdentity takes a *sdk.UserContext, and its\nsignature appears nowhere in the guide — for the single most\nsecurity-sensitive call in the framework, in the section that points at an\nexample the author was not allowed to read. Now shown, with roles, and\nwith why they belong there.\n\nIts self-declared highest risk — that TxClient.Get mirrors DB.Get and\nreturns a version — was right, by symmetry rather than by documentation.\nThe transaction example only ever showed Put and Delete, so reading inside\na transaction was a guess. It now shows Get and PutIfVersion.\n\nThe rest, all verified against the SDK before writing:\n\n- Consume blocks, exactly as Subscribe does. Subscribe says so and Consume\n  did not, which is the kind of asymmetry that reads as meaningful.\n- OnShutdown exists in sdk.Config and the guide mentioned it zero times —\n  so a plugin with a Consume goroutine had no documented way to stop it,\n  and an in-flight message waits out its 30s lease instead of returning to\n  the queue immediately.\n- QueueMessage''s fields: only Decode/Attempt/MaxAttempts were shown, so a\n  dead-letter record had nothing to key on. ID, Topic and ParentTraceID\n  now appear.\n- Configure was described as though an author implements it. It is the\n  SDK''s internal handshake and is not in sdk.Config, whose full field list\n  is now stated.\n- \"Do authorization in your handler\" and \"Core 401s before the handler\"\n  were both true and in different sections. The first now says which\n  callers it applies to.\n- Testing a plugin: nothing had ever been written about it. What works is\n  now stated, and so is the gap — there is no reusable harness for the\n  parts that need a live Core.\n\nWith SetIdentity corrected the author''s 23KB plugin compiles and vets\nclean, which is the measurement.","tree":{"sha":"c86800b562d5127cee552d163a366d6c137f486c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/c86800b562d5127cee552d163a366d6c137f486c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDU4MTU2NWUxYTU0NWU1M2Y2YzA2Y2E3MWViNmVhNDA0NDVjNmZlZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200","sha":"bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200"}],"sha":"581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/581565e1a545e53f6c06ca71eb6ea40445c6feda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:37:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:37:26Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: check the plugin guide against the SDK it documents\n\nThe guide is the only thing a third-party author reads — that is the point\nof shipping an SDK separately from Core — so a name in it that does not\nexist costs somebody an afternoon. It has already happened twice while\nwriting the shipped examples: reaching for SortAsc, which is Sort, and for\na WithBody on a short-circuit result, which does not exist.\n\nTwo checks: every sdk.X and every .Method( inside a Go fence resolves to\nsomething the SDK exports, and every top-level manifest key the guide\nshows is one the parser accepts — which matters more now that unknown\nfields are refused rather than ignored, since copying one stops a plugin\nloading.\n\nThe first version only looked at package-level sdk.X names, which would\nhave missed both real errors: SortAsc and WithBody are methods. Widening\nto methods means a name-only comparison — the guide writes q.Sort(...)\nwhere q came from somewhere earlier — so a standard-library allow-list is\ncarried explicitly rather than inferred.\n\nVerified by aiming a mutation properly: renaming .Where( or .Publish(\ninside a fence fails it, and doing the same to a name in prose does not,\nwhich is correct. There are no unlabelled Go fences for it to miss.\n\nArity, argument order and semantics are still out of reach. Compiling the\nfive examples is what covers those.","tree":{"sha":"78c9d7c4d72b8b5f19001a0e6e5b7d011d942155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/78c9d7c4d72b8b5f19001a0e6e5b7d011d942155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGJkODdjODFiMDM3ZDAyNTExYWVjYzRiMmMxYTRlYWJiYWRlZGYyMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110","sha":"4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110"}],"sha":"bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/bd87c81b037d02511aecc4b2c1a4eabbadedf200"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:25:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:25:36Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"chore: stop committing compiled plugin binaries\n\nFour of them — apikey, audit, echoplugin, inventory, 18MB each and 75MB\ntogether — are tracked in this repository. They arrived over four rounds\nof my own work: `go build ./extension-example/inventory` with no -o writes\n./inventory into the working directory, and `git add -A` takes it from\nthere. Nothing objected. The build was fine, the tests were fine, and git\ndoes not mind what it is handed.\n\nThis removes them and ignores the names `go build` produces, so no more\narrive. It does not recover the space: those blobs are in the pushed\nhistory, and getting them out needs a rewrite and a force push to main.\nThat is a decision for whoever owns the repository, not a cleanup to\nperform quietly — .git is currently 121MB, most of it this.\n\nThe guard is two tests: no tracked file over 2MB, and every name `go build`\nwould produce is ignored. The first one was itself broken when written —\nrun from tests/, `git ls-files` scopes to that directory, so it inspected\ntests/** and passed with an 18MB binary at the repository root, which is\nthe only place they ever land. Rooting the command at .. makes the\nmutation fail as it should.","tree":{"sha":"c24964dc4ce0a9a55f280d244e4c9c7f60d28578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/c24964dc4ce0a9a55f280d244e4c9c7f60d28578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDRhOTI4NDRkYWJiNGQ1YzM2MDQ5OGFhOWI5MzE1YTk4M2M0ODAxMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b","sha":"4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b"}],"sha":"4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4a92844dabb4d5c360498aa9b9315a983c480110"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:14:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:14:45Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: delete the extension management page, which led nowhere\n\nThe console carried a 「扩展管理」 nav item pointing at a 328-line page\nwhose every call went to /api/system/extensions/* — routes Core stopped\nserving in the plugin migration, against tables migration 000008 had\nalready dropped. It sat in the navigation looking like a feature and led\nto a page where every action 404s, offering an approve/reject/secrets\nworkflow that no longer exists in any form.\n\nFound by applying last round''s lesson — mount every page at least once —\nwhich is now a test rather than a habit. pages.test.js mounts each routed\nview; the assertions barely matter, since a render error surfaces as a\nthrown exception whatever else is checked. Demonstrated by putting a\n{{ nonexistent.field }} into Users.vue: vite build passes, the test fails.\n\nThat is the same gap that let the plugin page ship broken for two rounds.\nThe build cannot see it, so something has to render.","tree":{"sha":"e1c864541d874e102a04dba178a67e0dac7aa598","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e1c864541d874e102a04dba178a67e0dac7aa598"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQzNzY1NzNhM2ZkYmM2NzgyMTY3NmJlYThkNDIyMzgzZTA2NmI0M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5","sha":"5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5"}],"sha":"4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/4376573a3fdbc67821676bea8d422383e066b43b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:11:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:11:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: the plugin management page threw on every render\n\nThe config row''s <tr> sat outside the v-for, so `p` did not exist there.\nAny non-empty plugin list threw at render. It shipped two rounds ago with\nthe config form, and `vite build` passed every time since — Vue''s template\ncompiler does not catch this, it only fails when it runs.\n\nFound by mounting the component for the first time. The console had two\ntest files, covering pluginRegistry''s pure functions and AppView''s mount\nlogic; nothing had ever rendered the plugin list. A page that threw on\nevery render passed the build, the commit and the push.\n\nThe lesson is not more assertions, it is mounting each page at least once.\nThat bug needed no clever case — only for someone to call mount().\n\nAlso adds tests for the two things the console has to distinguish and\ncould easily not: a tripped circuit breaker reading as tripped rather than\nrunning (it is enabled, has its replicas, and is failing every call — the\nonly unhealthy state that clears itself, so reading it as \"running\" sends\nan operator to the wrong place), and a queue backlog shown separately from\nwhat the queue gave up on.\n\nAnd for PluginConfig, whose Go half is well covered and whose browser half\nwas not: the mask for a secret is submitted back unchanged, a default is\nshown for a setting nobody configured, and a save that was stored but not\ndelivered says so rather than reporting success. Verified by mutation —\nswallowing the warning, dropping the default, and blanking the secret each\nfail exactly one test.","tree":{"sha":"e35709dd6bb5ff4a8e3e79defd6a6183d9c98531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e35709dd6bb5ff4a8e3e79defd6a6183d9c98531"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDUyNzFkOTExYThkZjk0OTZjOTMxZjYyNDc1MjAzNGRiMGIzNzMyZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a","sha":"193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a"}],"sha":"5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/5271d911a8df9496c931f624752034db0b3732e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:05:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:05:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: a disabled plugin answered 502, which reads as a fault\n\nEvery backend failure became 502, including \"this plugin is not enabled\".\nMeasured by pointing real traffic at a plugin while an operator disabled\nit: 6889 requests, 1416 served and 5473 answered 502. A client cannot tell\nthat from a crash, so it retries; an operator watching for 502 gets paged\nby a change they made on purpose.\n\nThree situations, three answers:\n\n  404  not enabled, never installed, quarantined — the route does not\n       exist, the same way the menu does not. Do not retry.\n  503  enabled but between states: starting, draining, at capacity.\n       Transient, so retrying is right.\n  502  the plugin was there and the call failed.\n\nFound by testing the operator''s own path for the first time. What existed\nwas the registry''s blue-green swap under load, and a manager upgrade with\ntraffic aimed at a *different* plugin. Neither covers what an operator\nactually creates by clicking 重载 or 停用 on a plugin that is serving right\nnow. Upgrading under load turned out to be clean — 4008 requests, all 200.\nDisabling was not.\n\nFour existing tests pinned the old contract and had to change. Three were\nstraightforwardly better as 404 (offline, unloaded, never-installed). The\nfourth, TestDrainingPluginIsNotRouted, turned out not to test draining at\nall: with nothing in flight the drain completed immediately, so it\nexercised a stopped instance. Both were 502, so nothing said so. It is now\ntwo tests — stopped is 404, and a genuinely draining plugin, held open by\na request the fake blocks, is 503.","tree":{"sha":"051ac914467e01676c49207e657413044daa6ac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/051ac914467e01676c49207e657413044daa6ac4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDE5MzM1NmZmNDEyMWViODkwYzk3YmFlNzM0OTM5NDI4ZDdmODJlMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7","sha":"57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7"}],"sha":"193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/193356ff4121eb890c97bae734939428d7f82e0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:47:01Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:47:01Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: pin the phase order a real request actually produces\n\nEvery phase had been tested on its own, and the ordering had been tested\nat the pipeline level with fakes. Nothing checked the sequence a real\nrequest produces through real plugin processes — which is exactly where\nthe last bug lived: the 401 and the authenticate phase were each correct\nand happened in the wrong order, so the phase was unreachable. A bug where\nboth halves are right and the order is wrong is invisible to unit tests by\nconstruction.\n\nThe sequence is read back out of the plugin rather than inferred from side\neffects: the echo fixture records which phases it was called in per trace,\nand the test asks it. What is asserted is what happened.\n\nCovers the full order; on_error staying silent on success and firing when\nthe backend is killed; the log phase running for a request an earlier\nfilter refused — which both example READMEs claim and which is what makes\nan audit plugin worth having, since refused traffic is the traffic most\nworth recording; and declared order deciding across two plugins, observed\nby having the low-order filter refuse so the high-order one must never be\nreached. Two filters both returning Continue have no observable order.\n\nAll five claims hold. No bug this time.","tree":{"sha":"3448e5ad05806e7e4cee16430f2721cb1753dcfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/3448e5ad05806e7e4cee16430f2721cb1753dcfd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDU3NTM5OTU4ZDZmNmZkMTNlMWU1MmYwNzllM2E5MjU4ZTJiY2VkZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d","sha":"50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d"}],"sha":"57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/57539958d6f6fd13e1e52f079e3a9258e2bcedf7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:41:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:41:39Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: the authenticate phase was unreachable\n\nCore resolved the session at the top of servePlugin and answered 401 when\nit did not resolve — before the authenticate phase ran. So a caller\nholding an API key, a JWT, a signature, anything that is not one of Core''s\nown session cookies, was refused before the plugin that understands their\ncredential was ever asked.\n\nThe whole filter:authenticate mechanism was there: the permission, the\nphase gate, the discard-and-log when a plugin lacks it, the SDK''s\nSetIdentity, and a comment saying a filter \"can enrich or replace\" what\nCore resolved. Every piece except a request that could reach it. This is\nrequirement four of the original brief, and it was found by writing an\nexample that needed it.\n\nThe refusal moves to after authenticate and authorize. Same question,\nasked once the people whose job it is to answer have had their turn. It is\nstill unconditional, so a plugin route reached by a caller nobody could\nidentify is refused exactly as before, and a deployment with no\nauthenticate filter installed behaves identically.\n\nFour cases, because \"runs the phase\" and \"honours its verdict\" are\ndifferent things and a fix could do the first without the second: an API\nkey gets in, no credential does not, a wrong key does not, and a session\nstill does. Reverting the change fails the first and passes the rest.\n\nAlso tested for the first time: the identity one plugin establishes\nreaching another plugin''s handler. That is the product claim — plugins\nfrom different teams intervening at different phases of one request — and\neverything until now had checked one plugin at a time. The echo fixture\nnow echoes the caller Core passed it, so it can be checked rather than\nassumed.","tree":{"sha":"e19bb69c2bdfa0075e5c13035ecde7889cee6895","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e19bb69c2bdfa0075e5c13035ecde7889cee6895"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDUwMTI1YjYwYjY2ZWY1ZTZlYjM4OGE2MTJkNzcxNzFlNTljNzNmM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997","sha":"d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997"}],"sha":"50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/50125b60b66ef5e6eb388a612d77171e59c73f3d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:32:42Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:32:42Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: apikey example — the filter that decides who the caller is\n\nThe other three examples cover a filter that observes and one that\nrefuses. None covered the authenticate and authorize phases, which is the\nonly place in the model where a plugin can grant identity, and therefore\nthe part most worth having an example and a test for. Requirement four of\nthe original brief, with nothing to copy from.\n\nThe example issues and revokes keys, hashes rather than stores them,\nresolves one into an identity in the authenticate phase, and refuses\nanonymous callers on configured prefixes in the authorize phase. Both\nfilters are fail_closed, because an authenticator that fails open waves\nevery request through unauthenticated the moment the plugin has a bad\nminute.\n\nThe enforcement is tested against the real pipeline with the same plugin\nbinary and only the granted permissions changed: without\nfilter:authenticate the mutation is discarded and logged, with it the\nidentity is applied. Both directions, since a Core that ignored every\nidentity mutation would pass the first test alone.\n\nAnd a measurement worth having, found by writing it: sdk.Cache lives in\nCore, so a cache hit is still a cross-process round trip.\n\n  no credential at all      39 µs\n  sdk.Cache only           124 µs\n  in-process layer first    43 µs\n\nFor a handler that is a fine trade. For a filter subscribed to /** it is\nnot: those 80 µs are added to every request in the system, including ones\nbelonging to plugins that have nothing to do with this one. The example\ncaches in-process in front of sdk.Cache, with a separate short TTL —\nwhich is really configuring how long a revoked key keeps working — and\nthe timing test asserts the cached path stays within 2x of the\nno-credential path rather than against a wall-clock constant. Removing\nthe local layer takes it to 3x and fails.","tree":{"sha":"278e6a7a650fff8a75710442e5c4470defb2b5fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/278e6a7a650fff8a75710442e5c4470defb2b5fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGQxM2ZjNjRkMDg5YTlkMzA4MTA2NzJiNDgwMDMwNWNmYzg2Y2I5OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8","sha":"2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8"}],"sha":"d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/d13fc64d089a9d30810672b4800305cfc86cb997"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:22:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:22:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: say something when the queue gives up on work\n\nThe durable queue retries a failing message up to max_attempts and then\nparks it as dead. That policy is right — a poison message retried forever\nis worse — but nothing marked the moment it happened. The plugin''s handler\nhad already returned an error and moved on; Core wrote ''dead'' to a row and\nsaid nothing; and the depth the console shows counts pending and\nprocessing, so a dead message made the number go *down*.\n\nThe result: a plugin whose handler is permanently broken drains its entire\nbacklog into ''dead'' and reads, from the console, as one that has caught\nup. Work that was accepted and will never be done, presented as progress.\nFor a durable queue — whose whole purpose is that work is not lost — that\nis the worst available failure mode.\n\n- Queue.OnDeadLetter fires only when the attempts are actually exhausted,\n  so it marks giving up rather than every retry. Nack now uses RETURNING\n  to learn which branch the CASE took; reading it back afterwards would\n  race the next delivery.\n- Queue.DeadDepth counts them, deliberately separate from PendingDepth:\n  a backlog drains and a graveyard does not, and adding them would make\n  the two indistinguishable.\n- main.go logs it, the plugin Status carries it, the console shows it.\n- The guide tells plugin authors that a handler gets no \"this is the last\n  attempt\" signal and has to check msg.Attempt itself.\n\nBoth directions are tested: exhausting the budget reports once, and a\nretry that still has attempts left reports not at all — a hook that fired\non every failure would be noise, and noise gets filtered out along with\nthe one message that mattered.","tree":{"sha":"ee719f72bd6b794e6587e2ebe4593a8f4f4ecf48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/ee719f72bd6b794e6587e2ebe4593a8f4f4ecf48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDJkOWU0ZWZkOTQwODg1ZjE1NTU0NjI0MWQzMDg2Y2Y0ZDJjNmJkYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26","sha":"fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26"}],"sha":"2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/2d9e4efd940885f155546241d3086cf4d2c6bdc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:15:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:15:48Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: pin the pipeline''s per-filter allocation cost\n\nForty rounds of changes and nobody had checked the hot path since the\nnumbers in docs/plugin-development.md were written. Comparing: Core''s own\nroute is faster (52 -> 41 µs), pure RPC unchanged (37/43 -> 38/43), and\nevery filter-depth figure lands inside the noise. No regression.\n\nDoing that by hand is not a guard, and wall-clock cannot be one here —\nrun-to-run variance on the filter benchmark is wider than a change worth\ncatching, and the first run of a set is reliably high (filters_1 measured\n176 µs cold and 143-147 µs on the three runs after). Allocation counts do\nnot move with CPU load, so that is what this pins: the pipeline''s own cost\nper filter, with about double today''s figure as the ceiling.\n\nMeasured at five allocations per filter, against roughly 129 per filter\nend to end — the other ~124 are the gRPC round trip. A deep pipeline is\nexpensive because of the process boundary, and this keeps it that way.\n\nThe first version of the test guarded nothing: it used an empty header\nmap, and converting headers once per filter instead of once per request —\nthe regression it exists to catch — allocates nothing when there are no\nheaders. With a real request''s headers, disabling the cache takes it from\n5 to 14 and fails.","tree":{"sha":"1ce1d5b73822f1b23afe5225cff928838f493f5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/1ce1d5b73822f1b23afe5225cff928838f493f5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGZiNWM2N2ZhZWI0ZjZmMmY1ZDVjNDI1YzA1YzBmYzVjMmUwMGRkMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba","sha":"037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba"}],"sha":"fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/fb5c67faeb4f6f2f5d5c425c05c0fc5c2e00dd26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:11:00Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:11:00Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"perf: raise the transaction ceiling to 8, measured\n\nThe per-plugin ceiling was four, on the reasoning that \"four is generous\nfor work that is supposed to be short\". That was never checked against a\nrunning system, and it was wrong by about a third.\n\nThirty-two concurrent transactional reservations, completed per second:\n\n  ceiling      1     2     4     8    16    25\n  spread     713   920  1257  1683  1567   716\n  contended  410   346   273   187   132   128\n\nSpread — each transaction on its own document — is what a plugin normally\ndoes, and it peaks at eight. Past that the pool of twenty-five runs out:\nat sixteen the give-ups quadruple, at twenty-five throughput halves\nbecause callers wait on connections that are all held.\n\nContended — every transaction fighting for one row — gets worse as the\nceiling rises, since the extra concurrency becomes row-lock waiting and\nversion conflicts. That cost is real and accepted: a hot row is throttled\nby Postgres either way, and eight of twenty-five connections still leaves\nseventeen for every other plugin and for Core.\n\nThe benchmark contaminated itself before it was usable. Reusing one\ncollection meant each run left a few hundred thousand dead tuples in the\nsame row, and until autovacuum caught up the next run measured the bloat.\nTwo sweeps an hour apart differed 3x on absolute throughput with an\nidentical shape. Each run now gets its own collection and drops it.\nConclusions come from the shape; the absolute numbers belong to whatever\nthe machine was doing.\n\nTxRegistry.SetMaxOpen exists so the ceiling can be measured rather than\nargued about. Core does not call it, and its comment says so.","tree":{"sha":"b44f9632811f54c4cde03dd976f63f3b2c25b34b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/b44f9632811f54c4cde03dd976f63f3b2c25b34b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDAzNzg1NGEyOGM5YTMyNGVmZDdkMDA3NTFhMzU1MWIzYzJkNGQyYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0","sha":"933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0"}],"sha":"037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/037854a28c9a324efd7d00751a3551b3c2d4d2ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:59:31Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:59:31Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: inventory example, and the two bugs running it found\n\nA fourth example, built around the case where a plugin cannot get the\nright answer without a transaction: reserving stock. Written, then run\nunder real concurrency — thirty requests against ten units — which is\nwhere it earned its keep.\n\nTwo faults, one in Core:\n\nThe per-plugin transaction ceiling did not hold. The count was derived by\nwalking the open-transaction map in one critical section and the insert\nhappened in another, so concurrent callers all counted zero, all passed a\nlimit of four, and all opened one. Seventeen were open at once against a\npool of twenty-five — the ceiling that exists to stop one plugin taking\nthe pool was doing nothing at exactly the moment it was needed. Check and\nreservation now share a critical section. Reverting the fix does not just\nfail the new test: it hangs, because forty transactions exhaust the pool\nand every caller waits forever, which is the failure the ceiling prevents.\n\nA version conflict and an expired transaction were both FailedPrecondition\nand need opposite responses — retry the write, versus the transaction is\ngone. Version conflict is now Aborted, which is what gRPC means by a\nconcurrency conflict a client retries. Hitting the transaction ceiling was\nInternal and is now ResourceExhausted; it is a busy moment, not a fault.\n\nAnd a usability gap the example ran straight into: branching on any of\nthis meant importing google.golang.org/grpc and comparing codes, in a\nlibrary whose whole point is that plugins write against the SDK. There are\nnow sentinels — ErrVersionConflict, ErrTxExpired, ErrRateLimited,\nErrNotAllowed, ErrNotFound — that errors.Is matches.\n\nMeasured across the three versions of the example, ten units against\nthirty concurrent requests:\n\n  no retry                        2 sold, 28 server errors\n  retry version conflicts only   10 sold, 20 server errors\n  retry both, ceiling fixed      10 sold, 20 told there is none left, 0 errors\n\nNothing was ever oversold. But for two of those three, a system that was\nworking correctly looked broken from outside.","tree":{"sha":"d86b9f6d3e827656ee775406450e90601ccb9622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/d86b9f6d3e827656ee775406450e90601ccb9622"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDkzMzg3OWE3YWIzNmEyOWNmNzJjMDkwNmIxM2FmOWFlOTQyYWY4ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200","sha":"e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200"}],"sha":"933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/933879a7ab36a29cf72c0906b13af9ae942af8d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:39:55Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:39:55Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"chore: remove two accessors nobody calls, and label what is not connected\n\nSet.Patterns returned the backing slice of a compiled pattern set. Those\nsets are shared by the lock-free request path and are immutable after\ncompilation, so handing out the slice was an aliasing hole — and nothing\nused it. Client.HostBrokerID exposed a transport detail no caller needs.\n\nRegistry.SetFilterDefaults stays, with a comment saying Core does not call\nit and no environment variable reaches it. A setter nobody calls otherwise\nreads as a knob an operator can turn.\n\ncore/db/migrations.go is a complete, tested declarative migration engine\nthat Core never invokes: there is nowhere in a manifest to declare a\nmigration and no bookkeeping to decide when one runs. Both facts are now\nat the top of the file, along with what connecting it would still need.\nThe gap it leaves is real — ReconcileSchema only adds, so a renamed field\nleaves every existing document behind — so the plugin guide now tells\nauthors that this is theirs to handle and what their two options are.","tree":{"sha":"0f43b32ec8ed36e60e76d65678642600bd8c3be5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/0f43b32ec8ed36e60e76d65678642600bd8c3be5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGU1NzU3NzllYzBmZDIyYTE0MWUwMjMwODk0MTk2OTMyNjg1YjAyMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30","sha":"ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30"}],"sha":"e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/e575779ec0fd22a141e0230894196932685b0200"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:36:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:36:16Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: surface queue backlog; fix three comments that described other code\n\nThe queue refuses an Enqueue past MaxDepth, and nothing showed the\nbacklog growing toward it — the first sign was the refusal. The\nmaintenance loop already measures the depth for that ceiling check, so\nthis is only a matter of it reaching somewhere a person looks.\n\nThree comments describing behaviour the code does not have:\n\n- sdk/plugin/host.go: \"Metric records a measurement\" sat on asLogValue,\n  two functions above the Metric it describes.\n- pluginhost/instance.go: the state table claimed Failed -> Starting and\n  Quarantined -> Starting. Neither happens: a retry or a re-enable builds\n  a new Instance and replaces this one, so those states are terminal for\n  the instance that reaches them. Anyone debugging \"why is this failed\n  instance not starting again\" was being sent to look for a transition\n  that does not exist.\n- db/queue.go: QueueStats said \"for the console\", which never called it.\n  The console''s backlog comes from PendingDepth; QueueStats is the\n  finer-grained per-topic view an operator asks for by hand.","tree":{"sha":"8302bd7715581fcdcfab195f6c2473120c936161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/8302bd7715581fcdcfab195f6c2473120c936161"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGZmOGJiNDllNjlkMWIwMDg0OWRjNTQyMjJmZWZiMzBmMTEyYjZiMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0","sha":"ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0"}],"sha":"ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ff8bb49e69d1b00849dc54222fefb30f112b6b30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:32:47Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:32:47Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"feat: show a tripped breaker and replica uptime in the console\n\nBreaker.Open() said in its own comment that it was safe for diagnostics\nand was called by nothing but tests, because Status carried no breaker\nstate and the console had nowhere to read it from. Instance.StartedAt()\nwas the same.\n\nFrom the console a plugin Core has stopped calling looks exactly like one\nthat is merely slow: enabled, ready, failing. They need opposite\nresponses — a tripped breaker is Core protecting itself from a plugin that\nhas been erroring, and it clears on its own. And a plugin that restarts\nevery thirty seconds reads as \"running\" on every refresh unless something\nsays how long it has actually been up.\n\nOpen() rather than Allow(): Allow consumes the half-open probe, so reading\nthe state through it would starve the recovery being reported.","tree":{"sha":"07c60df4453c9fe3a11c95a9c36051c2213e508d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/07c60df4453c9fe3a11c95a9c36051c2213e508d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGFjMjY0YTlkZmU3NmQwNWRiYTVkNzFkNzFmYjQxNGRjNWUxMjUwYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009","sha":"cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009"}],"sha":"ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ac264a9dfe76d05dba5d71d71fb414dc5e1250b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:29:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:29:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"refactor: symmetry in the SDK''s transaction client, and one expiry rule\n\nTxClient.Get returned only (found, error), dropping the version, and\nTxClient.PutIfVersion did not exist. The asymmetry read as \"optimistic\nlocking is not needed inside a transaction\", which is not true: two\ntransactions can both read a row, and the second write proceeds against a\nrow the first has already changed. Both now mirror DBClient.\n\nCache and lock expiry was three copies of \"is this over\", two of which\ndisagreed at the boundary. Worth being precise about the impact, because\nit is smaller than it looks: acquisition''s boundary was already the right\none, and the sweeper only reclaims memory, so the only boundary that moves\nis the cache''s, by one tick. The value is having one predicate — copies\nthat drift unnoticed are the condition under which the next one breaks\nsomething. The test says exactly this, and names the one mutation it\ncatches.\n\nCacheBackend and LockBackend now take a context they do not yet use. The\ncomment above them promises that swapping in Redis is a change of backend\nrather than of contract; adding the parameter later would break that\npromise at the one moment it was supposed to pay off.","tree":{"sha":"dcec97cf455d6497635aef37d769dbede10045cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/dcec97cf455d6497635aef37d769dbede10045cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGNkMDdjYWU1ZWE2YWMzZDRkOWI2ZjdlZjk3MjI3MjEzOTU4NmUwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2","sha":"c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2"}],"sha":"cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/cd07cae5ea6ac3d4d9b6f7ef972272139586e009"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:22:53Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:22:53Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: outbound and file failures now say which failure they are\n\nEvery capability classifies its errors into gRPC codes so a plugin can\nbranch on them. Two did not, in opposite ways.\n\nFetch returned its backend error raw, so grpc-go wrapped everything in\ncodes.Unknown: a host that was never granted, a rate limit, a malformed\nURL and a remote server that is down all arrived identical. The first is\npermanent and means editing the manifest, the second means waiting, the\nthird is the plugin''s own bug, the fourth is worth retrying.\n\nThe file capability had one condition mapped three ways by its three\ncallers: a missing file was NotFound from DeleteFile and Internal from\nGenerateDownloadToken. An operator watching for Internal was being paged\nby an ordinary 404.\n\nEgress and file refusals now carry sentinels, classified by egressErr and\nfileErr in the same shape as the existing dataErr.\n\nGetFileMetadata deliberately keeps its different contract: it asks whether\na file exists and answers with the Found field the proto gives it, rather\nthan making the ordinary case an error. A file owned by another plugin\nstill reads exactly like a missing one everywhere.\n\nTwo of the tests in this commit were wrong before they were right, and the\ncomments say so: a loopback upstream never reaches the dial because the\naddress guard refuses it, so an unreachable host has to be a name that\ncannot resolve; and the allow-list has no bare \"*\" pattern.","tree":{"sha":"834887546c1c79032109a51f74675f06715a1543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/834887546c1c79032109a51f74675f06715a1543"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGM0N2U1YmE4NmRjZTVlM2JhNWVmMmI3YzA0ZjU2N2MxNWU2MzdhYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa","sha":"a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa"}],"sha":"c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/c47e5ba86dce5e3ba5ef2b7c04f567c15e637ac2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:15:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:15:19Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: disabling a plugin mid-restart could quarantine it\n\nDisable clears `enabled` before it removes the plugin from the registry.\nA crash recovery waking from its backoff inside that window still sees the\nplugin registered, tries to relaunch, and is refused because the plugin is\nno longer enabled. The supervisor treated that refusal as another failed\nrestart: it retried with a longer backoff, and every attempt counted\ntoward the crash threshold.\n\nEnough of them and a plugin an admin deliberately switched off is reported\nas one Core gave up on after repeated crashes — a state the console\npresents as a fault and which only an explicit re-enable clears.\n\nrelaunch now returns ErrPluginDisabled and the supervisor treats it as\nterminal rather than as a failure. The registry check stays as a cheap\nearly-out, with a comment saying why it is not the decision.\n\nBoth directions are tested: a disabled plugin is abandoned after one\nattempt, and a restart that fails for a real reason still escalates to\nquarantine — a supervisor that called every failure \"disabled\" would pass\nthe first test alone.","tree":{"sha":"3c5b55544a686a0dc2cfde5cdf86a2b29a0a7633","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/3c5b55544a686a0dc2cfde5cdf86a2b29a0a7633"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGEzN2UzN2E3MTA5OTQ5ODRhOTllZmZkZDA1MTEwNDgxNjE4YmU3ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2","sha":"436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2"}],"sha":"a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/a37e37a710994984a99effdd05110481618be7fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:11:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:11:35Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: reads inside a transaction ran outside it\n\nPut, Get, Delete and BatchWrite resolved a transaction id into the\nexecutor that transaction runs on. Find, Query and Aggregate accepted the\nsame parameter and dropped it. So a plugin that wrote a document and then\nqueried for it in the same transaction did not find it: the write was\nuncommitted, the query was on a different connection, and nothing reported\nan error — the plugin just got an answer that was wrong.\n\nThe permission gate had drifted the same way. Put, Get, Delete, Query and\nBatchWrite called requireTx; Find and Aggregate did not, so a plugin\nwithout the db:tx grant could pass a transaction id to those two\nunchecked. Free while the id was ignored — and a way to read uncommitted\ndata the moment the reads started honouring it, which is what this change\ndoes.\n\ndb.Find/Query/Aggregate now take an execer like the write paths already\ndid, nil meaning the pool. Find also takes a context, which it never had.\n\nTests cover both directions: a read in a transaction sees that\ntransaction''s writes, and an uncommitted write stays invisible to everyone\nelse.","tree":{"sha":"02ea964459a7b428f0fb2527d171e79efd1b54be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/02ea964459a7b428f0fb2527d171e79efd1b54be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDQzNjY4OTg1OGM4YmNlOTcwMjExYzQ5YjUzOGUyMmU5YjIxYjA2YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9","sha":"9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9"}],"sha":"436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/436689858c8bce970211c49b538e22e9b21b06a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:06:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T21:06:05Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: auditing was recording nothing, and believed the client''s identity\n\nTwo faults with one root, found by a coherence review.\n\nThe audit middleware carried its own copy of the API prefix as a string\nliteral. When the route was renamed from /api/extensions/ to\n/api/plugins/, the literal stayed behind: every request still passed\nthrough the middleware, none of them matched, and the audit table has been\nempty ever since. Nothing failed — the middleware''s own test used the dead\nprefix too, so it kept passing while a compliance feature was absent.\n\nBoth the middleware and the browser upload endpoint took the acting user\nfrom an X-User-Id header. Nothing in Core has ever set that header, so it\nwas whatever the client typed. An audit log recorded the name the audited\nparty chose, and every file''s uploader was chosen by whoever uploaded it.\nThat is worse than an empty column, because someone will use it to answer\n\"who put this here\".\n\n- the prefix now comes from whoever owns the route, and an empty one\n  panics at start-up rather than auditing nothing silently\n- identity is resolved from the session, the way every other handler\n  resolves it\n- clientIP now says in a comment that X-Forwarded-For is only as\n  trustworthy as the proxy in front of Core\n\nThe end-to-end test is the point: a unit test of the middleware can only\ncheck that the prefix it was handed is honoured, and in a test that prefix\nis whatever the test chose. Reverting the prefix to /api/extensions/ leaves\ncore/middleware green and fails tests/audit_test.go.","tree":{"sha":"b77476c5ca76640c365608e209ba6676032751e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/b77476c5ca76640c365608e209ba6676032751e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKDllZDhhNDRiOTE5MzNlOTFkODkzOTM0MGEyZThjZTEzMjJmZDVmZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56","sha":"ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56"}],"sha":"9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/9ed8a44b91933e91d8939340a2e8ce1322fd5fd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T20:58:14Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T20:58:14Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"test: assert every host capability is actually wired in main.go\n\nGeneralises the bug shape this codebase has produced three times: a\ncapability with a complete contract on both ends and nothing joining them\nin the middle. Configuration push had it, the cron scheduler had it, and\nconfiguration storage had it — every half was tested, the join was not.\n\nA nil field in hostsvc.Deps is an error nowhere. The capability reports\nUnavailable forever, which is indistinguishable from a Core deliberately\nstarted without a database.\n\nParsed rather than grepped, so a field mentioned only in a comment does\nnot count as wired. Verified by removing the Egress wiring and watching it\nfail.","tree":{"sha":"058bd5eb5fb9d7c32bc5477f1e355742ba04e0c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/058bd5eb5fb9d7c32bc5477f1e355742ba04e0c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGFkM2VhMWFiOGZiNWZjMmM2OTQzNjZkNDQ3YjU0MGUwNjg1MjNlNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9","sha":"f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9"}],"sha":"ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/ad3ea1ab8fb5fc2c694366d447b540e068523e56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T20:55:56Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T20:55:56Z","email":"taills@qq.com","name":"taills"},"message":"fix: refuse manifest fields Core does not recognise\n\nA manifest is what a reviewer reads to decide whether to install a plugin\nand what Core enforces. yaml.Unmarshal dropped anything it did not\nrecognise, so those two could disagree without a word from either side.\n\nMost typos happen to fail closed — a misspelled `permissions:` leaves the\nplugin with none and it fails on its first call. `filters:` is the\nexception, and it is the one that matters: a plugin whose entire purpose\nis a fail-closed authenticate filter installs cleanly, reports as running,\nand every request goes unauthenticated while the console shows the\nmanifest that says otherwise.\n\nAlso covers the reverse direction — a decoder that refused valid manifests\nwould pass the strictness test on its own. All three examples still load.","tree":{"sha":"e31cc3c95807381a1a279dd984a500c24f1536fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/trees/e31cc3c95807381a1a279dd984a500c24f1536fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/git/commits/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9","node_id":"C_kwDOTJL4O9oAKGY3NGVhYzZjZDQ2MmIxOWFjMDZkNGNjNDQwNWQ5OTI4MjY0Mzk5ZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/taills/moduless/commit/64df9e043986ef23c83c80a6b28535e51fdc41d6","sha":"64df9e043986ef23c83c80a6b28535e51fdc41d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/64df9e043986ef23c83c80a6b28535e51fdc41d6"}],"sha":"f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taills/moduless/commits/f74eac6cd462b19ac06d4cc4405d9928264399d9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47925925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taills","id":47925925,"login":"taills","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTI1OTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taills","use