orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seo-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seo-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seo-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seo-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seo-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kroelofs/bidneighbor/commits/c7540d51487242232b8113aa2e361bffa93bd7d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T23:19:47Z","email":"seo-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"seo-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T23:19:47Z","email":"seo-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"seo-byte"},"message":"feat(uploads): auto-shrink oversized images before upload\n\nAdd a client-side image downscaler (lib/image.ts): if a photo is larger than\n~2 MB it''s re-encoded via a canvas — longest edge capped at 1600px, JPEG quality\nstepped down (and dimension shrunk again if needed) until it fits — so oversized\nuploads succeed instead of bouncing off the 10 MB server limit. Runs entirely in\nthe browser; the network only sees the smaller file.\n\nWired into every image upload: message attachments (MessageThread), resource\nphotos (PostResource), and task photos (PostTask). JPEG/PNG/WebP are re-encoded;\nGIFs and non-images (PDFs) pass through untouched. createImageBitmap with an\n<img> fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc18b313aa69abddf373172c69df4edda4a4cac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kroelofs/bidneighbor/git/trees/dc18b313aa69abddf373172c69df4edda4a4cac8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kroelofs/bidneighbor/git/commits/c7540d51487242232b8113aa2e361bffa93bd7d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27709607