ogin":"polasudo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODY0MTQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/polasudo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/commits/a498f0667ab17b270ec726d74042af6c6933b4c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T08:36:11Z","email":"mpolasko@redhat.com","name":"Martin Polasko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T10:57:07Z","email":"mpolasko@redhat.com","name":"Martin Polasko"},"message":"fix: address review feedback on GraphQL fallback\n\n- Narrow fallback condition to connection-level errors only (ECONNRESET,\n  ECONNREFUSED) and also check error.cause.code; drop the broad\n  HttpError match that could mask auth/permission failures\n- Only treat 404 from git.getRef as \"no existing HEAD\"; rethrow\n  401/403/rate-limit/network errors instead of swallowing them\n- Delete .gitkeep in the follow-up GraphQL commit when it was used to\n  initialize an empty repository, so no leftover file remains\n- Remove unused gitAuthorInfo param from pushFilesViaGitHubApi since\n  GraphQL createCommitOnBranch uses the authenticated user identity\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Polasko <mpolasko@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Martin Polasko <mpolasko@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bf45c938da422f57bd17c98e19c9be4e1b22007","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/git/trees/9bf45c938da422f57bd17c98e19c9be4e1b22007"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/git/commits/a498f0667ab17b270ec726d74042af6c6933b4c6","ve