reben/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/commits/cb0040dcb4eb88f033e5b1af04bd7cdb7b83936e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T09:07:07Z","email":"freben@gmail.com","name":"Fredrik Adelöw"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T10:43:26Z","email":"freben@gmail.com","name":"Fredrik Adelöw"},"message":"fix(catalog-backend): extend autovacuum tuning to all high-churn tables\n\nAdd final_entities, relations, and refresh_state_references to the\nautovacuum scale factor tuning alongside search. All four tables\nexperience high churn from stitching and ingestion, and their visibility\nmaps degrade between default autovacuum runs (85.6%, 81%, and 45.9%\nrespectively), preventing index-only scans.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Fredrik Adelöw <freben@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2737c243dd102b19b5e2d45afc573d3e30143166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/git/trees/2737c243dd102b19b5e2d45afc573d3e30143166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SerenityInAllThings/Backstage_test/git/commits/cb0040dcb4eb88f033e5b1af04bd7cdb7b83936e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3097461?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/