"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/128d620808062beeaa9a82155a677bf7e5c3fbb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:57:52Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:57:52Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"fix: translate agent names to English in EN mode\n\nLanding page pipeline titles (lpF1Title..lpF5Title) had never actually\nbeen translated in the en dict — copy-pasted Indonesian values. The\nagent-activity chip panel on the Chat page was worse: labels were\nhardcoded plain text, not wired into the existing T.id/T.en i18n system\nat all.\n\nAdded agEyes/agBookkeeper/agInventory/agStrategy/agDataEntry/\nagReasoning/agVoice keys to both dicts and wrapped each chip label in\na <span id=\"ag...\">, wired into _applyStaticLabels(). The data-agent\nattributes used by _flashAgents() for highlight-matching are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86fbb1f518d05090dca879fe736656fd44f7d35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/86fbb1f518d05090dca879fe736656fd44f7d35a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/128d620808062beeaa9a82155a677bf7e5c3fbb8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/128d620808062beeaa9a82155a677bf7e5c3fbb8","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKDEyOGQ2MjA4MDgwNjJiZWVhYTlhODIxNTVhNjc3YmY3ZTVjM2ZiYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d","sha":"cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d"}],"sha":"128d620808062beeaa9a82155a677bf7e5c3fbb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/128d620808062beeaa9a82155a677bf7e5c3fbb8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T03:57:03Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T03:57:03Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"fix: data_entry_agent ignores counter-questions and voice_agent answers wrong item\n\nTwo related context bugs in the chat data-entry flow:\n\n- data_entry_agent''s system prompt only listed item names, never their\n  stock, so it had no way to answer a counter-question mid slot-filling\n  (e.g. \"sekarang ada berapa?\") and just repeated its own question.\n  Now includes current stock and an explicit rule to answer before re-asking.\n\n- voice_agent''s context builder only surfaced inventory items below\n  reorder point, so a just-restocked item was invisible to it — a\n  follow-up question about that item fell through to whichever other\n  item was low and got answered about that instead. Now always includes\n  full per-item stock levels, and the mock synthesizer prioritizes an\n  item explicitly named in the query over the alert list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42bc618806667366e498d466e7c94af541ab1bae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/42bc618806667366e498d466e7c94af541ab1bae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGNhZTA0MTJmNGJlM2NmZmUyMGE5OTVlYTdhMDJhMGM2NTIyZGY0NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d","sha":"ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d"}],"sha":"cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/cae0412f4be3cffe20a995ea7a02a0c6522df46d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:26:55Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:26:55Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"revert: simplify agent-activity panel back to the plain chip version\n\nRestores api/static/index.html''s agent panel to exactly its state at\n844e99a (the last commit before isometric characters were introduced),\nundoing the isometric-character/walk-animation/sidebar/3x3-grid work\nbuilt on top of it since. Chosen deliberately over trying to hand-edit\nthe current version down: 844e99a..HEAD touches this file in exactly\n4 commits (9cf7160, d760b61, ddd4868, 947bf76), all scoped purely to\nthis panel with nothing else mixed in, so restoring the whole file to\nthat commit is a complete, surgical revert — no other feature (sales/\nexpense entry, sticky routing, file cleanup, CSS fixes) lives in this\nfile and none of it is touched.\n\nBack to: a horizontal row of 7 text/dot chips above the chat, filling\nsolid blue with a bold label for 2.5s when agents_invoked names them,\nthen fading — same trigger wiring (_flashAgents reading agents_invoked\nfrom /chat), just the plain presentation from before any of the\ncharacter/animation work.\n\nVerified locally before committing: server starts clean, all 7 chips\nrender with correct data-agent ids, no viewport overflow, a real chat\nround trip (\"gimana stoknya\") highlights exactly inventory_agent +\nvoice_agent and nothing else, data_entry_agent''s expense-entry flow\nstill responds correctly through the reverted panel, no console\nerrors in any check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55e9ee46f53c5e2a4221b247110100fb953d0f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/55e9ee46f53c5e2a4221b247110100fb953d0f1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGNhOWFhYzgxNWUyOGE0NzAwM2EwMDBjNWFlYTQ2M2I0MmMwMDI5OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee","sha":"947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee"}],"sha":"ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ca9aac815e28a47003a000c5aea463b42c00298d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:59:10Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:59:10Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: redesign agent panel as a 3x3 hub-spoke grid, center = user\n\nReplaces the single-column vertical sidebar with a 3x3 CSS grid: the\nuser mascot sits fixed at the center cell, the 7 agents fill 7 of the\n8 surrounding cells (row3/col3 left spare), tracks now radiate from\neach agent to the center instead of running straight down a column.\n\nReused as-is, no changes needed: _isoCharTile template, AGENT_CHARACTERS\nconfig, agents_invoked trigger via _flashAgents, the walk keyframes''\neasing/bounce/stagger. The anchor-based position system built for the\nvertical layout (_tileAnchor/_updateTracks/_walkToUser) already worked\nfrom live getBoundingClientRect() positions rather than an assumed\ndirection, so pointing it at a grid needed zero logic changes — only\neach tile''s actual (row,col) changed.\n\nWhat did change:\n- .agent-sidebar: 92px column -> 240px, .agent-panel: flex-column ->\n  3x3 CSS grid (place-items:center), each tile gets an inline\n  grid-row/grid-column from a new `pos` field on its config entry.\n- _agentAnchor() dropped the horizontal \"fan\" offset added for the old\n  layout (needed there because every agent shared one X in a single\n  column; a grid already gives each agent a distinct position, so the\n  offset was redundant and would have skewed tracks off from true\n  center).\n\nVerified in a real browser: idle layout renders correctly (grid intact,\n7 distinct-colored tracks radiating to center, no overlap), no viewport\noverflow, single-agent walk moves diagonally along its exact track to\ncenter and back, 4-agent simultaneous walk shows distinct non-colliding\npaths converging on the center cell, all tiles settle back to\ntransform:none afterward, and a real chat round trip (\"gimana stoknya\")\nstill triggers the correct characters with no console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0d9a06563dc26bc2598b9d1b79ef0bffc51f54e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/f0d9a06563dc26bc2598b9d1b79ef0bffc51f54e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKDk0N2JmNzZlOGJlNjg5ZDg1ZWZmNGI0YzNhNGJiMGIyM2JiYzRhZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd","sha":"7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd"}],"sha":"947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/947bf76e8be689d85eff4b4c3a4bb0b23bbc4aee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:37:47Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:37:47Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"chore: remove dead debug/fallback files ahead of submission\n\nDeletes six files confirmed unused by the live deploy path:\n- Dockerfile.railway — debug variant from early dependency troubleshooting;\n  railway.json has no dockerfilePath override, so Railway builds the root\n  Dockerfile, never this one.\n- scripts/test_import.py — standalone smoke test, not imported by any\n  module, not wired into any build/CI step.\n- api/server_minimal.py, api/entrypoint.py, Procfile — a fallback chain\n  (Procfile -> entrypoint.py -> server_minimal.py on import failure) that\n  the actual deploy never uses: railway.json''s startCommand runs\n  \"python -m api.server\" directly.\n- CONTAINERIZATION_README.md — described an earlier self-managed MI300X\n  Droplet + Groq-for-dev plan that was superseded by the current\n  Fireworks-based setup; left in place it would mislead a reviewer.\n\nAlso trims README.md''s file tree to match — removes the four deleted\nfiles it listed by name.\n\nVerified: `python -m api.server` starts clean (Firestore connects,\n/health returns 200) and all core modules (agents, orchestrator,\napi.server, config.settings, data.firestore_client, data.forecast,\nmain) import without error after the deletions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e4407bb05f877c0d6df02693ac04c6d168740ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/0e4407bb05f877c0d6df02693ac04c6d168740ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKDc0NjdiMjM2NTk0NjRjNzk2ZmZiNjhkY2Q4ZjU5YTY0NjMyMjU3Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639","sha":"ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639"}],"sha":"7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/7467b23659464c796ffb68dcd8f59a64632257cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T14:02:38Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T14:02:38Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: move agent-activity panel to a vertical sidebar with persistent tracks\n\nReworks the agent-activity panel''s geometry from a horizontal row above\nthe chat to a fixed-width (92px) vertical sidebar to the right of\nchat-card. #view-chat.active is now a row (chat-card + agent-sidebar)\ninstead of a single column; the height fix from earlier sessions\n(calc(100vh - 80px - 18px)) didn''t need to change since it''s a vertical\nconcern, unaffected by adding a second column.\n\nNew: each agent now has a persistent dotted track — a static line from\nits fixed position to the user mascot''s, tinted with the agent''s own\ncolor, visible before any animation as a \"map\" of who reports where.\nWalking now moves along that same line (2D translate, not just\nhorizontal) using the same per-keyframe-eased, double-bounce animation\nbuilt earlier — only the geometry changed, not the animation''s feel.\n\nTwo problems found and fixed while building this:\n- All 7 agents sit in one vertical column directly above the user, so\n  every track''s start/end X coincided — 7 lines rendered as one\n  overlapping strand. Fixed by fanning each agent''s anchor point out\n  horizontally by a small per-index offset (~±24px total), used for\n  both the drawn track and the walk destination, so what''s drawn is\n  exactly what''s walked.\n- Track positions are computed from live getBoundingClientRect() calls,\n  which return all-zero while the chat view is display:none — true at\n  page load (still on the landing page). _renderAgentPanel() ran once\n  at load and baked in zero-coordinate tracks that never updated.\n  Fixed by recomputing in showView() whenever the chat tab specifically\n  becomes visible, not just once at load.\n\nVerified in a real browser: no viewport overflow at 1440, 1366, 1280,\nor 1200px widths (chat-card narrows proportionally but stays roomy,\ndown to 810px at the narrowest); a 4-agent and a full 7-agent\nsimultaneous activation both show a clean cascading stagger down the\ncolumn with no visual collision (precise DOM position tracking showed\nminimum ~85px vertical separation against ~55px tile height); all\ntiles settle back to transform:none with active/walking classes fully\ncleared afterward; general-question routing regression-checked with no\nconsole errors in any run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5e65faf4a8ffd38d9f70a7f8474bef028b71e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/b5e65faf4a8ffd38d9f70a7f8474bef028b71e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGRkZDQ4Njg5NTc2MjkwYjUzNzlkZDVmYjA4NDQxOTIwODVmN2Q2Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d","sha":"d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d"}],"sha":"ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/ddd48689576290b5379dd5fb0844192085f7d639"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:53:13Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:53:13Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: agent characters walk to a user mascot and back when active\n\nAdds an 8th character, USER_MASCOT (\"Anda\") — same body+head cube\ntemplate as the 7 agents but a neutral warm palette, a gold visor\ninstead of cyan, and a storefront icon accessory, so it reads as the\nwarung owner rather than an 8th data agent. Always idle/stationary:\nits id never matches an entry in agents_invoked, so it never animates.\n\nWhen an agent activates, its character now walks toward the mascot,\ndoes a small double-bounce \"reporting\" nod, then walks back home —\nlayered on top of the existing active-state cues (floor glow, tile\nglow-ring, visor brighten, bold label), which keep their own 2.5s\nduration independent of the ~1.8s walk.\n\nTwo things this needed to not look chaotic with several agents active\nat once:\n- Each agent travels toward ~70% of its own distance to the mascot\n  rather than a shared endpoint, so agents starting far from the\n  mascot naturally stop further away than ones already close by,\n  instead of stacking on the same spot.\n- Walk starts are staggered ~130ms apart per agent (by position in\n  agents_invoked) so simultaneous activations don''t move in lockstep.\nVerified via precise DOM position tracking across a 4-agent activation\n(eyes/bookkeeper/strategy/reasoning) — minimum gap between any two\nwalking characters was 114px against a 44px tile width, at every\nsampled frame through the full animation.\n\nEasing is set per keyframe stop rather than one curve for the whole\n1.8s — brisk ease-out leaving home, a snappy back-and-forth for the\ntwo report bounces, calmer ease settling back in — plus a small\nsquash/stretch at mid-walk for a touch of life. One global easing\ncurve made the bounce segment feel mushy instead of like a nod.\n\nVerified end-to-end in a real browser: frame-by-frame capture of a\nsingle-agent walk (voice_agent via \"halo\") confirms the full\nwalk-out -> report -> walk-back cycle; multi-agent activation (3 and\n4 agents, including a direct 4-agent stress call) shows no visual\ncollision; regression check confirms data_entry_agent''s clarify-then-\nconfirm flow and general-question routing both still work correctly\nthrough the new panel, no console errors in any scenario.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e0909826a4da33cd8649268d9dc7e3507d5619c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/1e0909826a4da33cd8649268d9dc7e3507d5619c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGQ3NjBiNjExMWFiNDBjZmNjMWM0ZGYxOWVjNmU4ZWM4ZjAwMWI3N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff","sha":"9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff"}],"sha":"d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d760b6111ab40cfcc1c4df19ec6e8ec8f001b77d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:23:40Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:23:40Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: isometric character panel replacing the plain agent-activity chips\n\nReplaces the 7 text chips above Chat Kira with small blocky isometric\nSVG robots — one per agent, sharing one construction (body+head cubes,\ncyan gradient \"visor\" screen, floor tile) with only body color and one\nsmall role-accessory differing per agent (camera for Mata, coin stack\nfor Juru Hitung, crate for Penjaga Stok, bar-chart for Strategi,\nclipboard for Catat Data, chip for Reasoning, equalizer bars for Suara).\n\nIdle: character rests on its floor tile, no glow. Active: it levitates\n~11px AND the tile glows — two simultaneous signals rather than one,\nper the approved design checkpoint. All 7 characters are generated at\nruntime from a single template function (AGENT_CHARACTERS config +\n_isoCharTile()) rather than hand-duplicated per-agent, since the only\nvariation is a 4-color shade array and an accessory SVG fragment —\nkeeps the 7 in sync and avoids copy-paste drift.\n\nColors are Tailwind 200/300/400/500 per hue (teal/green/blue/purple/\namber/pink/red), spread across the hue wheel for at-a-glance\ndistinction when several agents highlight at once.\n\nReuses the existing agents_invoked -> _flashAgents() wiring unchanged —\nonly the DOM structure under #agentPanel changed (data-agent + .active\nstill drive the highlight), so no orchestrator/backend changes needed.\n\nVerified in a real browser: all 7 render with correct ids/colors, no\nconsole errors, single-agent and multi-agent activation both light up\nexactly the right characters (confirmed via DOM query + high-res\nclose-up screenshot showing levitate+glow), no layout overflow at\n1440x1000 or 1366x768 (chat input row stays fully visible, 0px scroll\noverflow at both sizes), and the data_entry_agent stock-update flow\nstill works correctly through the new panel with no premature writes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23b8206d5505e4fcc2db3e968043365bf855eaed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/23b8206d5505e4fcc2db3e968043365bf855eaed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKDljZjcxNjBhMDNlY2E5ZTA2NzgwMGZmMTY5M2E3MDE0ZjAzZDQzZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a","sha":"844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a"}],"sha":"9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/9cf7160a03eca9e067800ff1693a7014f03d43ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:28:36Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:28:36Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: live agent activity panel on Chat Kira\n\nAdds a row of 7 chips (one per agent, using the persona names already\nestablished on the landing page) above the chat message area. When a\nchat response comes back, whichever agents the orchestrator actually\ninvoked (agents_invoked, already returned by /chat but previously\nunused by the frontend) light up together for 2.5s, then fade — no\nsequencing, no animation library, just a CSS transition and a\nsetTimeout, per the demo-video requirement to keep this simple and\nreliable.\n\nPanel sits inside .chat-card as a flex-shrink:0 row alongside the\nexisting chat-body/chat-input-row, so it doesn''t reintroduce the\ninput-row viewport overflow fixed earlier — chat-body''s flex:1 just\nshrinks to make room.\n\nVerified end-to-end in a real browser: single-agent and multi-agent\n(3 agents) messages both highlight the correct chips simultaneously,\nand the highlight auto-clears after the timeout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5d316bd96db2a8ff4e2067b3780f6b0ae35c6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/d5d316bd96db2a8ff4e2067b3780f6b0ae35c6d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKDg0NGU5OWE0MzlmMjI4Y2U2YzkwOTIwYjBmYjhhOTQ2MjUwMTVjOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80","sha":"d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80"}],"sha":"844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/844e99a439f228ce6c90920b0fb8a94625015c8a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:08:51Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:08:51Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: add chat-based expense entry, completing the data-entry feature set\n\nOwners can now log ad-hoc operational expenses by chat (\"catat pengeluaran\nbeli bensin 20rb\", \"tadi keluar 50rb buat plastik\") the same way stock\nupdates and sales already work. New record_expense() in firestore_client.py\ndecrements cash_balance and logs an itemized entry to a new expense_history\nfield (mirrors sales_history''s per-day structure, but keeps a description\nper item since — unlike sales — there''s no separate products array to\nrecover \"what was this for\" from later).\n\nDeliberately does NOT feed into daily_operating_expenses or bookkeeper_agent''s\nnet_profit calculation, to avoid double-counting the fixed daily overhead\nestimate against ad-hoc entries. Expenses affect cash_balance (and so cash\nrunway forecasts) immediately; P&L reporting is unchanged and still assumes\nthe fixed daily estimate.\n\ndata_entry_agent gains a third tool, record_expense, using the same\nconfirm-before-write pattern as record_sale (it''s money-moving). The\ntrickier part: \"beli X\" is ambiguous between buying operational supplies\n(record_expense) and restocking inventory for resale (not something any\ntool here handles — doing so would misrepresent a cash-for-inventory swap\nas a pure cost). The system prompt now explicitly tells the model to\nrecognize resale signals (\"buat dijual\", or the item matching an existing\ninventory item) and redirect to the stock-update flow instead of silently\nmis-categorizing it as an expense.\n\nVerified end-to-end against live Firestore (user_001, full snapshot/restore\naround every write): complete expense, missing-info follow-up, declined\nconfirmation, the specific buy-for-supplies vs buy-for-resale ambiguity\nscenarios, and regression checks confirming general questions and the\nexisting stock/sales flows still route correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e9706f6b223f20def3c6fbd9674991037ffaf5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/7e9706f6b223f20def3c6fbd9674991037ffaf5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGQ1OGM2ZjgxZTM5NTc0ZTU0YWI0N2Y3ZDFhODJhYmQ0NTc5MTBiODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772","sha":"dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772"}],"sha":"d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/d58c6f81e39574e54ab47f7d1a82abd457910b80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T10:28:30Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T10:28:30Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"fix: sticky routing for data-entry follow-ups, chat input CSS overflow, add chat-based sales entry\n\nFixes:\n- Router classified each chat message in isolation, so bare follow-ups\n  (\"iya\" confirming a fuzzy product/item match) had no context and got\n  misrouted to voice_agent, silently abandoning the pending data_entry_agent\n  conversation. _node_route now checks has_pending(user_id) before running\n  intent classification and routes straight back when a slot-filling or\n  confirmation flow is in progress.\n- Chat input row was clipped below the viewport: the CSS assumed a 64px\n  header, but the real rendered height is 80px, and .view-content''s 18px\n  top padding was never accounted for either (only padding-bottom was\n  zeroed by .no-scroll). Corrected the height calc and matched\n  .chat-input-row''s horizontal padding to .chat-body''s.\n\nFeature:\n- data_entry_agent gains a second tool, record_sale, so owners can log a\n  sale by chat (\"catat penjualan gorengan 3 porsi harga 4500\") the same\n  way stock updates already work: tool-calling extracts product/quantity/\n  price, asks a follow-up when something''s missing, and rejects products\n  that don''t match real records instead of inventing new ones.\n- Unlike update_stock, record_sale always confirms before writing — it''s\n  a money-moving action. The confirmation text and the yes/no read-back\n  are plain Python, not LLM output, so the write can''t be talked around by\n  a confused model. Declining cancels cleanly with no write.\n\nTested end-to-end against live Firestore (user_001) with full\nsnapshot/restore around every write — complete info, missing info\nrequiring follow-up, fuzzy product-name matching, unknown product\nrejection, and confirmation decline all verified, plus regression checks\nthat general questions and stock updates still route correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6d1249a58053ce2e307b4933cb7a095262fdbfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/b6d1249a58053ce2e307b4933cb7a095262fdbfb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGRjMzRmNTJhZjcyMDM4NWUzNDgxNzQ4Y2MwY2FmNzMwMDA4ZmU3NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3","sha":"bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3"}],"sha":"dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/dc34f52af720385e3481748cc0caf730008fe772"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:13:40Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:13:40Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"feat: add chat-based stock updates via LLM tool calling\n\nOwners can now update inventory stock through Chat Kira (\"update stok gula\njadi 8kg\") instead of only the manual Catat Data form. New data_entry_agent\nuses tool calling (confirmed supported on Fireworks'' gpt-oss-120b) to\nextract item_name/new_stock_quantity from natural language, asking a\nfollow-up question when a slot is missing instead of guessing, and\nrejecting items that don''t match existing inventory rather than silently\ncreating new ones. Session state is in-process per user_id, no persistence\nneeded for this slice.\n\nAlso hardens routing failure handling: previously a broken/failing router\ncall silently fell back to voice_agent with empty context, which — now\nthat voice_agent calls a real LLM — could fabricate confident \"done!\"\nresponses with no data behind them. Routing failures now short-circuit to\na fixed, non-LLM honest error message instead.\n\nScope: stock updates only. Sales/expense entry via chat are separate,\nnot-yet-built slices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a53eb8ac5e1050ecb198ffcf446dcea2446c3d57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/a53eb8ac5e1050ecb198ffcf446dcea2446c3d57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3","node_id":"C_kwDOTKRZJdoAKGJiYzUwNmUwM2ZiNDMyZDk3MmQzYWQ5N2FkMDI2OGE1MWM5MzJkZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commit/5778523c490d521765fde263695c75ee599e4baf","sha":"5778523c490d521765fde263695c75ee599e4baf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/5778523c490d521765fde263695c75ee599e4baf"}],"sha":"bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/bbc506e03fb432d972d3ad97ad0268a51c932df3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/commits/5778523c490d521765fde263695c75ee599e4baf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T04:45:33Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T04:45:33Z","email":"habibrmdni0@gmail.com","name":"Hz"},"message":"fix: propagate language param to backend-generated forecast/alert text\n\nLanguage toggle previously only swapped static UI labels; forecast\nsummaries and proactive alert narratives kept whatever language the\nbusiness record was stored in. /forecast and /proactive now accept\n?lang=id|en and thread it through forecast_business() and\nrun_proactive_check(), and the frontend re-fetches on toggle instead\nof re-rendering stale cached text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a207c11641cbf26100c17d1ba16c7431644f1a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/trees/0a207c11641cbf26100c17d1ba16c7431644f1a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/habibrmdni0-hue/Kira/git/commits/5778523c490d521765fde263695c75ee599e4baf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254685572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-hue","id":254685572,"login":"habibrmdni0-hue","node_id":"U_kgDODy4xhA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/habibrmdni0-hue","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/habibrmdni0-