om/users/vinaysomawat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/commits/3c3a1b60c1667fa96c68ab728e898ce94ad1588e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T20:11:17Z","email":"vinaysomawat40@gmail.com","name":"vinaysomawat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T20:11:17Z","email":"vinaysomawat40@gmail.com","name":"vinaysomawat"},"message":"Fix Evening Reflection disappearing at midnight\n\nThe visibility gate only checked hour < 18, which silently hid the\nsection again past midnight even mid-late-night-session. Extended to\nhour >= 18 || hour < 5, and made the server reflect on yesterday (not\nthe just-started, nearly-empty new calendar day) when viewed in that\npost-midnight window -- gatherTodayActivityLines() now takes an\nexplicit daysAgo param (default 0, unchanged for the daily-journal\ncron), and generateEveningReflection()/getEveningReflection() thread\nan isLateNight flag down from the client''s own local-hour check.\nTomorrow''s top priority still anchors to the real current date\nregardless of which day''s activity is being reflected on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c793c5ea3f0b87fbd802a8bf8e1feee803a190f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/git/trees/c793c5ea3f0b87fbd802a8bf8e1feee803a190f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/git/commits/3c3a1b60c1667fa96c68ab728e898ce94ad1588e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30196269?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat/followers","followi