"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vinaysomawat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/commits/a4d838e75d3332683431c1b5d3ca58f58f9f415c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T12:46:07Z","email":"vinaysomawat40@gmail.com","name":"vinaysomawat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T12:46:07Z","email":"vinaysomawat40@gmail.com","name":"vinaysomawat"},"message":"Wire JD missingSkills into the Topic Quiz''s weak-area seeding\n\nBacklog item 1: analyzeJobDescription''s missingSkills sat on each\napplication card as a static badge with no further use. Now:\n\n- analyzeJobDescription''s priorityTopics is constrained to the same\n  fixed QUIZ_TOPICS list the Topic Quiz uses, instead of open free text\n  -- makes it reliably matchable without a second AI call or fuzzy\n  matching (stays rule-engine-first).\n- handleGenerateQuiz merges missingSkills from any active (non-rejected)\n  application whose jd_analysis.priorityTopics includes the topic being\n  quizzed into the same weakAreas hint array past quiz misses already\n  feed generateTopicQuiz -- so prepping a topic a real JD cares about is\n  biased toward what that JD says you''re actually missing.\n\nVerified live: generated a real React quiz end-to-end against actual\napplication data, no console errors, no stray quiz_attempts row left\nbehind (closed without submitting).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c3c09844dbbe942452d398f4cc8b80ca8da2ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/git/trees/4c3c09844dbbe942452d398f4cc8b80ca8da2ee9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vinaysomawat/personal-ai-os/git/commits/a4d838e75d3332683431c1b5d3ca58f58f9f415c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":