ml_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/dd3341a0f872305ce5f48731987ce7973db0885d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:06:24Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:06:24Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"feat(design-system): add Icon component (Angular + React)\n\nThin lucide-angular / lucide-react wrapper per spec §0.2, locked to the\n14/16/18 size scale from §0.4. Each Lucide icon ships as its own standalone\ncomponent rather than a name-keyed lookup, so `icon` takes the component\nreference directly on both sides; Angular mounts it via NgComponentOutlet''s\n`inputs` binding (17+) since lucide-angular''s icons are attribute-selector\ncomponents (`svg[lucideSparkles]`), not a dynamic-by-name API. Decorative\nby default (aria-hidden), labelled via the DS''s own `label` prop when an\nicon is meaningful rather than relying on each library''s implicit default.\n\nInstalls @lucide/angular — lucide-angular (the name in the spec''s Icon row)\nis deprecated in favor of this package; same v1.23.0 line as the\nlucide-react already used elsewhere in this repo (packages/remote-admin).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"90c2d4da650e5a23ef8a9bd8c5b036856ee40f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/90c2d4da650e5a23ef8a9bd8c5b036856ee40f0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/dd3341a0f872305ce5f48731987ce7973db0885d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/dd3341a0f872305ce5f48731987ce7973db0885d","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGRkMzM0MWEwZjg3MjMwNWNlNWY0ODczMTk4N2NlNzk3M2RiMDg4NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053","sha":"e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053"}],"sha":"dd3341a0f872305ce5f48731987ce7973db0885d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/dd3341a0f872305ce5f48731987ce7973db0885d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:05:51Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:05:51Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"feat(design-system): add Card component (Angular + React)\n\nSurface wrapper per spec §0.2: --surface bg, 1px --border, radius 6px\n(--radius-panel), --space-4 pad — border, not shadow. Deliberately no\nheader/footer subcomponents: a metric is a Card composing a label + a big\nmono number, not a dedicated MetricTile (§0.2, locked).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe1dc66575f6b2e05b193769bb289de76a4a0ac6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/fe1dc66575f6b2e05b193769bb289de76a4a0ac6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGU0ZjhiMmMxOTYyNjQxZDk5OGNmMjIzYWJkODA3NTk2NWQwZTcwNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522","sha":"d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522"}],"sha":"e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/e4f8b2c1962641d998cf223abd8075965d0e7053"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:05:21Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T07:05:21Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"fix(design-system): Skeleton honors prefers-reduced-motion\n\nBoth twins always animated a moving shimmer, ignoring the a11y floor''s\nreduced-motion requirement (atlas-ui-implementation-spec.md §0.2/session\nbrief). Under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, swap the sliding gradient for\na static background with a pure-opacity pulse (no positional movement).\n\nAlso wires up zoneless TestBed rendering (test-setup.ts +\nsetupFilesAfterEnv) so this package can finally unit-test Angular\ncomponents via TestBed — needed for the Skeleton spec and every DS\ncomponent test going forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0d3a1040f08ecc8bd64bbeb6c9bb3e8ac5334a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/f0d3a1040f08ecc8bd64bbeb6c9bb3e8ac5334a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGQ2Mzg5OWUzZjE1MzYwMWE1NjZjMGMwYmM1MGM1ODQxY2IxYWM1MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159","sha":"b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159"}],"sha":"d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/d63899e3f153601a566c0c0bc50c5841cb1ac522"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:37:20Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:37:20Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"feat(ci): compatibility gate for federated shared-dependency versions (ADR-0004 §3)\n\nNative Federation''s strictVersion has never been evaluated at runtime\n(ADR-0004) - this is what actually replaces it: a script, run in CI right\nafter every federated project builds, that reads each remote''s emitted\nremoteEntry.json and enforces a per-dependency policy rather than one global\nrule.\n\n- @angular/* (including its /primitives/* sub-paths): exact resolved-version\n  match required. DEMONSTRATED - this is precisely the pair (21.2.17 vs\n  21.2.18, both satisfying the declared ~21.2.0 range) that produced NG0203\n  in ADR-0004''s drift experiment.\n- rxjs: also exact-match, but PRECAUTIONARY only - ADR-0004 Decision §3 never\n  reproduced a multi-copy rxjs failure, so the code and this message say so\n  rather than overclaiming.\n- Everything else singleton-shared: semver range satisfaction against the\n  declared requiredVersion - the check strictVersion was assumed to already\n  be doing.\n- zone.js has no rule at all: this app is zoneless (confirmed in ADR-0004),\n  so it never appears in a shared list. A rule for a package not in the\n  graph would guard nothing.\n\nVerified by execution against the real builds, not just read: a clean run\nagainst shell + remote-monitoring''s actual dist/ output passes. Then, to\nprove the gate actually catches something, remote-monitoring''s built\nremoteEntry.json was hand-edited to resolve @angular/core to 21.2.18 against\nshell''s 21.2.17 - the literal ADR-0004 NG0203 scenario - and the gate failed\nwith both versions and remote names named. Reverted after confirming.\n\nOne real edge case found along the way: Native Federation auto-shares\nworkspace-local packages like @atlas/design-system with empty version/\nrequiredVersion (no real semver identity - one monorepo install, no possible\ndrift). The gate skips those rather than misreading \"no declared range\" as a\nrange violation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cd117bfee00bcd49d49a4cc79a2ccbf4eceede8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/2cd117bfee00bcd49d49a4cc79a2ccbf4eceede8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGIxODAzMzA1M2M2ODYxNWFhYzdhMzc5NWJmYjkzMjljMmZiYzMxNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75","sha":"8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75"}],"sha":"b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/b18033053c68615aac7a3795bfb9329c2fbc3159"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:30:13Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:30:13Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"fix(module-registry): live three-origin verification — TAMPER/ALLOW-LIST hold, but the shell never booted first\n\nADR-0006 shipped with real SRI hashes computed from real builds, but the\nregistry had never actually run in a browser — only asserted against by unit\ntests. Stood up three genuine CORS-enabled static origins from production\nbuilds (shell:5500, remote-monitoring/federation:4201, remote-admin/esm:4202,\nper .claude/launch.json''s *-prod-static configs) and verified by execution,\nper ADR-0004''s own method.\n\nFinding zero, blocking everything else: the shell never booted. module-registry.ts\ndefined both the pre-bootstrap loadModuleRegistry() fetch (which main.ts must\nstatically import before initFederation() installs the import map) and the\nMODULE_REGISTRY InjectionToken (which pulls in @angular/core) in the same\nfile. esbuild bundled both into one chunk, so resolving the bare specifier\n\"@angular/core\" failed at ESM link time before any import map existed — a\nsilent failure that never even reached main()''s own .catch(), reproduced live\nvia manual importShim() against the running page. Fixed by splitting the\ntoken into module-registry-token.ts, the only file in this feature allowed to\nimport @angular/core; confirmed at the bundle level that main.ts''s static\nimport graph is now Angular-free.\n\nWith that fixed, both planned live tests passed:\n- TAMPER: one byte flipped in the served remote-entry.js after its hash was\n  already committed. fetch(url, { integrity }) rejected with \"Failed to\n  fetch\" (the browser''s native SRI enforcement) before import() ever ran —\n  tampered bytes never executed. RemoteMountHost caught it and rendered the\n  A.3 fallback, focus included (this session''s earlier commit).\n- ALLOW-LIST: remote-admin''s entryUrl repointed at an unserved port. Zero\n  network requests to that origin were ever made — filtered at registry-load\n  time, before routing. remote-monitoring kept mounting normally in the same\n  session, confirming per-entry filtering isolates one bad entry.\n\nDocumented asymmetry re-checked against live behavior, not just re-read: SRI\nonly has a hook on the esm path (confirmed by what there was to tamper), the\nfederation path has none, and the origin allow-list is the real protection\nthere, exactly as ADR-0006 already claimed. Full account in the ADR-0006\namendment. All tamper edits were to gitignored dist/ output and were restored\nimmediately after each test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23ee49cf6f5671bf4d4f8fb7add58ff85f63da55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/23ee49cf6f5671bf4d4f8fb7add58ff85f63da55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKDhiOTc5MWM2MTIyN2I1NWNlZGVmZDUzMWI1NjNiM2U0ZTIwYjZlNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca","sha":"f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca"}],"sha":"8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/8b9791c61227b55cedefd531b563b3e4e20b6e75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:10:25Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T05:10:25Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"fix(remote-mount-host): move focus to the A.3 fallback on ESM mount-time throw\n\nRemoteMountHost set the error signal and announced to the live region on a\nmount-time failure but never moved focus, leaving a keyboard/screen-reader\nuser stranded on a dead control behind the rendered fallback. Mirrors\nAngularRemoteBoundary''s afterNextRender-based focusFallbackOnNextRender,\nwhich already handles this correctly for the Angular federation path — same\nzoneless-signal-write timing applies to both boundaries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b41da7c444c57fb5c4a027f74fdd2b675ae70a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/b41da7c444c57fb5c4a027f74fdd2b675ae70a38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGYwMDVjYTRmMWU4ZTQ1ZTdmZTQ5ZGMwZTEyYzZlZWE4OTg2NDAwY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26","sha":"a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26"}],"sha":"f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/f005ca4f1e8e45e7fe49dc0e12c6eea8986400ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:46:33Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:46:33Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"feat(a3): runtime-fetched module registry with origin allow-list and SRI\n\nADR-0004 Decision §5, sequenced last per this session''s plan: replaces both\npublic/federation.manifest.json (runtime-fetched but unvalidated, and its\nlocalhost URLs never get environment-injected even in a \"production\"\nbuild) and app.routes.ts''s hardcoded REMOTE_ADMIN_ENTRY_URL (genuinely\nbaked into the JS bundle) with one schema - { name, type, entryUrl,\nversion, integrity } - fetched from public/module-registry.json before\nNative Federation initializes and before any Angular code is imported.\n\nThe security decision this ADR treats as the point, not boilerplate:\n- Origin allow-list, checked before any network request for an entry''s\n  bytes - the one guarantee in this file with no caveats.\n- SRI is fully enforced for the esm remote (fetch(url, { integrity })\n  before import(), per the Fetch spec''s own rejection behavior) - and\n  honestly weaker for the federation remote, because initFederation()\n  does its own internal unmodified fetches with no integrity hook\n  (verified by reading InitFederationOptions'' actual type, not assumed).\n  This asymmetry is real and documented in ADR-0006, not glossed over.\n- A blob-URL \"verify then execute the exact verified bytes\" design was\n  tried and rejected empirically: remote-admin''s built remote-entry.js has\n  a relative import to a shared chunk that only resolves against its real\n  http(s) origin, so importing from a blob: URL breaks it. What ships is a\n  validate-then-trust check instead, with the gap named plainly in\n  load-remote-esm.ts and ADR-0006.\n\nA malformed or disallowed entry drops just that entry (logged, not\nthrown); the registry fetch itself failing returns an empty array so the\nshell still boots with no remotes rather than not booting at all.\n\nRemoteMountHost''s entryUrl input became remoteName - a registry lookup\nkey, resolved at mount time - so a missing/filtered registry entry fails\nthrough the same A.3 catch as any other mount failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9735a8837a6cb4b79aefb1c21d5c295da25eb759","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/9735a8837a6cb4b79aefb1c21d5c295da25eb759"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKGE2YThiMjc4ZDZkYjIyODZkNmE3NjZlMjFiZDQ3NGQyMzY0ZWFjMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2","sha":"9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2"}],"sha":"a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/a6a8b278d6db2286d6a766e21bd474d2364eac26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:29:26Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:29:26Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"test(remote-mount-host): adversarially verify THE RACE test, not just design it\n\nLast session''s race test passed on the first try - designed defensively,\nnever proven to actually break on a bad implementation. Verified rather\nthan trusted: temporarily replaced the destroyed/stale-token guard in\nremote-mount-host.ts with `if (false && ...)` and reran the suite. Exactly\none test failed (0 unmount() calls instead of 1) - THE RACE test itself -\nevery other test still passed.\n\nThis confirms both things the test''s construction implies but doesn''t\nprove on its own: resolveMount() genuinely isn''t called until after\nfixture.destroy() (the mock never resolves synchronously, so the race\nwindow is real, not closed before it opens), and the guard the test\nexercises is the one actually preventing the leak. No source change - the\nguard was correct and the test was already legitimate. Recorded the\nverification methodology in the test''s own comment so this doesn''t need\nre-litigating.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c1b9da8d1ae6036138e0f3567b09337c1099eaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/9c1b9da8d1ae6036138e0f3567b09337c1099eaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKDk1NDRjNjJlODg3MWEwNTYwNTg5ZGM3YzVjYmUxNTA2NWEwOTQ4ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3","sha":"6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3"}],"sha":"9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/9544c62e8871a0560589dc7c5cbe15065a0948d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/commits/6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:26:07Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:26:07Z","email":"adithibalaji03@gmail.com","name":"Adithi Balaji"},"message":"feat(a3): close the NG0203 loop for remote-monitoring''s Angular federation\n\nAppendix A.3''s Angular half, deferred at the end of commit b711f8d (\"no\nAngular remote is being wired this session\"). remote-monitoring now mounts\nthrough AngularRemoteBoundary instead of the router''s loadComponent\nresolving straight to the remote''s component: a route-scoped\nRemoteRouteErrorHandler swaps in the same RemoteErrorFallback the ESM path\nuses, with the same focus-moves-to-fallback and announce() contract.\n\nThe first design didn''t survive contact with a real reproduction. Route-\nlevel `providers` should scope ErrorHandler to just this route (this is\nAngular''s own documented DI model) - but a RouterTestingHarness test that\nforced a mount-time throw showed it propagating raw past every handler,\nnever reaching the route-scoped one. Reading ChangeDetectionSchedulerImpl\nand INTERNAL_APPLICATION_ERROR_HANDLER in @angular/core explains why: the\nscheduler that drives a real mount-time throw to ErrorHandler is an\napp-wide singleton whose captured injector is permanently root, regardless\nof what any route provides - the same \"schema, not runtime guarantee\"\nshape ADR-0004 already found in strictVersion. AngularRemoteBoundary now\ncreates the remote''s component itself and calls handleError directly on\ncatch; the ErrorHandler token registration is kept because it still\ncorrectly protects a POST-mount throw from inside the remote''s own tree\n(Angular resolves that case per-view, not via the scheduler). Full\nmechanism and the amendment to ADR-0004 explain the two paths.\n\nVerified with a synthetic mount-time throw (a real NG0203 needs the\noriginal worktree version-drift setup, out of reach for a unit test) via\nRouterTestingHarness first, then AngularRemoteBoundary''s own spec once the\nharness proved the route-scoped-provider design didn''t work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96635bea4f04fc967b374546addff5427c333b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/trees/96635bea4f04fc967b374546addff5427c333b90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adithiB/atlas/git/commits/6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83456549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB","id":83456549,"login":"adithiB","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDU2NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adithiB","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adithiB/atlas/commit/6c3f8dad95c837cb28acdbf5b87152a7695e95a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTKuufNoAKDZjM2Y4ZGFkOTVjODM3Y2