ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gbonin-ciandt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gbonin-ciandt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ms-ciandt/trilha-react-native/commits/729ad13813047c8df0663a8cccd1bebe8b203e6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:10:01Z","email":"gbonin@ciandt.com","name":"Gabriel Matallo Bonin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:17:03Z","email":"gbonin@ciandt.com","name":"Gabriel Matallo Bonin"},"message":"feat(infra): migrate video hosting from static/ to GitHub Releases\n\nProblem: static/assets/videos/ has grown to 5.1 GB / 101 MP4 files,\nexceeding the GitHub Pages artifact limit of 1 GB.\n\nSolution: host videos on GitHub Releases (v0-videos tag).\n\nChanges:\n- deploy.yml: strip *.mp4/webm/mov from build before artifact upload\n- upload-videos-to-release.yml: manual workflow to upload all 101 videos\n  to a GitHub Release in one shot (trigger via Actions → workflow_dispatch)\n- scripts/migrate-video-urls.mjs: updates all <source src> in docs from\n  static paths to GitHub Release URLs (run after creating the release)\n- .gitignore: block future accidental commits of video files\n\nMigration steps (run after merging this PR):\n  1. Actions → Upload Videos to GitHub Release → Run workflow (tag: v0-videos)\n  2. Verify all 101 assets appear in the release\n  3. node scripts/migrate-video-urls.mjs --dry-run   # preview\n  4. node scripts/migrate-video-urls.mjs             # apply\n  5. git rm -r static/assets/videos/\n  6. Commit + push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b21d18e62b9f351f4e06a24cd62d32b9aeefd5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ms-ciandt/trilha-react-native/git/trees/b21d18e62b9f351f4e06a24cd62d32b9aeefd5fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ms-ciandt/trilha-react-native/git/commits/729ad13813047c8df0663a8cccd1bebe8b203e6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":