om/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel","id":35613825,"login":"vercel[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MzU2MTM4MjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jrrembert/rembert.dev/commits/878fbc7e0dbb2033e225499896bc6ce10e7f3e42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T22:11:20Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T22:11:51Z","email":"jrrembert@users.noreply.github.com","name":"J. Ryan Rembert"},"message":"Install Vercel Web Analytics\n\n## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation\n\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the rembert.dev Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. Installed @vercel/analytics package:**\n   - Added `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1` to project dependencies\n   - Used npm (since bun was not available in the environment)\n   - Created `package-lock.json` for dependency management\n\n**2. Modified app/layout.tsx:**\n   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from \"@vercel/analytics/next\";`\n   - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout inside the `<body>` tag\n   - Placed the component after the `{children}` to track all page views\n   - Followed Next.js App Router best practices as specified in the Vercel documentation\n\n**3. Files Modified:**\n   - `/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component\n   - `/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency\n\n**4. Files Created:**\n   - `/package-lock.json` - NPM lock file for consistent dependency resolution\n\n### Implementation Details:\n\nThe Analytics component was integrated following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects. The component is placed in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) within the `<body>` tag, which ensures that analytics tracking is active across all pages of the application.\n\n### Verification:\n\n- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`\n- ✅ TypeScript type checking passed with `npm run typecheck`\n- ✅ No linting errors introduced\n- ✅ Lock file generated for dependency consistency\n\n### Next Steps:\n\nTo complete the setup, ensure that Web Analytics is enabled in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section for this project. Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically start collecting data.\n\n### Notes:\n\nThe implementation is minimal and non-invasive, preserving all existing code structure and functionality. The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals without requiring additional configuration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2423b9ede3aee826166ce24636b181d0c57d584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jrrembert/rembert.dev/git/trees/b2423b9ede3aee826166ce24636b181d0c57d584"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jrrembert/rembert.dev/git/commits/878fbc7e0dbb2033e225499896bc6ce10e7f3e42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2006091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrrembert/events{/privacy}","followers_u